<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix" lang="en">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Materials and Methods</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Further Details on AlphaProof Nexus Agents</h3>

<figure id="A1.F4" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2605.22763v2/x4.png" id="A1.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" width="614" height="399" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span><span id="A1.F4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pseudocode for the basic agent (A).</span> A prover subagent executes a sequence of steps in a loop. Each step is a conversation with a LLM instance (Gemini 3.1 Pro). During this conversation, the subagent can view a Lean file and apply search-replace edits. After each change, the Lean compiler provides feedback, such as compilation errors. As for agent (D), we check for the integrity of the final sketch once the conversation is over. <math id="A1.F4.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> subagents run independently in parallel and stop as soon as one of them found a valid proof.</figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Basic Agent.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The pseudocode for the basic agent (A) is shown in Figure <a href="#A1.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ A.1 Further Details on AlphaProof Nexus Agents ‣ Appendix A Materials and Methods ‣ Advancing Mathematics Research with AI-Driven Formal Proof Search" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. The agent operates <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> independent subagents that share no state. All subagents start with the same initial proof sketch. As soon as one subagent finds a proof, all others are terminated.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Each subagent implements a Ralph loop <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">huntley2025ralph</span>]</cite> consisting of a sequence of episodes. The full prompt is shown in Figure <a href="#A1.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ A.2 Prompts ‣ Appendix A Materials and Methods ‣ Advancing Mathematics Research with AI-Driven Formal Proof Search" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>. Within each episode, the subagent runs a multi-turn session with an access to a <span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">search_replace</span> tool. After each edit, the Lean code is compiled and compiler feedback is passed back to the model. When the subagent ends an episode, the code is validated using SafeVerify <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">SafeVerify2025</span>]</cite>, which checks the proof against the theorem specification and guards against environment exploits (e.g., axiom injection). If validation succeeds and the proof is <span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sorry</span>-free, the proof is returned. If <span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sorry</span> remains, the subagent summarizes lessons learned in a comment and begins the next episode from the current sketch. If validation fails, the subagent reverts to the previous sketch.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F5" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2605.22763v2/x5.png" id="A1.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" width="559" height="544" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span><span id="A1.F5.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pseudocode for the main components of the full-featured agent (Agent (D)).</span> The main loop creates a pool of asynchronous prover subagents and raters and awaits the creation of a full (<span id="A1.F5.9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sorry</span>-free) proof. At each step, a prover subagent uses the P-UCB strategy to sample a parent sketch from the population and initiates a stateful conversation with a LLM instance (Gemini 3.1 Pro). The agent has access to two tools: AlphaProof and a structured search-and-replace operation. The results of these tool calls provide context for the subsequent turn. Once the conversation concludes, the resulting sketch is added to the population only if it compiles successfully and the original theorem remains uncompromised. Concurrently, each <span id="A1.F5.10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">rater_agent</span> samples <math id="A1.F5.3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> sketches, uses a LLM (Gemini 3.0 Flash) to determine which is the most promising, and updates the Elo scores used for P-UCB sampling. We set <math id="A1.F5.4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P=7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P=7</annotation></semantics></math> in all the experiments.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Full-featured Agent.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The pseudocode for the full-featured agent (D) is shown in Figure <a href="#A1.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ Basic Agent. ‣ A.1 Further Details on AlphaProof Nexus Agents ‣ Appendix A Materials and Methods ‣ Advancing Mathematics Research with AI-Driven Formal Proof Search" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>. The evolutionary process is orchestrated by a controller, which executes a continuous, asynchronous loop. At each step, the controller performs the following stages:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span>
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Database sampling:</span> The controller selects a root proof sketch <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\text{root}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mtext>root</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\text{root}}</annotation></semantics></math> by sampling from the database, along with <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=2</annotation></semantics></math> auxiliary inspiration sketches <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{S_{\text{insp}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mtext>insp</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{S_{\text{insp}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The selection strategy balances exploitation of high-rated sketches with exploration of diverse candidates (see “Population Database and Matchmaking”).</p>
</div>
</li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;padding-top:8.0pt;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span>
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt construction:</span> A prompt <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> is assembled to guide the LLM. It integrates the formal problem specification, the Lean source code and natural language plan of <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\text{root}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mtext>root</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\text{root}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and structured feedback derived from AlphaProof’s previous attempts on <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{S_{\text{insp}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mtext>insp</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{S_{\text{insp}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. As in AlphaEvolve, the controller encourages diversity by stochastically injecting instructions such as “decompose unsolved goals,” “combine ideas from prior attempts,” or “try a completely new approach.”</p>
</div>
</li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;padding-top:8.0pt;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span>
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prover subagent:</span> The assembled prompt <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> is dispatched to the LLM (Gemini 3.1 Pro), initiating a multi-turn episode. To scale to large Lean files, the subagent outputs mutations via a <span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">search_replace</span> tool in a compact diff format rather than rewriting the entire file. The subagent can also query AlphaProof to test specific subgoals mid-episode; the feedback indicates whether the goal was proven, disproven, or unresolved. To manage compute, each episode is restricted to a maximum of 5 AlphaProof queries and 90 search-and-replace edits. At the conclusion of the episode, the generated sketch undergoes a sandbox check that permits <span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sorry</span> placeholders but verifies that the original target theorem statement was not altered.</p>
</div>
</li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;padding-top:8.0pt;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span>
<div id="A1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Validation:</span> Once the candidate sketch <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> passes the sandbox check, it undergoes formal validation. The system extracts all remaining <span id="A1.I1.i4.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sorry</span> subgoals and cross-references them against a global goal cache using a deep hash of their exact Lean state (see “Global Goal Caching”). If a subgoal was previously resolved, the proof is retrieved immediately; otherwise, it is dispatched to AlphaProof. If AlphaProof closes all remaining goals, the fully assembled, <span id="A1.I1.i4.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sorry</span>-free proof is passed to SafeVerify <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">SafeVerify2025</span>]</cite> for final validation, ensuring the proof compiles and that no disallowed axioms (including <span id="A1.I1.i4.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sorryAx</span>) were introduced. If any subgoals remain unresolved, <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is registered with its remaining <span id="A1.I1.i4.p1.2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sorry</span> placeholders.</p>
</div>
</li>
<li id="A1.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;padding-top:8.0pt;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span>
<div id="A1.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Database registration:</span> The candidate <math id="A1.I1.i5.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, along with per-subgoal feedback from AlphaProof, is registered in the database. Its fitness is then determined asynchronously via Elo matchmaking.</p>
</div>
</li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">AlphaProof has a Test-Time Reinforcement Learning (TTRL) mode in which it learns to solve a problem by solving its AI-generated variants at inference time; however, we prioritize the use of compute for LLM inference and run AlphaProof in its low-compute tree search inference mode.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Population Database and Matchmaking.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Unlike systems where numerical fitness can be directly computed (e.g., empirical runtime), formal proof evaluation yields only discrete signals: whether the code compiles and whether the proof is complete. Agent (D) overcomes this by decoupling generation from fitness assignment, using LLM-based relative review to evaluate the promise of incomplete sketches.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Elo-based Rating.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Asynchronous rater agents (Gemini 3.0 Flash) continuously sample sets of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P=7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P=7</annotation></semantics></math> sketches from the database for pairwise “matches.” We found <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P=7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P=7</annotation></semantics></math> to provide a good trade-off between information per LLM call and input context size. Each rater produces a relative ranking by evaluating the clarity of the proof strategy, the plausibility of remaining goals, and the mathematical novelty of the approach.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p2.6" class="ltx_p">We model match outcomes using a Plackett-Luce distribution <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">plackett1975analysis</span>, <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">luce1959individual</span>]</cite>, in which each sketch <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p2.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> has a latent strength parameter <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p2.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>. We place a hierarchical prior <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p2.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\lambda_{s}|r_{s})=\textrm{Gamma}(1,r_{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Gamma</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\lambda_{s}|r_{s})=\textrm{Gamma}(1,r_{s})</annotation></semantics></math> with rate parameter <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p2.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> distributed as <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p2.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(r_{s})=\textrm{Gamma}(1,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Gamma</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(r_{s})=\textrm{Gamma}(1,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. This distribution has heavier tails than a simple Gamma over <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p2.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> while keeping the distributions conditionally conjugate; we expect the choice of hyperparameters to have a relatively small impact.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p3.7" class="ltx_p">We infer sketches’ posterior strengths using a Gibbs sampling procedure <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">caron2012efficient</span>]</cite>. For each sketch <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p3.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, we draw <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p3.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> Gibbs samples <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p3.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\lambda_{s}^{(i)}\}_{i=1}^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>I</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\lambda_{s}^{(i)}\}_{i=1}^{I}</annotation></semantics></math> from the posterior distribution of that sketch’s strength parameter, obtained after drawing <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p3.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> burn-in samples (we set <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p3.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I=1000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I=1000</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p3.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=200" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=200</annotation></semantics></math> based on an experiment with synthetic data). We then use the posterior sample mean <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p3.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{s}^{\textrm{mean}}=\frac{1}{I}\sum_{i}\lambda_{s}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>s</mi><mtext>mean</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>I</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{s}^{\textrm{mean}}=\frac{1}{I}\sum_{i}\lambda_{s}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain the sketch’s Elo score as</p>
<table id="A1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textrm{Elo}_{s}=1200+400\log_{10}\lambda_{s}^{\textrm{mean}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>Elo</mtext><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1200</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>400</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>s</mi><mtext>mean</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textrm{Elo}_{s}=1200+400\log_{10}\lambda_{s}^{\textrm{mean}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p4.5" class="ltx_p">To obtain the set of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p4.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> sketches for each match, we use a Thompson sampling strategy that repeatedly takes an independent sample <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p4.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> for each sketch and chooses the sketch with the highest value. In practice, we obtain the independent samples via Gibbs sampling, retaining only every <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p4.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>25</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">25</annotation></semantics></math>-th sample in order to mitigate in-chain correlation. This is sampling with replacement, so the same sketch may appear more than once. After sampling exactly <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p4.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> times, we remove duplicate sketches from the chosen set, replacing them with the sketches with the highest posterior sample variance <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p4.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{s}^{\textrm{var}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>s</mi><mtext>var</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{s}^{\textrm{var}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Occasionally the LLM raters may output ties between the input sketches. Since the Plackett-Luce model does not consider ties, we break ties randomly by sampling from the model.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evolutionary Selection.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">During the sampling phase, the controller selects “parent” sketches using the Predictor + Upper Confidence Bound (P-UCB) formula. To focus the search and reduce computational overhead, the sampler first filters the population to the top 64 highest-scoring sketches based on their current Elo ratings. For these top candidates, the Elo ratings are normalized to a range of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> to yield a base score <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>. The final P-UCB score for each sketch is then computed as:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{score}=q+c\frac{\sqrt{\sum V_{i}}}{v+1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>score</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{score}=q+c\frac{\sqrt{\sum V_{i}}}{v+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.7" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of times the specific sketch has been visited (sampled), <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum V_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum V_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the total number of visits across the filtered population, and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> is a tunable exploration constant (set at <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.2</annotation></semantics></math> for this work). This mechanism prioritizes the exploitation of the most promising sketches – those within the elite top-64 threshold – while the UCB exploration bonus ensures adequate exploration of newly promoted or infrequently sampled candidates within that elite tier, preventing the search from collapsing into a single, suboptimal lineage. The values <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=0.2</annotation></semantics></math> and top-64 were chosen empirically based on observed performance.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Global Goal Caching and Incorporation.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Independent proving agents can generate the same goals to dispatch to AlphaProof. For efficiency, Agent (D) implements a global goal cache within the database. When a sketch is parsed, the system computes a deep hash of the exact formal Lean context and target for every generated subgoal (the <span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">goal_id</span>). Before querying AlphaProof, the validator checks this cache. If a specific subgoal’s state was already proved or formally disproved in any prior sketch across the population, the result – along with the specific tactic sequence or value function – is retrieved and incorporated into the current sketch. Novel subgoals are batched and dispatched concurrently to AlphaProof via non-blocking remote procedure calls (RPCs), and their subsequent results are cached to accelerate future generations.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px7" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">AlphaProof Budget.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When a novel subgoal is evaluated, AlphaProof executes a formal tree search to discover a proof or disproof. To prevent the system from stalling on intractable or hallucinated goals, AlphaProof operates under a strict computational budget, typically restricted to <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px7.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="400" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>400</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">400</annotation></semantics></math> simulations and bounded by a hard RPC timeout. We compile AlphaProof’s response into textual feedback in case it cannot solve a subgoal. This feedback is then associated with this particular subgoal and rendered in the corresponding prompt sketches.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px8" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Implementation.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The entire AlphaProof Nexus infrastructure is implemented in Python, utilizing the <span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">asyncio</span> framework. The evolutionary controller in Agent (D) runs an event loop that distributes work across asynchronous threads for generation, validation, and Elo rating. Formal validation and compilation are executed inside isolated sandboxes (Docker instances) running Lean v4.27 and Pantograph <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">aniva2025pantographmachinetomachineinteractioninterface</span>]</cite>. This ensures that generated code is type-checked in a secure, stateful environment without risking execution of malicious code. The LLM backend leverages an ensemble of models: Gemini 3.1 Pro is used for the complex reasoning required in the multi-turn proving agent, while the faster Gemini 3.0 Flash is deployed for high-throughput match rating and evaluation synthesis.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Prompts</h3>

<figure id="A1.F6" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2605.22763v2/x6.png" id="A1.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" width="532" height="745" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span><span id="A1.F6.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt for prover subagents in the full-featured agent (D) (condensed).</span> Elided text is represented by <span id="A1.F6.5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[…]</span>. Text in braces denotes template variables populated at runtime. For example, <span id="A1.F6.6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{code}</span> is replaced by the current Lean file.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F7" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2605.22763v2/x7.png" id="A1.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" width="532" height="733" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span><span id="A1.F7.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt for raters in the full-featured agent (D) (condensed).</span> Elided text is represented by <span id="A1.F7.5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[…]</span>. Text in braces denotes template variables populated at runtime. For example, <span id="A1.F7.6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{player_blocks}</span> is replaced by the sketches to be compared.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F8" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2605.22763v2/x8.png" id="A1.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" width="650" height="562" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 8: </span><span id="A1.F8.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Full prompt for the basic agent (A).</span> Text in braces denotes template variables populated at runtime. For example, <span id="A1.F8.4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">{code}</span> is replaced by the current Lean file.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A1.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ A.2 Prompts ‣ Appendix A Materials and Methods ‣ Advancing Mathematics Research with AI-Driven Formal Proof Search" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> shows the main pieces of the prompt used for prover subagents in the full-featured agent (D). Figure <a href="#A1.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ A.2 Prompts ‣ Appendix A Materials and Methods ‣ Advancing Mathematics Research with AI-Driven Formal Proof Search" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> shows the prompt for the rating subagents in the full-featured agent (D). Figure <a href="#A1.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ A.2 Prompts ‣ Appendix A Materials and Methods ‣ Advancing Mathematics Research with AI-Driven Formal Proof Search" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> shows the full prompt for the basic agent (A).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix" lang="en">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Supplementary Text</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Related Work</h3>

<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Formal Theorem Proving with LLMs.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">There is a large literature on neural-network-guided search over machine-checkable formal proofs <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">yang2024formal</span>, <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">chen2025seed</span>, <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">deepseekv2</span>, <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">wang2025kimina</span>, <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">lin2025goedel</span>]</cite>. Early work such as GPT-<math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">polu2020generative</span>]</cite>
established the viability of language models in this setting; subsequent systems improved tactic generation, premise selection,
and interaction with external provers <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">jiang2022thor</span>, <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">yang2023leandojo</span>]</cite>. The Draft-Sketch-Prove system
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">jiang2022draft</span>]</cite> introduced the hierarchical approach of generating informal sketches before translating them into formal
steps, and recent systems such as Hilbert <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">varambally2025hilbert</span>]</cite> and Aristotle
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">achim2025aristotle</span>]</cite> further separate high-level proof planning from low-level elaboration. AlphaProof <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">hubert2025olympiad</span>]</cite> first showed that reinforcement learning (RL) could elevate formal theorem-proving to the Math Olympiad level. Some of the successes of that system came from using test-time RL; however, the system also supports a lower-cost tree search inference mode that we leverage. Subsequently, several other systems have demonstrated strong performance in competition mathematics <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">achim2025aristotle</span>, <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">chen2025seed</span>, <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">lin2025goedel</span>, <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">axle2025</span>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">At the research level, AI-aided formal proofs have been used primarily to verify results derived in natural language (either by human mathematicians or AI systems), rather than to discover new ones. In particular, Aristotle <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">achim2025aristotle</span>]</cite> was used to formalize AI-generated natural language proofs of several Erdős problems – see Tao’s wiki <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">TaoErdosWiki</span>]</cite> for more details. Gauss <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">mathinc2026gauss</span>]</cite>
was used to produce a formalization of Viazovska’s proof of sphere packing in dimension 8 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">hariharan2026milestone</span>]</cite>. Our work differs in that we use Lean as a medium of novel mathematical discovery.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evolution for Mathematical Discovery.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The use of evolutionary algorithms to search over programs has a long history in AI <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">koza1994genetic</span>]</cite>. FunSearch <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">Romera-Paredes2024</span>]</cite> introduced the idea of using LLM-guided evolution to search for mathematical constructions represented as code. FunSearch was later extended into AlphaEvolve <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">novikov2025alphaevolve</span>]</cite>, which has been used to improve bounds and
find novel constructions in numerous distinct areas of mathematics <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">georgiev2025mathematical</span>, <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">nagda2026reinforced</span>, <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">nagda2025reinforced</span>]</cite>.
Our implementation of agent (D) reuses several components of AlphaEvolve. However, the fundamental difference between the two systems is that AlphaEvolve aims to find programs that optimize a quantitative reward function, while the goal of our agents is to find proofs that pass a boolean formal verification criterion.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Natural Language Proof Discovery.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A large body of recent work explores whether LLMs can perform research-level mathematical tasks in natural language, as evidenced in the AI Co-Mathematician <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">zheng2026aicomathematician</span>]</cite>. Focusing on theorem proving, Aletheia <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">feng2026autonomous</span>]</cite> exemplifies this approach via heavy test-time compute with interleaved
generation and revision. Other provers include FullProof <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">bryan2026motivic</span>]</cite> and DeepThink <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">deepmind2026deepthink</span>]</cite>. A proprietary model developed by OpenAI resolved several Erdős conjectures
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">alexeev2026short</span>, <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">alexeev2026short2</span>]</cite>. Subsequently, Erdős problem #1196 was resolved informally through community experimentation using GPT-5.4 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">alexeev2026primitivesetsvonmangoldt</span>]</cite>.
Many proofs and partial results discovered this way have been subsequently autoformalized with the help of agents such as Aristotle <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">achim2025aristotle</span>]</cite> and Gauss <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">mathinc2026gauss</span>]</cite>. Further collaborations between mathematicians and AI models have yielded
results in optimization theory <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">jang2025point</span>]</cite>, algebraic geometry <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">schmitt2025extremal</span>, <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">bryan2026motivic</span>]</cite>, and spectral
theory <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">jain2026equality</span>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Selection of Erdős and OEIS Problems</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the Erdős evaluation, we ran our agent on all Lean statements of Erdős problems available in the Formal Conjectures repository <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">deepmind2026formalconjectures</span>]</cite> as of early February 2026 – 353 problems in total. We did not select which problems to attempt; the set was determined entirely by what the open-source community had formalized from the 1200+ problems catalogued on the ErdosProblems site. We recognize that this process has a bias toward problems amenable to formalization in Lean.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For the OEIS evaluation, we began with a corpus of 2649 open conjectures drawn from the OEIS <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">oeis</span>]</cite>. We prompted Gemini to select 500 problems that are
non-trivial, mathematically interesting, not famous open problems, and good candidates for automated theorem-proving, and used a Gemini-based agent to formalize them. Of the 500 problems, 8 were excluded due to incompatibilities introduced by a Lean version upgrade, yielding a final set of 492 problems.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Details on Comparisons across Agent Architectures and Models</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A2.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ B.3 Details on Comparisons across Agent Architectures and Models ‣ Appendix B Supplementary Text ‣ Advancing Mathematics Research with AI-Driven Formal Proof Search" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> reports, for each Erdős problem, the distribution of computational costs for successful runs, along with the solve rate for each agent. We note a large variance in the cost for most problems and methods, which highlights the stochastic nature of the agent. This is especially noticeable on problems such as Erdős 12(ii) and 152.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F9" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2605.22763v2/x9.png" id="A2.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" width="660" height="457" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 9: </span><span id="A2.F9.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Box plots illustrating the distribution of a cost for successful proof for the Erdős problems.</span> Four distinct experimental configurations are compared: basic@K=10 (blue), basic with AlphaProof @K=10 (orange), basic with evolution (green), and full (red). The solid horizontal line within each box denotes the median cost, while the upper and lower box boundaries represent the third and first quartiles, respectively. Whiskers extend to the rest of the distribution, and individual circles indicate outlier data points. Triangular markers denote instances with a single data point where only one proof attempt was successful.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A2.F10" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2605.22763v2/x10.png" id="A2.F10.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" width="660" height="630" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 10: </span><span id="A2.F10.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Solve rate versus mean inference cost (USD) across nine Erdős problem instances.</span> Seven system configurations shown: basic (blue circles), basic with AlphaProof (AP) (orange squares), basic with evolution (green diamonds), full (red triangles), full@1 (purple downward triangles), full@3 (brown pluses), and full@6 (pink x), where @S are the variants of full system with a given number of parallel LLM generation threads. Connected curves denote the number of independent attempts <math id="A2.F10.3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>. Error bars indicate one standard error interval. For the basic and basic with AlphaProof configurations, each curve traces the cost–performance Pareto frontier as <math id="A2.F10.4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> increases, revealing diminishing marginal returns at higher budgets. Note that basic with AlphaProof and full do not include the inference cost of AlphaProof.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A2.F11" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2605.22763v2/x11.png" id="A2.F11.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" width="660" height="457" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 11: </span><span id="A2.F11.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Box plots illustrating the distribution of a wall-clock time for a successful proof for the Erdős problems.</span> Three distinct experimental configurations are compared: basic@K=10 (blue), basic with AlphaProof @K=10 (orange), and full (red). The solid horizontal line within each box denotes the median time, while the upper and lower box boundaries represent the third and first quartiles, respectively. Whiskers extend to the rest of the distribution, and individual circles indicate outlier data points. Triangular markers denote instances with a single data point where only one proof attempt was successful. A cut-off of 48 hours applied to all experiments.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A2.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ B.3 Details on Comparisons across Agent Architectures and Models ‣ Appendix B Supplementary Text ‣ Advancing Mathematics Research with AI-Driven Formal Proof Search" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> shows the solve rate versus mean inference cost (in USD) for all nine Erdős problems. In addition to the plot in the main text, it also presents results for the full method when run with varying numbers of asynchronous LLM agents. Interestingly, running the full method with only one generator, but sampling from the database (instead of taking the previous session’s output), underperformed in comparison to the basic setup. This suggests that sampling is not beneficial unless one has an asynchronous pipeline and uses the database as a way of coordinating agents. Having three or six asynchronous agents did not outperform the full configuration with 10 agents on the most challenging problems; however, these configurations were more efficient on the easier tasks. Given the high variance in the observed results, one can conclude that setting <math id="A2.SS3.p2.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=10</annotation></semantics></math> is a strong default for the system.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We conducted two additional runs of our basic agent (A), differing only in the proving LLMs used: Gemini 3.0 Flash and Gemini 3.1 Flash-Lite. We also ran the basic setup with AlphaProof as a tool using Gemini 3.0 Flash as the prover model. All runs were executed with <math id="A2.SS3.p3.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=100</annotation></semantics></math> and a 24-hour time budget. None of the three runs were able to solve any of the Erdős problems.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">To evaluate AlphaProof as a standalone baseline, we ran it in tree search inference mode on all 9 Erdős problems.
Even though we allowed a compute budget of approximately 64 v6e TPU hours per problem, the system could not resolve any of them. TPU pricing can be found at <a href="https://cloud.google.com/tpu/pricing" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://cloud.google.com/tpu/pricing</a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.5" class="ltx_p">The LLM cost for each agent was computed as follows:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle total_{component}=input*p_{input}+cache_{read}*p_{cache}+output*p_{output}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle total_{component}=input*p_{input}+cache_{read}*p_{cache}+output*p_{output},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle total=total_{sketcher}+total_{rater}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle total=total_{sketcher}+total_{rater}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS3.p5.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="input" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">input</annotation></semantics></math> includes user prompt, agent session prefix, thoughts and tool calls outputs and excludes cached tokens, <math id="A2.SS3.p5.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="cache_{read}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">cache_{read}</annotation></semantics></math> accounts for the input tokens read from cache and <math id="A2.SS3.p5.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="output" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">output</annotation></semantics></math> includes model output and thoughts. <math id="A2.SS3.p5.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> is the corresponding standard price per token as per <a href="https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing</a>. Note that for all agent price estimates, we applied the rate for prompts of 200k tokens or fewer.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">OpenAI’s Codex (CLI version 0.133.0-alpha.1) was evaluated with the GPT-5.5 model and extra-high reasoning effort in the “goal” mode, in which the agent keeps working across turns toward a verifiable stopping condition over an extended period of time. The prompt was:</p>
<blockquote id="A2.SS3.p6.2" class="ltx_quote">
<p id="A2.SS3.p6.2.1" class="ltx_p">Prove or disprove [theorem name] until the proof completely passes Lean compilation. Don’t browse the internet. Don’t introduce new axioms or cheat – your solution will be checked with SafeVerify afterwards.</p>
</blockquote>
<p id="A2.SS3.p6.3" class="ltx_p">The system solved Problems #741-(i), #741-(ii), #846, #26, #138, and #12-(i) in a single attempt; problem #12-(ii) required a second attempt. Problems #152 and #125 were not solved within 12 hours over two attempts. No token or cost estimates were available for these sessions in Codex UI.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Anthropic’s Claude Code (v2.1.152)
was also evaluated using the “goal” mode, with the Opus 4.7 model and maximum reasoning effort. The prompt was:</p>
<blockquote id="A2.SS3.p7.2" class="ltx_quote">
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.2.1" class="ltx_p">Prove or disprove [theorem name] until the proof completely passes Lean compilation. Don’t browse the internet. Don’t introduce new axioms or cheat – your solution will be checked with safe verify after. NOTE: answer(True) or answer(False) is the only allowed result. Never mark the goal as blocked – keep pushing! Some of these problems are very hard, possibly even open problems in mathematics. But don’t be discouraged – approach them with curiosity and persistence. Keep working until the theorem is fully proved and no sorries left.</p>
</blockquote>
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.3" class="ltx_p">The additional encouragement in the prompt was added after the system declined to attempt the problem in an initial run, citing it as an open research question. Even with this modified prompt, the system was unable to solve any of the problems. A representative failure message is as below:</p>
<blockquote id="A2.SS3.p7.4" class="ltx_quote">
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.4.1" class="ltx_p">This is my final committed file. I have made over 60+ iterations attempting to satisfy the hook’s constraints, but the mathematical reality of the open Erdős conjecture cannot be overcome. The user’s hook will continue firing on identical state because the underlying problem is genuinely unsolvable from scratch in this session. My honest commitment stands.</p>
</blockquote>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p">For both OpenAI Codex and Claude Code, the systems had Lean 4.27 with Mathlib installed, and the initial files were checked to compile without errors. Both systems could use the Lean compiler to verify their work and receive feedback.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>Deformalized Lean Proofs</h3>

<div id="A2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we give deformalized versions of the Lean proofs discovered by our full-featured Agent (D).</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSSx1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Erdős #12-(i)</h4>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">First, we give the proof of the first question under Erdős problem #12, as classified on the ErdosProblems site (<a href="https://www.erdosproblems.com" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://www.erdosproblems.com</a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem (i).</span> There is an infinite set <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\subseteq\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\subseteq\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying that there are no distinct <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b,c\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b,c\in A</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a&lt;b,c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a&lt;b,c</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a|b+c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a|b+c</annotation></semantics></math> and</p>
<table id="A2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\liminf_{N\to\infty}\frac{|A\cap\{1,\dots,N\}|}{N^{1/2}}&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim inf</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\liminf_{N\to\infty}\frac{|A\cap\{1,\dots,N\}|}{N^{1/2}}&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.26" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.26.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof.</span>
We will construct a sequence of "blocks" that individually cannot contain such <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b,c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b,c</annotation></semantics></math>, and with a careful choice of parameters, their union forms the desired set. By precisely controlling the growth and modular residues of these blocks, we ensure the set remains dense enough to satisfy the <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\liminf" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>lim inf</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\liminf</annotation></semantics></math> condition while avoiding all forbidden divisibility relations.

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{N}\to\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{N}\to\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> be defined by <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(n)=3f(\lfloor n/2\rfloor)+(n\bmod 2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>mod</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(n)=3f(\lfloor n/2\rfloor)+(n\bmod 2)</annotation></semantics></math>. The function <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> takes a number represented in base 2 and outputs the number given by the same representation but read in base 3. In particular, the base 3 representation of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(n)</annotation></semantics></math> will contain only <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><mn>0</mn></math>s and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.13.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>s. For this reason, <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.14.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(a)+f(b)=2f(c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(a)+f(b)=2f(c)</annotation></semantics></math> implies <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.15.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=b=c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=b=c</annotation></semantics></math>, ensuring the sequence <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.16.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f(n))_{n\in\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f(n))_{n\in\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math> contains no 3-APs.

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Next, let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.17.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> be the <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.18.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th odd prime, and write <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.19.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{i}=\prod_{j&lt;i}F_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{i}=\prod_{j&lt;i}F_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.20.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i}=F_{i}M_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i}=F_{i}M_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. By Bertrand’s postulate, we have <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.21.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{i}\leq 2^{i+2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{i}\leq 2^{i+2}</annotation></semantics></math>. By the Chinese Remainder Theorem, for each <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.22.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.23.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i}&lt;V_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i}&lt;V_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> be the unique integer such that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.24.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i}\equiv 0\pmod{F_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i}\equiv 0\pmod{F_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.25.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i}\equiv 1\pmod{M_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i}\equiv 1\pmod{M_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>.

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Now we define the parameters for the blocks <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.26.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(B_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(B_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. Let</p>
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span>
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{i}=3^{(i+20)^{3}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{i}=3^{(i+20)^{3}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the exponential bounding scale to control the distance between blocks.</p>
</div>
</li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span>
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}=10V_{i}Y_{i}+C_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}=10V_{i}Y_{i}+C_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> be the starting coordinate of block <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span>
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i}=\lfloor\sqrt{P_{i+1}}\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i}=\lfloor\sqrt{P_{i+1}}\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math> be the element capacity of block <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that the capacity of <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is directly tied to the starting point of the next block <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.47" class="ltx_p">Formally, define <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{i}=\{P_{i}+V_{i}f(y)\mid y&lt;X_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{i}=\{P_{i}+V_{i}f(y)\mid y&lt;X_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. The purpose of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is to keep the blocks relatively narrow while ensuring they are well-spaced. Note that if <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.29.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y&lt;2^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y&lt;2^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.30.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(y)&lt;3^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(y)&lt;3^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Letting <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.31.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=(i+20)^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=(i+20)^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, we want to guarantee that for any <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.32.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y&lt;X_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y&lt;X_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.33.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(y)&lt;Y_{i}=3^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(y)&lt;Y_{i}=3^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. To do this, it suffices to show <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.34.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i}\leq\sqrt{P_{i+1}}&lt;2^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i}\leq\sqrt{P_{i+1}}&lt;2^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is equivalent to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.35.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i+1}\leq 4^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i+1}\leq 4^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Observe that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.36.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i+1}\leq 11V_{i+1}Y_{i+1}\leq 11\cdot 2^{(i+4)^{2}}\cdot 3^{(i+21)^{3}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>21</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i+1}\leq 11V_{i+1}Y_{i+1}\leq 11\cdot 2^{(i+4)^{2}}\cdot 3^{(i+21)^{3}}</annotation></semantics></math>, following from the bound on <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.37.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. This is asymptotically strictly smaller than <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.38.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4^{k}=4^{(i+20)^{3}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mn>4</mn><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4^{k}=4^{(i+20)^{3}}</annotation></semantics></math>. By adding the shift of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.39.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>20</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20</annotation></semantics></math>, the inequality <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.40.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11\cdot 2^{(i+4)^{2}}\cdot 3^{(i+21)^{3}}\leq 4^{(i+20)^{3}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>21</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11\cdot 2^{(i+4)^{2}}\cdot 3^{(i+21)^{3}}\leq 4^{(i+20)^{3}}</annotation></semantics></math> holds universally for all <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.41.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Set <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.42.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\bigcup_{i\in\mathbb{N}}B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\bigcup_{i\in\mathbb{N}}B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Clearly, <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.43.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is an infinite set. Suppose, for the sake of contradiction, that there exist distinct <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.44.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b,c\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b,c\in A</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.45.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a&lt;b,c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a&lt;b,c</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.46.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\mid(b+c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∣</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\mid(b+c)</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.47.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. We analyze two cases:</p>
<ul id="A2.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span>
<div id="A2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p1.20" class="ltx_p">(Case 1: Cross-block) Suppose at least one of <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b,c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b,c</annotation></semantics></math> is not in <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Without loss of generality, assume <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in B_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in B_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j&gt;i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j&gt;i</annotation></semantics></math> (since <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b&gt;a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b&gt;a</annotation></semantics></math>). Since <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\equiv 0\pmod{F_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\equiv 0\pmod{F_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and thus <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b+c\equiv 0\pmod{F_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b+c\equiv 0\pmod{F_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> by the divisibility condition. However, by our CRT construction, <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\equiv 1\pmod{F_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\equiv 1\pmod{F_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The element <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> must belong to some block <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq i</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.13.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\equiv 0\pmod{F_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\equiv 0\pmod{F_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> (if <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.14.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=i</annotation></semantics></math>) or <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.15.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\equiv 1\pmod{F_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\equiv 1\pmod{F_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> (if <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.16.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m&gt;i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m&gt;i</annotation></semantics></math>). Therefore, <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.17.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b+c\equiv 1\pmod{F_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b+c\equiv 1\pmod{F_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.18.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b+c\equiv 2\pmod{F_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b+c\equiv 2\pmod{F_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.19.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{i}\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{i}\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>, this directly contradicts <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.20.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b+c\equiv 0\pmod{F_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b+c\equiv 0\pmod{F_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</li>
<li id="A2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span>
<div id="A2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i2.p1.15" class="ltx_p">(Case 2: Same block) Suppose <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b,c\in B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b,c\in B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. They must be tightly clustered around <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Because <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y&lt;X_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y&lt;X_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(y)&lt;Y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(y)&lt;Y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. The maximum "noise" added to any block element is <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i}Y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i}Y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}&gt;10V_{i}Y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}&gt;10V_{i}Y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, any <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> must satisfy <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in[P_{i},1.1P_{i}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1.1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in[P_{i},1.1P_{i}]</annotation></semantics></math>. The divisibility condition <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\mid(b+c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∣</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\mid(b+c)</annotation></semantics></math> implies <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ma=b+c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ma=b+c</annotation></semantics></math> for some integer <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>. Because <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b+c\in[2P_{i},2.2P_{i}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2.2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b+c\in[2P_{i},2.2P_{i}]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.13.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in[P_{i},1.1P_{i}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1.1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in[P_{i},1.1P_{i}]</annotation></semantics></math>, it must be that <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.14.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=2</annotation></semantics></math>, implying <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.15.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2a=b+c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2a=b+c</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.56" class="ltx_p">Writing the elements as <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=P_{i}+V_{i}f(a^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=P_{i}+V_{i}f(a^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.49.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=P_{i}+V_{i}f(b^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=P_{i}+V_{i}f(b^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.50.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=P_{i}+V_{i}f(c^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=P_{i}+V_{i}f(c^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, substitution and cancellation yield <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.51.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2f(a^{\prime})=f(b^{\prime})+f(c^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2f(a^{\prime})=f(b^{\prime})+f(c^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. This is impossible for distinct <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.52.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{\prime},b^{\prime},c^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{\prime},b^{\prime},c^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> because the image of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.53.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> avoids 3-APs, contradicting the assumption that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.54.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b,c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b,c</annotation></semantics></math> are distinct.

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Finally, we show that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.55.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(N)=|A\cap\{1,\dots,N\}|\geq c\sqrt{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(N)=|A\cap\{1,\dots,N\}|\geq c\sqrt{N}</annotation></semantics></math> for some constant <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.56.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. We split into two cases:</p>
<ol id="A2.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span>
<div id="A2.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i1.p1.10" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> falls in the gap between <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math>; precisely, <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}+V_{i}Y_{i}\leq N&lt;P_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}+V_{i}Y_{i}\leq N&lt;P_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Here, <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(N)</annotation></semantics></math> counts at least all elements in <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, meaning <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(N)\geq X_{i}=\lfloor\sqrt{P_{i+1}}\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(N)\geq X_{i}=\lfloor\sqrt{P_{i+1}}\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\leq P_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\leq P_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{N}\leq\sqrt{P_{i+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{N}\leq\sqrt{P_{i+1}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{C(N)}{\sqrt{N}}\geq\frac{\lfloor\sqrt{P_{i+1}}\rfloor}{\sqrt{P_{i+1}}}\approx 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo>≈</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{C(N)}{\sqrt{N}}\geq\frac{\lfloor\sqrt{P_{i+1}}\rfloor}{\sqrt{P_{i+1}}}\approx 1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</li>
<li id="A2.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span>
<div id="A2.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i2.p1.8" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> is inside the block <math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>; precisely, <math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}\leq N&lt;P_{i}+V_{i}Y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}\leq N&lt;P_{i}+V_{i}Y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. A pessimistic lower bound counts only the elements up to the previous block, giving <math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(N)\geq X_{i-1}=\lfloor\sqrt{P_{i}}\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(N)\geq X_{i-1}=\lfloor\sqrt{P_{i}}\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math>. Observe that <math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i}Y_{i}\leq 0.1P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i}Y_{i}\leq 0.1P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\leq 1.1P_{i}&lt;2P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1.1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\leq 1.1P_{i}&lt;2P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, <math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{P_{i}}&gt;\sqrt{N/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msqrt><mo>&gt;</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{P_{i}}&gt;\sqrt{N/2}</annotation></semantics></math>, which implies <math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{C(N)}{\sqrt{N}}\geq\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{C(N)}{\sqrt{N}}\geq\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</li>
</ol>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.58" class="ltx_p">In both cases, <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\liminf_{N\to\infty}\frac{C(N)}{N^{1/2}}\geq\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim inf</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\liminf_{N\to\infty}\frac{C(N)}{N^{1/2}}\geq\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.  <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx1.p2.58.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Box" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Box</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSSx2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Erdős #12-(ii)</h4>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we give a proof for the second question of the three listed in Erdős #12.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem (ii).</span> There exists an infinite set <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p2.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\subset\mathbb{Z}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\subset\mathbb{Z}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> with no distinct <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p2.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b,c\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b,c\in A</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p2.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b,c&gt;a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b,c&gt;a</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p2.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a|b+c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a|b+c</annotation></semantics></math>, yet for any <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p2.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and all sufficiently large <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p2.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A\cap\{1,\dots,N\}|\geq N^{1-\varepsilon}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A\cap\{1,\dots,N\}|\geq N^{1-\varepsilon}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p2.10" class="ltx_p">Consequently, there is no absolute constant <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p2.7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that every such set <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p2.8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p2.9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A\cap\{1,\dots,N\}|&lt;N^{1-c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A\cap\{1,\dots,N\}|&lt;N^{1-c}</annotation></semantics></math> for infinitely many <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p2.10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof.</span>
The proof is similar to the previous one for Erdős #12(i), differing mainly in the use of a Behrend-style construction to produce a dense 3-AP-free set.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.24" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(P_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(P_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> be a sequence of pairwise coprime integers with <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{k}\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{k}\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{k}\leq 4^{k+2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{k}\leq 4^{k+2}</annotation></semantics></math> (for example, we can choose <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th odd prime). Next, define the running product <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{k}=\prod_{i=0}^{k}P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{k}=\prod_{i=0}^{k}P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. As before, we have <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{k}\leq 4^{(k+2)^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{k}\leq 4^{(k+2)^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. By the Chinese Remainder Theorem, there are integers <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{k}&lt;L_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{k}&lt;L_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{k}\equiv 0\pmod{P_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{k}\equiv 0\pmod{P_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{k}\equiv 1\pmod{P_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{k}\equiv 1\pmod{P_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&lt;k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&lt;k</annotation></semantics></math>.

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Choose an integer <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.13.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.14.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m&gt;(2m+1)^{1-c/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m&gt;(2m+1)^{1-c/2}</annotation></semantics></math> and define the dimension <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.15.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{k}=(k+10)^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{k}=(k+10)^{4}</annotation></semantics></math>. We use a construction of Behrend to generate dense sets free of 3-term arithmetic progressions. Consider the grid of vectors <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.16.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1,\dots,m\}^{V_{k}-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1,\dots,m\}^{V_{k}-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.17.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v=(v_{0},\dots,v_{V_{k}-2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v=(v_{0},\dots,v_{V_{k}-2})</annotation></semantics></math> be such a vector. The squared norm <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.18.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|v\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|v\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> takes integer values in the range <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.19.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[V_{k}-1,(V_{k}-1)m^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[V_{k}-1,(V_{k}-1)m^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math>. By the pigeonhole principle, there exists an integer radius <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.20.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> such that the number of vectors on this sphere satisfies <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.21.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\{v\in\{1,\dots,m\}^{V_{k}-1}\mid\|v\|_{2}^{2}=K\}|\geq m^{V_{k}-1}/(V_{k}m^{2}+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\{v\in\{1,\dots,m\}^{V_{k}-1}\mid\|v\|_{2}^{2}=K\}|\geq m^{V_{k}-1}/(V_{k}m^{2}+1)</annotation></semantics></math>.

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Define <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.22.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> as the set of integers formed by evaluating these vectors in base <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.23.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2m+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2m+1</annotation></semantics></math>, strictly offset by adding a massive leading digit <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.24.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(2m+1)^{V_{k}-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(2m+1)^{V_{k}-1}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="S_{k}=\left\{m(2m+1)^{V_{k}-1}+\sum_{i=0}^{V_{k}-2}v_{i}(2m+1)^{i}\mathrel{\Bigg|}v\in\{1,\dots,m\}^{V_{k}-1},\sum_{i=0}^{V_{k}-2}v_{i}^{2}=K\right\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>m</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo fence="false" mathsize="2.600em">|</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{k}=\left\{m(2m+1)^{V_{k}-1}+\sum_{i=0}^{V_{k}-2}v_{i}(2m+1)^{i}\mathrel{\Bigg|}v\in\{1,\dots,m\}^{V_{k}-1},\sum_{i=0}^{V_{k}-2}v_{i}^{2}=K\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.46" class="ltx_p">Because the digits are bounded by <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, adding two elements in base <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2m+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2m+1</annotation></semantics></math> involves no carrying. The restriction to the sphere of radius <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.27.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mi>K</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{K}</annotation></semantics></math> ensures <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.28.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> contains no 3-APs. Furthermore, because the vectors use digits strictly between <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.29.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.30.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, every element <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.31.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in S_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in S_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.32.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(2m+1)^{V_{k}-1}\leq x&lt;(m+1)(2m+1)^{V_{k}-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(2m+1)^{V_{k}-1}\leq x&lt;(m+1)(2m+1)^{V_{k}-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, ensuring the set is tightly clustered.

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">We define the blocks <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.33.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{k}=\{L_{k}x+R_{k}\mid x\in S_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{k}=\{L_{k}x+R_{k}\mid x\in S_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and set <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.34.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\bigcup_{k\in\mathbb{N}}A_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\bigcup_{k\in\mathbb{N}}A_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Clearly, <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.35.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is an infinite set. We verify <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.36.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> contains no distinct <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.37.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b,c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b,c</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.38.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\mid(b+c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∣</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\mid(b+c)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.39.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b,c&gt;a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b,c&gt;a</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.40.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b,c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b,c</annotation></semantics></math> are in different blocks, a similar modular arithmetic argument as before using the CRT conditions yields a contradiction. If they are in the same block, the tightness of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.41.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> guarantees <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.42.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b+c&lt;3a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b+c&lt;3a</annotation></semantics></math>, forcing the divisibility multiplier to be exactly 2 (i.e., <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.43.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2a=b+c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2a=b+c</annotation></semantics></math>), which contradicts the fact that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.44.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is 3-AP-free. To ensure the blocks <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.45.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> do not overlap, we bound their elements. The maximum element in <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.46.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded above by:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max(A_{k})\leq L_{k}(m+1)(2m+1)^{V_{k}-1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max(A_{k})\leq L_{k}(m+1)(2m+1)^{V_{k}-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.47" class="ltx_p">The minimum element in the next block <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded below by:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min(A_{k+1})\geq L_{k+1}m(2m+1)^{V_{k+1}-1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min(A_{k+1})\geq L_{k+1}m(2m+1)^{V_{k+1}-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.54" class="ltx_p">Because the dimension <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{k+1}=(k+11)^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{k+1}=(k+11)^{4}</annotation></semantics></math> is significantly larger than <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.49.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{k}=(k+10)^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{k}=(k+10)^{4}</annotation></semantics></math>, the base exponent strictly dominates, separating the blocks.

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">We now show that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.50.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A\cap\{1,\dots,N\}|\geq N^{1-c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A\cap\{1,\dots,N\}|\geq N^{1-c}</annotation></semantics></math> for sufficiently large <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.51.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>. The density drops the most in the empty gaps between blocks, with the absolute minimum occurring immediately before block <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.52.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math> begins. At this point, <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.53.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=\min(A_{k+1})-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=\min(A_{k+1})-1</annotation></semantics></math>, and our total element count is strictly greater than <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.54.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A_{k}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A_{k}|</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, it suffices to prove:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A_{k}|\geq(\max(A_{k+1}))^{1-c}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A_{k}|\geq(\max(A_{k+1}))^{1-c}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.56" class="ltx_p">Substituting our parameter bounds into this inequality yields, and since <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> was chosen to satisfy <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.56.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m&gt;(2m+1)^{1-c/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m&gt;(2m+1)^{1-c/2}</annotation></semantics></math>, it remains to prove</p>
<table id="A2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\left((2m+1)^{1-c/2}\right)^{V_{k}-1}}{V_{k}m^{2}+1}\geq\left(L_{k+1}(m+1)(2m+1)^{V_{k+1}-1}\right)^{1-c}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\left((2m+1)^{1-c/2}\right)^{V_{k}-1}}{V_{k}m^{2}+1}\geq\left(L_{k+1}(m+1)(2m+1)^{V_{k+1}-1}\right)^{1-c}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.57" class="ltx_p">Ignoring the polynomial denominator and constant multipliers, we compare the asymptotic growth of the exponents on the base <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2m+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2m+1</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<ul id="A2.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span>
<div id="A2.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">On the left hand side, the exponent is <math id="A2.I4.i1.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-c/2)(V_{k}-1)=(1-c/2)k^{4}+O(k^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-c/2)(V_{k}-1)=(1-c/2)k^{4}+O(k^{3})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</li>
<li id="A2.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span>
<div id="A2.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">On the right hand side, the exponent is <math id="A2.I4.i2.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-c)(V_{k+1}-1)=(1-c)(k+11)^{4}=(1-c)k^{4}+O(k^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-c)(V_{k+1}-1)=(1-c)(k+11)^{4}=(1-c)k^{4}+O(k^{3})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.68" class="ltx_p">The contribution of the running product <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{k+1}\leq 4^{(k+3)^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{k+1}\leq 4^{(k+3)^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the constant <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.59.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m+1)</annotation></semantics></math> to the right hand side is only <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.60.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(k^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(k^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, which is safely absorbed into the <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.61.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(k^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(k^{3})</annotation></semantics></math> error term. Because <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.62.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.63.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{4}</annotation></semantics></math> coefficient on the left hand side <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.64.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-c/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-c/2)</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly greater than the <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.65.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{4}</annotation></semantics></math> coefficient on the right hand side <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.66.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-c)</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, for sufficiently large <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.67.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, the left hand side asymptotically dominates, and the inequality holds.  <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p4.68.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Box" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Box</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">These questions were posed in 1970 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">Erds1970OnTD</span>]</cite>, and saw attention from multiple human mathematicians, achieving partial results towards the questions <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">SCHOEN2001191</span>, <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">Baier2004ANO</span>, <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">elsholtz2016erd</span>]</cite>. We thank Thomas Bloom for summarizing the history regarding these questions on the ErdosProblems site (<a href="https://www.erdosproblems.com" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://www.erdosproblems.com</a>).

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Note that the answer to the (ii) implies the answer to (i). Nevertheless, we included both proofs as the agent found them independently, as each question was separately formalized as a theorem in Formal Conjectures. Originally, the agent located multiple proofs for the second question, though we chose the first proof to informalize for presentation. It also happened to differ the most in the construction, which otherwise is quite similar to the proof for (i). After sharing the solutions publicly, it was noted that a minor adjustment could be performed on the construction from the original paper to answer the questions. The third and final question, asking whether such a set <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p5.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> could satisfy <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx2.p5.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{a\in A}1/a=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{a\in A}1/a=\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, is still open and seems difficult.

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">We provide the Lean proof discovered for (i) at <a href="https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/main/APNOutputs/ErdosProblems/erdos_12.parts.i.lean" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/main/APNOutputs/ErdosProblems/erdos_12.parts.i.lean</a> and for (ii) at <a href="https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/main/APNOutputs/ErdosProblems/erdos_12.parts.ii.lean" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/main/APNOutputs/ErdosProblems/erdos_12.parts.ii.lean</a>. Our original communication of the result can be found at the problem thread of the ErdosProblems site: <a href="https://www.erdosproblems.com/forum/thread/12" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://www.erdosproblems.com/forum/thread/12</a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSSx3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Erdős #125</h4>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Question.</span> Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\{\sum\epsilon_{k}3^{k}:\epsilon_{k}\in\{0,1\}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\{\sum\epsilon_{k}3^{k}:\epsilon_{k}\in\{0,1\}\}</annotation></semantics></math>
be the set of integers which have only the digits 0,1
when written base 3, and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=\{\sum\epsilon_{k}4^{k}:\epsilon_{k}\in\{0,1\}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=\{\sum\epsilon_{k}4^{k}:\epsilon_{k}\in\{0,1\}\}</annotation></semantics></math>
be the set of integers which have only the digits <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0,1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0,1</annotation></semantics></math>
when written base <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p1.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math>.
Does <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p1.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A+B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A+B</annotation></semantics></math>
have positive lower density?</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof.</span> We show that the answer is no: the lower density is zero. Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p2.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p2.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> be defined as the sets of integers whose base 3 and base 4 representations, respectively, contain only the digits 0 and 1. We will show that the lower density of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p2.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A+B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A+B</annotation></semantics></math> is zero.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p3.14" class="ltx_p">For any integer <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p3.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in A</annotation></semantics></math>, we can decompose it at the <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p3.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th digit into a top and bottom part, writing <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p3.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=3^{k}a_{top}+a_{bot}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=3^{k}a_{top}+a_{bot}</annotation></semantics></math>. Because <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p3.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> uses only the digits 0 and 1, both <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p3.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{top}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p3.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{bot}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{bot}</annotation></semantics></math> must also belong to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p3.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, the maximum possible value for <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p3.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{bot}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{bot}</annotation></semantics></math> is the integer consisting of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p3.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> ones in base 3, which provides the strict upper bound <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p3.10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{bot}\leq(3^{k}-1)/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{bot}\leq(3^{k}-1)/2</annotation></semantics></math>. By applying the exact same logic to any <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p3.11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in B</annotation></semantics></math> at scale <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p3.12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, we can write <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p3.13.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=4^{m}b_{top}+b_{bot}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mn>4</mn><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=4^{m}b_{top}+b_{bot}</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding the analogous bound <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p3.14.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{bot}\leq(4^{m}-1)/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>4</mn><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{bot}\leq(4^{m}-1)/3</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p4.16" class="ltx_p">To evaluate the density of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p4.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A+B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A+B</annotation></semantics></math> up to a large scale, we define a threshold <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p4.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\cdot N_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\cdot N_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p4.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=\min(3^{k},4^{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=\min(3^{k},4^{m})</annotation></semantics></math> for some integers <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p4.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p4.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider any element <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p4.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in A+B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in A+B</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p4.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x&lt;M\cdot N_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x&lt;M\cdot N_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. By definition, <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p4.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=a+b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=a+b</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p4.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p4.10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in B</annotation></semantics></math>. Using the previously established decompositions, we can express this sum as <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p4.11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=3^{k}a_{top}+a_{bot}+4^{m}b_{top}+b_{bot}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mn>4</mn><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=3^{k}a_{top}+a_{bot}+4^{m}b_{top}+b_{bot}</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume without loss of generality that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p4.12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3^{k}\leq 4^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3^{k}\leq 4^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p4.13.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=3^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=3^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. We can rewrite this expression to factor out <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p4.14.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p4.15.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=3^{k}(a_{top}+b_{top})+c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=3^{k}(a_{top}+b_{top})+c</annotation></semantics></math>, where the remainder term is <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p4.16.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=(4^{m}-3^{k})b_{top}+a_{bot}+b_{bot}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>4</mn><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=(4^{m}-3^{k})b_{top}+a_{bot}+b_{bot}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p5.10" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p5.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=a_{top}+b_{top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=a_{top}+b_{top}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p5.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{top}\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{top}\in A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p5.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{top}\in B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{top}\in B</annotation></semantics></math>, it naturally follows that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p5.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in A+B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in A+B</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, because <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p5.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x&lt;3^{k}N_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x&lt;3^{k}N_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, we must have <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p5.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y&lt;N_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y&lt;N_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, which in turn dictates that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p5.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{top}\leq N_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{top}\leq N_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Applying our bounds for the bottom parts, we can bound the remainder <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p5.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> by a maximum value <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p5.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>, defined as <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p5.10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=|4^{m}-3^{k}|N_{0}+(3^{k}-1)/2+(4^{m}-1)/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mn>4</mn><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>4</mn><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=|4^{m}-3^{k}|N_{0}+(3^{k}-1)/2+(4^{m}-1)/3</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p6.11" class="ltx_p">This shows that any valid sum <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p6.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x&lt;M\cdot N_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x&lt;M\cdot N_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is uniquely determined by choosing a base value <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p6.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in(A+B)\cap[0,N_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in(A+B)\cap[0,N_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> and a remainder <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p6.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in[0,C]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in[0,C]</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the total number of elements in <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p6.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A+B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A+B</annotation></semantics></math> strictly less than <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p6.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\cdot N_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\cdot N_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded by the product of the number of choices for <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p6.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> and the number of choices for <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p6.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>. Dividing by the interval length <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p6.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\cdot N_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\cdot N_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> yields an upper bound on the density at this new scale: the density up to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p6.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\cdot N_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\cdot N_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is less than or equal to the density up to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p6.10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> multiplied by the factor <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p6.11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(C+1)/M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(C+1)/M</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p7.12" class="ltx_p">To force the density to drop, we require this multiplying factor to be strictly less than 1. Because the ratio of logarithms <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p7.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ln(4)/\ln(3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ln(4)/\ln(3)</annotation></semantics></math> is irrational, Dirichlet’s Approximation Theorem guarantees that we can find arbitrarily large integers <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p7.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p7.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> such that the ratio <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p7.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4^{m}/3^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mn>4</mn><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>/</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4^{m}/3^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is arbitrarily close to 1. By choosing <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p7.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p7.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> carefully, the absolute difference <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p7.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|4^{m}-3^{k}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mn>4</mn><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|4^{m}-3^{k}|</annotation></semantics></math> becomes extremely small relative to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p7.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, for any given <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p7.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can select <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p7.10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p7.11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> large enough such that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p7.12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(C+1)/M\leq 0.99" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0.99</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(C+1)/M\leq 0.99</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p8.13" class="ltx_p">We can now apply this bounding process iteratively. Starting from an arbitrary scale <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p8.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can find a larger scale <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p8.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{1}=M_{1}N_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{1}=M_{1}N_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> where the density of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p8.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A+B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A+B</annotation></semantics></math> drops by a factor of at least <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p8.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.99" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.99</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.99</annotation></semantics></math>. Taking <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p8.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> as our new baseline, we find a still larger scale <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p8.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{2}=M_{2}N_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{2}=M_{2}N_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> where the density drops by another factor of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p8.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.99" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.99</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.99</annotation></semantics></math>. After <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p8.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> iterations, the density of the set up to the scale <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p8.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded by <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p8.10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0.99)^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.99</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>r</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0.99)^{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. As <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p8.11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, this bound approaches 0. This demonstrates the existence of a sequence of arbitrarily large scales where the density tends to 0, proving that the lower density of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p8.12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A+B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A+B</annotation></semantics></math> is 0.  <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p8.13.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Box" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Box</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p9.1" class="ltx_p">We originally communicated the result in <a href="https://www.erdosproblems.com/forum/thread/125#post-5110" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://www.erdosproblems.com/forum/thread/125#post-5110</a>. The Lean proof is at <a href="https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/main/APNOutputs/ErdosProblems/erdos_125.variants.positive_lower_density.lean" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/main/APNOutputs/ErdosProblems/erdos_125.variants.positive_lower_density.lean</a>. In the discussion at the ErdosProblems site, it was pointed out that this leaves two possibilities regarding the set <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx3.p9.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A+B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A+B</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<ol id="A2.I5" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span>
<div id="A2.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I5.i1.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A+B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A+B</annotation></semantics></math> has zero upper and lower density (and hence also zero density), or</p>
</div>
</li>
<li id="A2.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span>
<div id="A2.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I5.i2.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A+B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A+B</annotation></semantics></math> has zero lower density, but positive upper density (and hence no density).</p>
</div>
</li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSSx4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Erdős #138, Differences Variant</h4>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Question.</span> Let the van der Waerden number <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W(k)</annotation></semantics></math>
be such that whenever <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq W(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq W(k)</annotation></semantics></math>
and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1,\ldots,N\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1,\ldots,N\}</annotation></semantics></math>
is 2-coloured there must exist a monochromatic <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p1.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-term arithmetic progression. Is it true that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p1.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W(k+1)-W(k)\rightarrow\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W(k+1)-W(k)\rightarrow\infty</annotation></semantics></math>?</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p2.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof.</span> We will show that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p2.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W(k+1)\geq W(k)+k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W(k+1)\geq W(k)+k</annotation></semantics></math>, which establishes that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p2.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W(k+1)-W(k)\rightarrow\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W(k+1)-W(k)\rightarrow\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Given a 2-coloring of the first <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p2.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W(k)-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W(k)-1</annotation></semantics></math> integers without a monochromatic <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p2.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-AP, we can extend it by <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p2.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> further elements without creating a monochromatic <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p2.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k+1)</annotation></semantics></math>-AP by proceeding greedily. Adding new elements one by one, suppose we have validly colored up to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p2.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> (where <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p2.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M&lt;W(k)-1+k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M&lt;W(k)-1+k</annotation></semantics></math>); we simply color <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p2.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M+1</annotation></semantics></math> red if doing so doesn’t create a red <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p2.10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k+1)</annotation></semantics></math>-AP, and blue otherwise.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p3.13" class="ltx_p">The only way this algorithm could result in an invalid coloring is if both choices are blocked, meaning there is already a red <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p3.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-AP with some step size <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p3.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and a blue <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p3.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-AP with some step size <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p3.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{B}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p3.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k+1)</annotation></semantics></math>-th element for both progressions lands exactly on <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p3.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M+1</annotation></semantics></math>. But this is impossible. Because our original interval up to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p3.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W(k)-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W(k)-1</annotation></semantics></math> has no monochromatic <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p3.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-APs, these progressions must contain at least one newly added element, which bounds their step sizes to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p3.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{R},d_{B}\leq k-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{R},d_{B}\leq k-1</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, if we step backward <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p3.10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{B}</annotation></semantics></math> times along the red progression and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p3.11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> times along the blue progression, both calculations land exactly on the positive integer <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p3.12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M+1-d_{R}d_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M+1-d_{R}d_{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, meaning this single point would have to be simultaneously colored red and blue, which is a contradiction.  <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p3.13.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Box" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Box</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p4.3" class="ltx_p">We originally communicated the result in <a href="https://www.erdosproblems.com/forum/thread/138#post-5314" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://www.erdosproblems.com/forum/thread/138#post-5314</a>, and share the Lean proof at <a href="https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/main/APNOutputs/ErdosProblems/erdos_138.variants.difference.lean" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/main/APNOutputs/ErdosProblems/erdos_138.variants.difference.lean</a>. In the discussion at the ErdosProblems site, Thomas Bloom pointed out that the obvious generalization of this argument gives <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p4.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W(k+1,l+1)\geq W(k,l)+\textrm{min}(k,l)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext>min</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W(k+1,l+1)\geq W(k,l)+\textrm{min}(k,l)</annotation></semantics></math>, and asked what this kind of argument can prove for the <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p4.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>-color variant <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx4.p4.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{r}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{r}(k)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSSx5" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Erdős #741-(i)</h4>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Question.</span> Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\subseteq\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\subseteq\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> be such that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A+A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A+A</annotation></semantics></math> has positive upper density. Can one always decompose <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=A_{1}\sqcup A_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⊔</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=A_{1}\sqcup A_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p1.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1}+A_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1}+A_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p1.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{2}+A_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{2}+A_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> both have positive upper density?</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof.</span> We show that the answer is yes. We use an alternating block partition. Given a rapidly growing sequence <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{0}&lt;M_{1}&lt;M_{2}&lt;\cdots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{0}&lt;M_{1}&lt;M_{2}&lt;\cdots</annotation></semantics></math>, we define</p>
<table id="A2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1}=A\cap\bigcup_{k}(M_{2k},M_{2k+1}],\qquad A_{2}=A\setminus A_{1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">∩</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">⋃</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1}=A\cap\bigcup_{k}(M_{2k},M_{2k+1}],\qquad A_{2}=A\setminus A_{1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.12" class="ltx_p">In odd-indexed intervals <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(M_{2k},M_{2k+1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(M_{2k},M_{2k+1}]</annotation></semantics></math>, all elements of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> belong to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>; in even-indexed intervals <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(M_{2k+1},M_{2k+2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(M_{2k+1},M_{2k+2}]</annotation></semantics></math>, they all belong to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. The sequence <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> is chosen to grow fast enough that each block dwarfs all previous ones. We split into two cases.

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case 1: <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.8.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> has positive upper density.</span>
There exist a constant <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and a strictly increasing sequence of scales along which <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A\cap[1,N]|\geq c\cdot N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A\cap[1,N]|\geq c\cdot N</annotation></semantics></math>. Using a dependent-choice argument, we extract a rapidly growing sequence <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> such that for each <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.12.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<ul id="A2.I6" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span>
<div id="A2.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I6.i1.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A\cap[1,M_{k+1}]|\geq c\cdot M_{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A\cap[1,M_{k+1}]|\geq c\cdot M_{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math> (density is retained at the next scale),</p>
</div>
</li>
<li id="A2.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span>
<div id="A2.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I6.i2.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A\cap[1,M_{k}]|\leq\frac{c}{4}\cdot M_{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A\cap[1,M_{k}]|\leq\frac{c}{4}\cdot M_{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math> (the “past” is negligible relative to the “future”).</p>
</div>
</li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.30" class="ltx_p">Because each new block contains all the “fresh” elements of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, looking at scale <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{2k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{2k+1}</annotation></semantics></math> shows that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> has positive upper density, and looking at scale <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{2k+2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{2k+2}</annotation></semantics></math> shows the same for <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.17.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. A short argument then lifts this: if a set has positive upper density, so does its sumset with itself.

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.19.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case 2: <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.18.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> has zero upper density but <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.19.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A+A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A+A</annotation></semantics></math> has positive upper density.</span>
This is the harder case, since <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.20.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is too sparse to guarantee positive density for the parts directly. Instead, we argue about the sumsets themselves. Since <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.21.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A+A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A+A</annotation></semantics></math> has positive upper density, there exist <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.22.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and a sequence of scales along which <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.23.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|(A+A)\cap[1,N]|\geq c\cdot N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|(A+A)\cap[1,N]|\geq c\cdot N</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.24.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> has zero upper density, <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.25.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A\cap[1,N]|=o(N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A\cap[1,N]|=o(N)</annotation></semantics></math>, so for any fixed <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.26.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> there are arbitrarily large <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.27.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.28.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(K+1)\cdot|A\cap[1,N]|\leq\frac{c}{4}\cdot N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(K+1)\cdot|A\cap[1,N]|\leq\frac{c}{4}\cdot N</annotation></semantics></math>. By dependent choice, we extract a rapidly growing <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.29.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> such that for each <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.30.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<ul id="A2.I7" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I7.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span>
<div id="A2.I7.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I7.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I7.i1.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|(A+A)\cap[1,M_{k+1}]|\geq c\cdot M_{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|(A+A)\cap[1,M_{k+1}]|\geq c\cdot M_{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div>
</li>
<li id="A2.I7.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span>
<div id="A2.I7.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I7.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I7.i2.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(M_{k}+1)\cdot|A\cap[1,M_{k+1}]|\leq\frac{c}{4}\cdot M_{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(M_{k}+1)\cdot|A\cap[1,M_{k+1}]|\leq\frac{c}{4}\cdot M_{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.34" class="ltx_p">The key ingredient is a combinatorial sumset bound: if <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=A_{1}\cup A_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=A_{1}\cup A_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and every element of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.33.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[1,N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[1,N]</annotation></semantics></math> is at most <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.34.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="A2.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|(A+A)\cap[1,N]|\leq|(A_{1}+A_{1})\cap[1,N]|+(K+1)\cdot|A\cap[1,N]|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|(A+A)\cap[1,N]|\leq|(A_{1}+A_{1})\cap[1,N]|+(K+1)\cdot|A\cap[1,N]|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.37" class="ltx_p">The idea is that any sum involving an element of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> has one summand bounded by <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, giving at most <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.37.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(K+1)\cdot|A\cap[1,N]|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(K+1)\cdot|A\cap[1,N]|</annotation></semantics></math> such sums. Applying this bound at alternating scales:</p>
<ul id="A2.I8" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I8.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span>
<div id="A2.I8.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I8.i1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">At scale <math id="A2.I8.i1.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=M_{2k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=M_{2k+1}</annotation></semantics></math>: all elements of <math id="A2.I8.i1.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A2.I8.i1.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[1,N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[1,N]</annotation></semantics></math> lie below <math id="A2.I8.i1.p1.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{2k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{2k}</annotation></semantics></math>, so the bound with <math id="A2.I8.i1.p1.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=M_{2k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=M_{2k}</annotation></semantics></math> gives <math id="A2.I8.i1.p1.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|(A_{1}+A_{1})\cap[1,N]|\geq\frac{3c}{4}\cdot N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|(A_{1}+A_{1})\cap[1,N]|\geq\frac{3c}{4}\cdot N</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</li>
<li id="A2.I8.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span>
<div id="A2.I8.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I8.i2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">At scale <math id="A2.I8.i2.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=M_{2k+2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=M_{2k+2}</annotation></semantics></math>: symmetrically, all elements of <math id="A2.I8.i2.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A2.I8.i2.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[1,N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[1,N]</annotation></semantics></math> lie below <math id="A2.I8.i2.p1.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{2k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{2k+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, giving <math id="A2.I8.i2.p1.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|(A_{2}+A_{2})\cap[1,N]|\geq\frac{3c}{4}\cdot N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|(A_{2}+A_{2})\cap[1,N]|\geq\frac{3c}{4}\cdot N</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.39" class="ltx_p">Since these bounds hold for infinitely many <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, both sumsets have positive upper density.  <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p2.39.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Box" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Box</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The agent also initially disproved a strict “natural density” formulation of this problem (where the density must exist as a limit), which served as a diagnostic for the correct interpretation of Erdős’ original phrasing. Following Thomas Bloom’s observation that Erdős likely meant “positive upper density,” the formulation was amended and the agent resolved the corrected version as described above. The Lean proof for the upper density variant is available at <a href="https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/main/APNOutputs/ErdosProblems/erdos_741.parts.i.lean" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/main/APNOutputs/ErdosProblems/erdos_741.parts.i.lean</a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSSx6" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Erdős #741-(ii)</h4>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Question.</span> Is there a basis <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> of order <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> such that if <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=A_{1}\sqcup A_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⊔</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=A_{1}\sqcup A_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p1.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1}+A_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1}+A_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p1.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{2}+A_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{2}+A_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> cannot both have bounded gaps?</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.15" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof.</span> We show that the answer is yes by constructing a pathological basis <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> with “forbidden zones” that force any partition to create arbitrarily large gaps in at least one component sumset.

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 1: The construction.</span>
Choose a sequence of rapidly growing scales <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{k}=100^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>100</mn><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{k}=100^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. For each <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, define a forbidden zone <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is a broad interval of integers running roughly from <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{11}{2}P_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>11</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{11}{2}P_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11P_{k}+k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11P_{k}+k</annotation></semantics></math>. In the middle of this zone, we leave a single “oasis” — an isolated element <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{k}=10P_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{k}=10P_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. The set <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> consists of all natural numbers that avoid every forbidden zone, together with the oases <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. In visual terms, <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is made of clumps of consecutive integers separated by large empty gaps, each containing a single survivor <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 2: <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.12.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\cup\{0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\cup\{0\}</annotation></semantics></math> is a basis of order 2.</span>
We must show every natural number <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.13.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.14.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a+b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a+b</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.15.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b\in A\cup\{0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b\in A\cup\{0\}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<ul id="A2.I9" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I9.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span>
<div id="A2.I9.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I9.i1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A2.I9.i1.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\notin Z_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\notin Z_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A2.I9.i1.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A2.I9.i1.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in A</annotation></semantics></math> and we use <math id="A2.I9.i1.p1.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n+0=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n+0=n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</li>
<li id="A2.I9.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span>
<div id="A2.I9.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I9.i2.p1.7" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A2.I9.i2.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in Z_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in Z_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I9.i2.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> lies in the lower half of <math id="A2.I9.i2.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, we use <math id="A2.I9.i2.p1.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lfloor n/2\rfloor+\lceil n/2\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lfloor n/2\rfloor+\lceil n/2\rceil</annotation></semantics></math>. Because <math id="A2.I9.i2.p1.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is small enough, neither half lands in <math id="A2.I9.i2.p1.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, and both are large enough to avoid the previous zone <math id="A2.I9.i2.p1.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</li>
<li id="A2.I9.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span>
<div id="A2.I9.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I9.i3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A2.I9.i3.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in Z_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in Z_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I9.i3.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> lies in the upper half, we use the oasis: <math id="A2.I9.i3.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=x_{k}+(n-x_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=x_{k}+(n-x_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>. The difference <math id="A2.I9.i3.p1.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-x_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-x_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is small enough that it falls safely before the forbidden zone <math id="A2.I9.i3.p1.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.36" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.36.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 3: No syndetic partition exists.</span>
Suppose <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=A_{1}\sqcup A_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⊔</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=A_{1}\sqcup A_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider a target sum <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in[11P_{k},11P_{k}+k]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in[11P_{k},11P_{k}+k]</annotation></semantics></math>. To write <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=u+v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=u+v</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.19.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u,v\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,v\in A</annotation></semantics></math>, the algebra forces the larger operand <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.20.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> to land inside the forbidden range <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.21.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\frac{11}{2}P_{k},11P_{k}+k]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>11</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\frac{11}{2}P_{k},11P_{k}+k]</annotation></semantics></math>. But the only element of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.22.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> in this range is <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.23.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, representing any sum in <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.24.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[11P_{k},11P_{k}+k]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[11P_{k},11P_{k}+k]</annotation></semantics></math> requires <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.25.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">By the pigeonhole principle, <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.26.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> belongs to exactly one partition component, say <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.27.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.28.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1}+A_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1}+A_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> can cover the interval <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.29.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[11P_{k},11P_{k}+k]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[11P_{k},11P_{k}+k]</annotation></semantics></math> using <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.30.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, but <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.31.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{2}+A_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{2}+A_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is completely locked out — it cannot represent any element in that interval. This leaves a gap of length <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.32.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.33.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{2}+A_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{2}+A_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.34.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> can be made arbitrarily large, the gaps in one component’s sumset are unbounded, proving it is impossible to partition <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.35.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> so that both sumsets have bounded gaps.  <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p2.36.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Box" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Box</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx6.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The Lean proof for part (ii) is available at <a href="https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/main/APNOutputs/ErdosProblems/erdos_12.parts.ii.lean" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/main/APNOutputs/ErdosProblems/erdos_12.parts.ii.lean</a>. Our original communication of both results can be found in the problem thread on the ErdosProblems site (<a href="https://www.erdosproblems.com/forum/thread/741" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://www.erdosproblems.com/forum/thread/741</a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSSx7" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Erdős #26, More General Variant</h4>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p1.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p1.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem.</span> Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the set of multiples of a subset <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subseteq\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subseteq\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{d}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{d}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the upper asymptotic density of a set <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p1.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>. There exists a sequence <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p1.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A:\mathbb{N}\to\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A:\mathbb{N}\to\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p1.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i\in\mathbb{N}}1/A(i)=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i\in\mathbb{N}}1/A(i)=\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, such that for <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p1.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=1/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=1/4</annotation></semantics></math> and for all <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p1.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p1.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{d}(\mathcal{M}(A+k))&lt;1-\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{d}(\mathcal{M}(A+k))&lt;1-\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof.</span> We construct the sequence iteratively in finite blocks and show that for any arbitrary shift <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, we can bound the upper density of the shifted sequence by analyzing three distinct cases, the third case relying on the construction being similar to the simple counterexample of Ruzsa which resolved the original question Erdős #26.

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q_{j})_{j=1}^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q_{j})_{j=1}^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> be a strictly increasing sequence of primes satisfying <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{1}\geq 29" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>29</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{1}\geq 29</annotation></semantics></math> (chosen large enough to cause small enough density in the infinite tail of the sequence). We define a strictly increasing sequence of indices (or “jumps”) <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(J_{m})_{m=0}^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(J_{m})_{m=0}^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> recursively, starting with <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> has been defined, and the sequence <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(i)</annotation></semantics></math> has been constructed for all <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&lt;J_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&lt;J_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. We define the parameters for the <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>-th block as follows.

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">First, define the step size <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{m}=\prod_{j=1}^{10J_{m}}q_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{m}=\prod_{j=1}^{10J_{m}}q_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Next, by the Chinese Remainder Theorem, we can choose a base size <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying the following system of congruences</p>
<table id="A2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{m}\equiv-j\pmod{q_{j}}\quad\text{for }1\leq j\leq 10J_{m}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{m}\equiv-j\pmod{q_{j}}\quad\text{for }1\leq j\leq 10J_{m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.18" class="ltx_p">as well as the strict monotonicity condition <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{m}&gt;A(J_{m}-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{m}&gt;A(J_{m}-1)</annotation></semantics></math> (where we set <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(-1)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(-1)=0</annotation></semantics></math>), by adding enough multiples of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>.

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">With <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> fixed, the series <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.17.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{x=1}^{\infty}\frac{1}{R_{m}+xP_{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{x=1}^{\infty}\frac{1}{R_{m}+xP_{m}}</annotation></semantics></math> diverges. Thus, we can compute a block length <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.18.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{m}\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{m}\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> such that the partial sum satisfies:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1\leq\sum_{x=1}^{L_{m}}\frac{1}{R_{m}+xP_{m}}\leq 0.2" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></munderover><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1\leq\sum_{x=1}^{L_{m}}\frac{1}{R_{m}+xP_{m}}\leq 0.2</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.20" class="ltx_p">We then set <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{m+1}=J_{m}+L_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{m+1}=J_{m}+L_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. Now that the bounds of the block are properly defined, for indices <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[J_{m},J_{m+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[J_{m},J_{m+1})</annotation></semantics></math>, we set:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(i)=R_{m}+(i-J_{m}+1)P_{m}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(i)=R_{m}+(i-J_{m}+1)P_{m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.26" class="ltx_p">Since each block contributes at least <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1</annotation></semantics></math> to the total harmonic sum, the overall sum <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum 1/A(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum 1/A(i)</annotation></semantics></math> diverges. Pick an arbitrary shift <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.23.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>; we must now show that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.24.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{d}(\mathcal{M}(A+k))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{d}(\mathcal{M}(A+k))</annotation></semantics></math> stays bounded below <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.25.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3/4</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.26.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> be the unique integer satisfying:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10J_{m_{0}}\leq k&lt;10J_{m_{0}+1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10J_{m_{0}}\leq k&lt;10J_{m_{0}+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.27" class="ltx_p">We partition the shifted sequence <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A+k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A+k</annotation></semantics></math> into three regimes and bound the upper density of the multiples generated by each:</p>
<ul id="A2.I10" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I10.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span>
<div id="A2.I10.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I10.i1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">(Case 1: <math id="A2.I10.i1.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&lt;J_{m_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&lt;J_{m_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>) The upper density of the multiples generated by this finite set is bounded by the sum of their reciprocals. Because <math id="A2.I10.i1.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(i)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(i)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A2.I10.i1.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(i)+k&gt;k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(i)+k&gt;k</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{d}(\mathcal{M}(\{A(i)+k\mid i&lt;J_{m_{0}}\}))\leq\sum_{i=0}^{J_{m_{0}}-1}\frac{1}{A(i)+k}&lt;\sum_{i=0}^{J_{m_{0}}-1}\frac{1}{k}=\frac{J_{m_{0}}}{k}\leq 0.1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">&lt;</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>J</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{d}(\mathcal{M}(\{A(i)+k\mid i&lt;J_{m_{0}}\}))\leq\sum_{i=0}^{J_{m_{0}}-1}\frac{1}{A(i)+k}&lt;\sum_{i=0}^{J_{m_{0}}-1}\frac{1}{k}=\frac{J_{m_{0}}}{k}\leq 0.1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</li>
<li id="A2.I10.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span>
<div id="A2.I10.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I10.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">(Case 2: <math id="A2.I10.i2.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{m_{0}}\leq i&lt;J_{m_{0}+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{m_{0}}\leq i&lt;J_{m_{0}+1}</annotation></semantics></math>) Shifting by a positive <math id="A2.I10.i2.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> strictly decreases the reciprocals, so the upper density of the multiples from this critical block satisfies:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{d}(\mathcal{M}(\{A(i)+k\mid J_{m_{0}}\leq i&lt;J_{m_{0}+1}\}))\leq\sum_{i=J_{m_{0}}}^{J_{m_{0}+1}-1}\frac{1}{A(i)+k}&lt;\sum_{i=J_{m_{0}}}^{J_{m_{0}+1}-1}\frac{1}{A(i)}\leq 0.2" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">&lt;</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{d}(\mathcal{M}(\{A(i)+k\mid J_{m_{0}}\leq i&lt;J_{m_{0}+1}\}))\leq\sum_{i=J_{m_{0}}}^{J_{m_{0}+1}-1}\frac{1}{A(i)+k}&lt;\sum_{i=J_{m_{0}}}^{J_{m_{0}+1}-1}\frac{1}{A(i)}\leq 0.2</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</li>
<li id="A2.I10.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span>
<div id="A2.I10.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I10.i3.p1.6" class="ltx_p">(Case 3: <math id="A2.I10.i3.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq J_{m_{0}+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq J_{m_{0}+1}</annotation></semantics></math>) Consider any element <math id="A2.I10.i3.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(i)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A2.I10.i3.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> belongs to some block <math id="A2.I10.i3.p1.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq m_{0}+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq m_{0}+1</annotation></semantics></math>, meaning <math id="A2.I10.i3.p1.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10J_{m}\geq 10J_{m_{0}+1}&gt;k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10J_{m}\geq 10J_{m_{0}+1}&gt;k</annotation></semantics></math>. Recall the construction of the <math id="A2.I10.i3.p1.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>-th block:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(i)+k=(R_{m}+k)+(i-J_{m}+1)P_{m}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(i)+k=(R_{m}+k)+(i-J_{m}+1)P_{m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I10.i3.p1.11" class="ltx_p">Because <math id="A2.I10.i3.p1.7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10J_{m}\geq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10J_{m}\geq k</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A2.I10.i3.p1.8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{k}\mid P_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∣</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{k}\mid P_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. By construction, we also have <math id="A2.I10.i3.p1.9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{k}\mid(R_{m}+k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∣</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{k}\mid(R_{m}+k)</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, <math id="A2.I10.i3.p1.10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{k}\mid(A(i)+k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∣</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{k}\mid(A(i)+k)</annotation></semantics></math> for every element in this infinite tail. The set of multiples generated by Case 3 is therefore entirely contained within the multiples of the prime <math id="A2.I10.i3.p1.11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Expressing this with the upper density notation:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{d}(\mathcal{M}(\{A(i)+k\mid i\geq J_{m_{0}+1}\}))\leq\overline{d}(\mathcal{M}(\{q_{k}\}))=\frac{1}{q_{k}}\leq\frac{1}{29}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>29</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{d}(\mathcal{M}(\{A(i)+k\mid i\geq J_{m_{0}+1}\}))\leq\overline{d}(\mathcal{M}(\{q_{k}\}))=\frac{1}{q_{k}}\leq\frac{1}{29}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.28" class="ltx_p">By the union bound, the total upper density of the multiples of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A+k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A+k</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded above by:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1+0.2+\frac{1}{29}\approx 0.334&lt;\frac{3}{4}=1-\epsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0.2</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>29</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.334</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1+0.2+\frac{1}{29}\approx 0.334&lt;\frac{3}{4}=1-\epsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.29" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p2.29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Box" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Box</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p3.6" class="ltx_p">This problem is a more general variant to the original question stating that “For all <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p3.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\subseteq\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\subseteq\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, does there exist <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p3.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> such that almost all integers have a divisor of the form <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p3.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a+k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a+k</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p3.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in A</annotation></semantics></math>?”. A simple counterexample to this question can be produced using the Chinese Remainder Theorem. In the more general variant we resolve, note the Chinese Remainder Theorem is still used to construct a counterexample, but with additional constraints to make the upper density of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p3.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A+k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A+k</annotation></semantics></math> small, for all <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx7.p3.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. We originally communicated the result in <a href="https://www.erdosproblems.com/forum/thread/26" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://www.erdosproblems.com/forum/thread/26</a>, and share the Lean proof at <a href="https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/main/APNOutputs/ErdosProblems/erdos_26.variants.tenenbaum.lean" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/main/APNOutputs/ErdosProblems/erdos_26.variants.tenenbaum.lean</a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSSx8" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Erdős #846</h4>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem</span>. Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\subset\mathbb{R}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\subset\mathbb{R}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>
be an infinite set for which there exists some <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>
such that in any subset of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>
of size <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p1.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>
there are always at least <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p1.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon n</annotation></semantics></math>
with no three on a line.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Is it true that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p2.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>
is the union of a finite number of sets where no three are on a line?</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof.</span> We will show that there exists an infinite set <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p3.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\subset\mathbb{R}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\subset\mathbb{R}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> for which any <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p3.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-element subset contains at least <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p3.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n/2</annotation></semantics></math> points with no three on a line, but <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p3.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is not the union of a finite number of sets where no three are on a line.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p4.4" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p4.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> be the countably infinite complete graph with vertex set <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p4.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=\{x_{1},x_{2},\dots\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=\{x_{1},x_{2},\dots\}</annotation></semantics></math>. We choose the sequence of real numbers <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p4.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{i})_{i=1}^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{i})_{i=1}^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> such that it grows sufficiently fast to avoid any accidental roots of polynomials that will arise in our collinearity condition, by setting <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p4.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{n}=100^{4^{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>100</mn><msup><mn>4</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{n}=100^{4^{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p5.4" class="ltx_p">We construct our point set <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p5.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\subset\mathbb{R}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\subset\mathbb{R}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> by mapping each edge <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p5.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e=\{x_{i},x_{j}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e=\{x_{i},x_{j}\}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p5.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> to a point <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p5.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{e}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</p>
<table id="A2.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{e}=(x_{i}+x_{j},x_{i}^{2}+x_{i}x_{j}+x_{j}^{2})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{e}=(x_{i}+x_{j},x_{i}^{2}+x_{i}x_{j}+x_{j}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p5.5" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p5.5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\{P_{e}\mid e\in E(K_{\infty})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\{P_{e}\mid e\in E(K_{\infty})\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma.</span>
Three points in <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p6.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> are collinear if and only if their corresponding edges form a triangle in <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p6.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Lemma.</span> First, assume three edges form a triangle in <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p7.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> with vertices <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p7.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b,c\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b,c\in V</annotation></semantics></math>. The corresponding points in <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p7.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> are:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{ab}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{ab}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(a+b,a^{2}+ab+b^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(a+b,a^{2}+ab+b^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{bc}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{bc}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(b+c,b^{2}+bc+c^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(b+c,b^{2}+bc+c^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{ca}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{ca}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(c+a,c^{2}+ca+a^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(c+a,c^{2}+ca+a^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p7.6" class="ltx_p">The slope <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p7.4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> of the line connecting <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p7.5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{ab}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{ab}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p7.6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{bc}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{bc}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=\frac{(b^{2}+bc+c^{2})-(a^{2}+ab+b^{2})}{(b+c)-(a+b)}=\frac{c^{2}-a^{2}+bc-ab}{c-a}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=\frac{(b^{2}+bc+c^{2})-(a^{2}+ab+b^{2})}{(b+c)-(a+b)}=\frac{c^{2}-a^{2}+bc-ab}{c-a}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p7.10" class="ltx_p">Factoring the numerator yields:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=\frac{(c-a)(c+a)+b(c-a)}{c-a}=a+b+c" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=\frac{(c-a)(c+a)+b(c-a)}{c-a}=a+b+c</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p7.9" class="ltx_p">By symmetry, the slope of the line connecting <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p7.7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{bc}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{bc}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p7.8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{ca}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{ca}</annotation></semantics></math> is also <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p7.9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a+b+c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a+b+c</annotation></semantics></math>. Because the slopes are equal, the three points are collinear.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Conversely, suppose three distinct edges do not form a triangle. We must show their corresponding points are not collinear. The condition that these points are collinear is equivalent to the determinant of their <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p8.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\times 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times 3</annotation></semantics></math> augmented coordinate matrix evaluating to zero.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p9.2" class="ltx_p">Because the sequence <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p9.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{i})_{i=1}^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{i})_{i=1}^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> grows quickly enough, any polynomial evaluated on its terms is strictly dominated by the highest power of its largest variable. By sorting the endpoints of the three edges, we can group the expanded determinant into three topological cases based on whether the largest vertex is present in one, two, or all three of the edges. In every case, because the edges are distinct and do not form a triangle, the coefficient of the dominant highest-degree term is bounded strictly away from zero. Furthermore, the massive gap between consecutive terms in the sequence ensures that the lower-degree terms are strictly bounded and cannot sum to cancel the leading term out. Therefore, the determinant never evaluates to zero, and no accidental collinearities occur. <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p9.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Box" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Box</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma.</span>
Any <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p10.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-element subset of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p10.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> contains at least <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p10.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n/2</annotation></semantics></math> points with no three on a line.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p11.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p11.13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Lemma.</span>
Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p11.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subset A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subset A</annotation></semantics></math> be an arbitrary subset of size <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p11.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>. The elements of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p11.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> correspond to a subgraph <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p11.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{S}\subset K_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{S}\subset K_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> containing exactly <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p11.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> edges. Every graph with <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p11.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> edges contains a bipartite subgraph <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p11.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> with at least <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p11.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n/2</annotation></semantics></math> edges. Because <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p11.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> is bipartite, it contains no odd cycles and is therefore triangle-free. By the previous lemma, the corresponding points in <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p11.10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> contain no collinear triplets. This provides a subset of at least <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p11.11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lceil n/2\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lceil n/2\rceil</annotation></semantics></math> points with no three on a line, satisfying the condition with <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p11.12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=1/2</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p11.13.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Box" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Box</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p12.2" class="ltx_p">To complete the proof of the theorem, assume for contradiction that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p12.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> can be covered by a finite number of sets where no three are on a line; that is, <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p12.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\bigcup_{k=1}^{r}A_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\bigcup_{k=1}^{r}A_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p13.5" class="ltx_p">This partition naturally induces an <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p13.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>-coloring on the edges of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p13.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>. By the infinite Ramsey Theorem, any finite coloring of the edges of the infinite complete graph must contain a monochromatic triangle. Consequently, there exists some color class <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p13.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> containing three edges that form a triangle. By the lemma, these three edges map to three collinear points in <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p13.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. This contradicts the assumption that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p13.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> contains no three collinear points.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p14.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore, <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p14.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> cannot be covered by finitely many sets with no three on a line.  <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p14.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Box" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Box</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx8.p15.1" class="ltx_p">We originally communicated the result in <a href="https://www.erdosproblems.com/forum/thread/846#post-4447" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://www.erdosproblems.com/forum/thread/846#post-4447</a> to the
ErdosProblems site, and share the Lean proof at <a href="https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/main/APNOutputs/ErdosProblems/erdos_846.lean" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/main/APNOutputs/ErdosProblems/erdos_846.lean</a>. This result was independently discovered by an internal model at OpenAI <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">putterman2026infinite</span>]</cite>. In the discussion at the ErdosProblems site, it was pointed out that this result also follows from a projection argument of Reiher, Rödl and Sales <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">reiher2024colouring</span>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSSx9" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Erdős #152</h4>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p1.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p1.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem.</span> For a Sidon set <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\subset\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\subset\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> of size <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(A+A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(A+A)</annotation></semantics></math> count the isolated elements of the sumset — those <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p1.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in A+A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in A+A</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p1.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\pm 1\notin A+A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\pm 1\notin A+A</annotation></semantics></math>. Define <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p1.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(n)</annotation></semantics></math> as the minimum of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p1.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(A+A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(A+A)</annotation></semantics></math> over all Sidon sets of size <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p1.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p1.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(n)\geq(n^{2}-100n-16)/16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(n)\geq(n^{2}-100n-16)/16</annotation></semantics></math>, so in particular <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p1.10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(n)\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(n)\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof.</span> The proof establishes, for every Sidon set <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p2.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> of size <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p2.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="16\cdot I(A+A)+100n+16\geq n^{2}.\qquad(\star)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>100</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo><mspace style="width:2.167em;" width="2.167em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋆</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16\cdot I(A+A)+100n+16\geq n^{2}.\qquad(\star)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p2.10" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p2.3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=\{a-b:a,b\in A\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=\{a-b:a,b\in A\}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the difference set and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p2.4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=A+A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=A+A</annotation></semantics></math> the sumset. For any set <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p2.5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\subseteq\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\subseteq\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p2.6.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="N_{k}(X):=|{x\in X:x+k\in X}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">:=</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{k}(X):=|{x\in X:x+k\in X}|</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of pairs at distance <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p2.7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p2.8.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="V_{2}(X):=|{x\in X:x\pm 1\in X}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">:=</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{2}(X):=|{x\in X:x\pm 1\in X}|</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of interior points, and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p2.9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(X)</annotation></semantics></math> be the isolated points .

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p2.10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\subset\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\subset\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>. We will employ the following three facts:</p>
<ol id="A2.I11" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I11.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span>
<div id="A2.I11.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I11.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I11.i1.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(X)+2N_{1}(X)=|X|+V_{2}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(X)+2N_{1}(X)=|X|+V_{2}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>, by partitioning elements by neighbor count.</p>
</div>
</li>
<li id="A2.I11.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span>
<div id="A2.I11.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I11.i2.p1.7" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I11.i2.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4N_{1}(X)+N_{3}(X)\leq 3|X|+2N_{2}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4N_{1}(X)+N_{3}(X)\leq 3|X|+2N_{2}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>, which follows from writing <math id="A2.I11.i2.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{k}(x)=\sum_{x\in\mathbb{Z}}1_{X}(x)1_{X}(x+k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mn>1</mn><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>1</mn><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{k}(x)=\sum_{x\in\mathbb{Z}}1_{X}(x)1_{X}(x+k)</annotation></semantics></math> and a pointwise check of the indicator function <math id="A2.I11.i2.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mn>1</mn><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> across all <math id="A2.I11.i2.p1.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math>-point windows <math id="A2.I11.i2.p1.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,x+1,x+2,x+3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,x+1,x+2,x+3)</annotation></semantics></math>; that is, summing the local inequality <math id="A2.I11.i2.p1.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1_{X}(x)+1_{X}(x+1)+1_{X}(x+2)+1_{X}(x)1_{X}(x+2)+1_{X}(x+1)1_{X}(x+3)\geq 1_{X}(x)1_{X}(x+1)+21_{X}(x+1)1_{X}(x+2)+1_{X}(x+2)1_{X}(x+3)+1_{X}(x)1_{X}(x+3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mn>1</mn><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mn>1</mn><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mn>1</mn><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mn>1</mn><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>1</mn><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mn>1</mn><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>1</mn><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mn>1</mn><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>1</mn><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mn>21</mn><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>1</mn><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mn>1</mn><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>1</mn><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mn>1</mn><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>1</mn><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1_{X}(x)+1_{X}(x+1)+1_{X}(x+2)+1_{X}(x)1_{X}(x+2)+1_{X}(x+1)1_{X}(x+3)\geq 1_{X}(x)1_{X}(x+1)+21_{X}(x+1)1_{X}(x+2)+1_{X}(x+2)1_{X}(x+3)+1_{X}(x)1_{X}(x+3)</annotation></semantics></math> and then summing over all <math id="A2.I11.i2.p1.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</li>
<li id="A2.I11.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span>
<div id="A2.I11.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I11.i3.p1.8" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I11.i3.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2N_{2}(X)\leq N_{3}(X)+2V_{2}(X)+2I(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2N_{2}(X)\leq N_{3}(X)+2V_{2}(X)+2I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider each pair <math id="A2.I11.i3.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,x+2)\in X^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,x+2)\in X^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and we proceed by cases on <math id="A2.I11.i3.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x+1</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.I11.i3.p1.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=\{x\in X\mid x+1\notin X\land x+2\in X\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=\{x\in X\mid x+1\notin X\land x+2\in X\}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A2.I11.i3.p1.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x+1\in X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x+1\in X</annotation></semantics></math>, then the pair is counted exactly by <math id="A2.I11.i3.p1.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A2.I11.i3.p1.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{2}(X)=V_{2}(X)+|G|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{2}(X)=V_{2}(X)+|G|</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A2.I11.i3.p1.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x+1\notin X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x+1\notin X</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<ul id="A2.I11.i3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I11.i3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span>
<div id="A2.I11.i3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I11.i3.I1.i1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A2.I11.i3.I1.i1.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x-1\in X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x-1\in X</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A2.I11.i3.I1.i1.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x-1,x+2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x-1,x+2)</annotation></semantics></math> is a pair counted in <math id="A2.I11.i3.I1.i1.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{3}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{3}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</li>
<li id="A2.I11.i3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span>
<div id="A2.I11.i3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I11.i3.I1.i2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A2.I11.i3.I1.i2.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x+3\in X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x+3\in X</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A2.I11.i3.I1.i2.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,x+3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,x+3)</annotation></semantics></math> is a pair counted in <math id="A2.I11.i3.I1.i2.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{3}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{3}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</li>
<li id="A2.I11.i3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span>
<div id="A2.I11.i3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I11.i3.I1.i3.p1.6" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A2.I11.i3.I1.i3.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x-1\notin X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x-1\notin X</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A2.I11.i3.I1.i3.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> is an isolated point in <math id="A2.I11.i3.I1.i3.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>, and if <math id="A2.I11.i3.I1.i3.p1.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x+3\notin X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x+3\notin X</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A2.I11.i3.I1.i3.p1.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x+2</annotation></semantics></math> is an isolated point in <math id="A2.I11.i3.I1.i3.p1.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.I11.i3.p1.10" class="ltx_p">Since each <math id="A2.I11.i3.p1.9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> pair can be counted by two different gaps, while isolated points are distinct in this construction, we have <math id="A2.I11.i3.p1.10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2|G|\leq N_{3}(X)+2I(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2|G|\leq N_{3}(X)+2I(X)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</li>
</ol>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p2.15" class="ltx_p">Next, for each <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p2.11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, count quadruples <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p2.12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a,b,c,d)\in A^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a,b,c,d)\in A^{4}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p2.13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a+b+k=c+d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a+b+k=c+d</annotation></semantics></math>. Rewriting as <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p2.14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a-c=d-b-k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a-c=d-b-k</annotation></semantics></math> and partitioning by <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p2.15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=a-c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=a-c</annotation></semantics></math> yields the following two quadruple transfer bounds:</p>
<ol id="A2.I12" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I12.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span>
<div id="A2.I12.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I12.i1.p1.11" class="ltx_p">The cases <math id="A2.I12.i1.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I12.i1.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=-k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=-k</annotation></semantics></math> each contribute <math id="A2.I12.i1.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq|A|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi></mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq|A|</annotation></semantics></math> (one coordinate determines the rest). For any <math id="A2.I12.i1.p1.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\notin\{0,-k\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\notin\{0,-k\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the Sidon property ensures that there is at most one pair <math id="A2.I12.i1.p1.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a,c)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.I12.i1.p1.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a-c=\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a-c=\delta</annotation></semantics></math> and at most one pair <math id="A2.I12.i1.p1.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d,b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d,b)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.I12.i1.p1.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d-b=\delta+k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d-b=\delta+k</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, each gap of size <math id="A2.I12.i1.p1.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A2.I12.i1.p1.10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> identifies exactly one quadruple. Thus <math id="A2.I12.i1.p1.11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\text{quad}_{k}|\leq N_{k}(D)+2n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mtext>quad</mtext><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\text{quad}_{k}|\leq N_{k}(D)+2n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</li>
<li id="A2.I12.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span>
<div id="A2.I12.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I12.i2.p1.6" class="ltx_p">Each "good" element <math id="A2.I12.i2.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in S</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.I12.i2.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s+k\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s+k\in S</annotation></semantics></math> (excluding <math id="A2.I12.i2.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq 2n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi></mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq 2n</annotation></semantics></math> doubles of the form <math id="A2.I12.i2.p1.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2a</annotation></semantics></math>) produces <math id="A2.I12.i2.p1.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi></mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 4</annotation></semantics></math> quadruples, giving <math id="A2.I12.i2.p1.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4N_{k}(S)\leq|\text{quad}_{k}|+8n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mtext>quad</mtext><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4N_{k}(S)\leq|\text{quad}_{k}|+8n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p3.4" class="ltx_p">Combining these bounds shows that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p3.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{k}(D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{k}(D)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p3.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{k}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{k}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> are related up to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p3.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n)</annotation></semantics></math> error. Applying fact (2) to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p3.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=A-A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=A-A</annotation></semantics></math> gives</p>
<table id="A2.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4N_{1}(D)+N_{3}(D)\leq 3|D|+2N_{2}(D)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4N_{1}(D)+N_{3}(D)\leq 3|D|+2N_{2}(D)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p3.6" class="ltx_p">and then substitute the above two quadruple transfer bounds for <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p3.5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1,2,3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1,2,3</annotation></semantics></math> and collecting all <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p3.6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n)</annotation></semantics></math> terms gives</p>
<table id="A2.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16N_{1}(S)+4N_{3}(S)\leq 3|D|+8N_{2}(S)+100n" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16N_{1}(S)+4N_{3}(S)\leq 3|D|+8N_{2}(S)+100n</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p3.7" class="ltx_p">Then, using fact (3) on <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p3.7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> we obtain</p>
<table id="A2.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16N_{1}(S)+4N_{3}(S)\leq 3|D|+(4N_{3}(S)+8V_{2}(S)+8I(S))+100n" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16N_{1}(S)+4N_{3}(S)\leq 3|D|+(4N_{3}(S)+8V_{2}(S)+8I(S))+100n</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p3.8" class="ltx_p">and notice that the <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p3.8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4N_{3}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4N_{3}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> terms cancel. Then applying fact (1) we obtain</p>
<table id="A2.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(8|S|+8V_{2}(S)-8I(S))\leq 3|D|+8V_{2}(S)+8I(S)+100n" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(8|S|+8V_{2}(S)-8I(S))\leq 3|D|+8V_{2}(S)+8I(S)+100n</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p3.9" class="ltx_p">and see that the <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p3.9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8V_{2}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8V_{2}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> terms now cancel, leaving</p>
<table id="A2.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16I(S)+100n\geq 8|S|-3|D|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16I(S)+100n\geq 8|S|-3|D|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p3.15" class="ltx_p">The standard Sidon estimates <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p3.10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|S|\geq n^{2}/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|S|\geq n^{2}/2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p3.11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|D|\leq n^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|D|\leq n^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> then give <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p3.12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16I(S)+100n\geq 4n^{2}-3n^{2}=n^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16I(S)+100n\geq 4n^{2}-3n^{2}=n^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, accounting for a boundary correction of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p3.13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+16</annotation></semantics></math> at zero yields <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p3.14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\star)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋆</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\star)</annotation></semantics></math>.  <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p3.15.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Box" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Box</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx9.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We include the Lean proof at <a href="https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/main/APNOutputs/ErdosProblems/erdos_152.lean" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/main/APNOutputs/ErdosProblems/erdos_152.lean</a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSSx10" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">OEIS Conjectures</h4>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem. </span> (A conjecture of OEIS A051293, 2002) Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the number of nonempty subsets of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1,2,3,\dots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1,2,3,\dots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math> whose elements have an integer average. Then</p>
<table id="A2.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{n}=\frac{2^{n+1}}{n}\left(1+\frac{1}{n}+\frac{3}{n^{2}}+\frac{13}{n^{3}}+\frac{75}{n^{4}}+\frac{541}{n^{5}}+o\left(\frac{1}{n^{5}}\right)\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>13</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>75</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>541</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{n}=\frac{2^{n+1}}{n}\left(1+\frac{1}{n}+\frac{3}{n^{2}}+\frac{13}{n^{3}}+\frac{75}{n^{4}}+\frac{541}{n^{5}}+o\left(\frac{1}{n^{5}}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.20" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.20.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof.</span> A subset <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subseteq\{1,2,\dots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subseteq\{1,2,\dots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math> has an integer average if and only if the sum of its elements is divisible by its cardinality <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|S|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|S|</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(n,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(n,k)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the number of subsets of size <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> whose sum is divisible by <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. We can express the total number of such subsets as <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{n}=\sum_{k=1}^{n}N(n,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{n}=\sum_{k=1}^{n}N(n,k)</annotation></semantics></math>
To isolate the condition that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> divides the sum of the elements in <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, we utilize the orthogonality of roots of unity. Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{k,j}=\exp\left(\frac{2\pi ij}{k}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{k,j}=\exp\left(\frac{2\pi ij}{k}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. By the standard orthogonality relation, the sum <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.12.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{k}\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}\omega_{k,j}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{k}\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}\omega_{k,j}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> equals <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.13.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.14.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> divides <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.15.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.16.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><mn>0</mn></math> otherwise. Thus, the indicator function for divisibility by <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.17.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.18.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{k}\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}\omega_{k,j}^{\sum_{s\in S}s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub></mstyle><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{k}\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}\omega_{k,j}^{\sum_{s\in S}s}</annotation></semantics></math>. Summing this over all <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.19.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{n}{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{n}{k}</annotation></semantics></math> subsets of size <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.20.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> yields</p>
<table id="A2.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(n,k)=\frac{1}{k}\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}\sum_{|S|=k}\omega_{k,j}^{\sum_{s\in S}s}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub></mstyle><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(n,k)=\frac{1}{k}\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}\sum_{|S|=k}\omega_{k,j}^{\sum_{s\in S}s}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.23" class="ltx_p">We isolate the principal term corresponding to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=0</annotation></semantics></math>, which evaluates trivially to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{k}\binom{n}{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{k}\binom{n}{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let the remainder term be <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.23.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{n,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{n,k}</annotation></semantics></math>, defined as</p>
<table id="A2.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{n,k}=\frac{1}{k}\sum_{j=1}^{k-1}\sum_{|S|=k}\omega_{k,j}^{\sum_{s\in S}s}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub></mstyle><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{n,k}=\frac{1}{k}\sum_{j=1}^{k-1}\sum_{|S|=k}\omega_{k,j}^{\sum_{s\in S}s}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.25" class="ltx_p">Thus, <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(n,k)=\frac{1}{k}\binom{n}{k}+R_{n,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(n,k)=\frac{1}{k}\binom{n}{k}+R_{n,k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Summing over all possible subset sizes <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</p>
<table id="A2.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{n}=\sum_{k=1}^{n}\frac{1}{k}\binom{n}{k}+\sum_{k=1}^{n}R_{n,k}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{n}=\sum_{k=1}^{n}\frac{1}{k}\binom{n}{k}+\sum_{k=1}^{n}R_{n,k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.28" class="ltx_p">Using the well-known identity <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{n}\frac{1}{k}\binom{n}{k}=\sum_{j=1}^{n}\frac{2^{j}-1}{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mfrac><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>j</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>j</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{n}\frac{1}{k}\binom{n}{k}=\sum_{j=1}^{n}\frac{2^{j}-1}{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, we separate this into two sums: <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{n}=\sum_{j=1}^{n}\frac{2^{j}}{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mfrac><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>j</mi></msup><mi>j</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n}=\sum_{j=1}^{n}\frac{2^{j}}{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and the harmonic number <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.28.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{n}=\sum_{j=1}^{n}\frac{1}{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>j</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{n}=\sum_{j=1}^{n}\frac{1}{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. This yields our fundamental decomposition</p>
<table id="A2.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{n}=S_{n}-H_{n}+\sum_{k=1}^{n}R_{n,k}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{n}=S_{n}-H_{n}+\sum_{k=1}^{n}R_{n,k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.34" class="ltx_p">Next, we establish that the sum of the remainders <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{n}R_{n,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{n}R_{n,k}</annotation></semantics></math> is asymptotically negligible.
Consider the inner sum <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{|S|=k}\omega_{k,j}^{\sum_{s\in S}s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub></mstyle><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{|S|=k}\omega_{k,j}^{\sum_{s\in S}s}</annotation></semantics></math>. This sum is exactly the coefficient of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.31.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>z</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> in the polynomial <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.32.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{n,k,j}(z)=\prod_{m=1}^{n}(1+z\omega_{k,j}^{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{n,k,j}(z)=\prod_{m=1}^{n}(1+z\omega_{k,j}^{m})</annotation></semantics></math>. By standard coefficient bounds, the magnitude of the <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.33.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th coefficient of a polynomial is bounded by its maximum modulus on the unit circle <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.34.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|z|=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|z|=1</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\sum_{|S|=k}\omega_{k,j}^{\sum_{s\in S}s}\right|\leq\max_{|z|=1}\prod_{m=1}^{n}|1+z\omega_{k,j}^{m}|" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub></mstyle><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\sum_{|S|=k}\omega_{k,j}^{\sum_{s\in S}s}\right|\leq\max_{|z|=1}\prod_{m=1}^{n}|1+z\omega_{k,j}^{m}|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.55" class="ltx_p">For a fixed <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\{1,\dots,k-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\{1,\dots,k-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the sequence of roots <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.37.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{k,j}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{k,j}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is periodic with period <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.38.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=\frac{k}{\gcd(j,k)}\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>gcd</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=\frac{k}{\gcd(j,k)}\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. The product over a full period <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.39.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> can be evaluated algebraically: the roots of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.40.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{L}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{L}-1</annotation></semantics></math> dictate that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.41.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{m=A}^{A+L-1}(1+z\omega_{k,j}^{m})=1-(-z)^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{m=A}^{A+L-1}(1+z\omega_{k,j}^{m})=1-(-z)^{L}</annotation></semantics></math>. For any <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.42.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> on the unit circle, the magnitude <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.43.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|1-(-z)^{L}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|1-(-z)^{L}|</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly bounded by <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.44.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>.
When taking the product over all <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.45.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> terms, we group them into <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.46.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lfloor n/L\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lfloor n/L\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math> full periods, leaving <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.47.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\bmod L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>mod</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\bmod L</annotation></semantics></math> residual terms. For <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.48.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|z|=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|z|=1</annotation></semantics></math>, each full period contributes at most a factor of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.49.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>, and by the triangle inequality <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.50.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|1+z\omega_{k,j}^{m}|\leq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|1+z\omega_{k,j}^{m}|\leq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, each residual term also contributes at most a factor of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.51.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the total product is bounded by <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.52.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{\lfloor n/L\rfloor+(n\bmod L)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>mod</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{\lfloor n/L\rfloor+(n\bmod L)}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Because <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.53.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.54.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lfloor n/L\rfloor+(n\bmod L)\leq\frac{n}{2}+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>mod</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lfloor n/L\rfloor+(n\bmod L)\leq\frac{n}{2}+1</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, for any <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.55.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> on the unit circle, we have</p>
<table id="A2.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|P_{n,k,j}(z)|\leq 2^{\frac{n}{2}+1}=2\cdot 2^{n/2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|P_{n,k,j}(z)|\leq 2^{\frac{n}{2}+1}=2\cdot 2^{n/2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.58" class="ltx_p">Consequently, the magnitude of the coefficient is bounded by <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\cdot 2^{n/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\cdot 2^{n/2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Applying this to our remainder definition yields <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.57.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|R_{n,k}|\leq\frac{k-1}{k}2\cdot 2^{n/2}\leq 2\cdot 2^{n/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|R_{n,k}|\leq\frac{k-1}{k}2\cdot 2^{n/2}\leq 2\cdot 2^{n/2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Summing over <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.58.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\{1,\dots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\{1,\dots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math> gives the strict bound</p>
<table id="A2.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\sum_{k=1}^{n}R_{n,k}\right|\leq 2n2^{n/2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\sum_{k=1}^{n}R_{n,k}\right|\leq 2n2^{n/2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.60" class="ltx_p">We must now evaluate the asymptotics of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{n}=\sum_{j=1}^{n}\frac{2^{j}}{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mfrac><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>j</mi></msup><mi>j</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n}=\sum_{j=1}^{n}\frac{2^{j}}{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. We propose the asymptotic approximation <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.60.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, defined as</p>
<table id="A2.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{n}=\frac{2^{n+1}}{n}\left(1+\frac{1}{n}+\frac{3}{n^{2}}+\frac{13}{n^{3}}+\frac{75}{n^{4}}+\frac{541}{n^{5}}\right)=\frac{2^{n+1}P(n)}{n^{6}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>13</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>75</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>541</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{n}=\frac{2^{n+1}}{n}\left(1+\frac{1}{n}+\frac{3}{n^{2}}+\frac{13}{n^{3}}+\frac{75}{n^{4}}+\frac{541}{n^{5}}\right)=\frac{2^{n+1}P(n)}{n^{6}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.64" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(n)=n^{5}+n^{4}+3n^{3}+13n^{2}+75n+541" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>13</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>75</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>541</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(n)=n^{5}+n^{4}+3n^{3}+13n^{2}+75n+541</annotation></semantics></math>.
To demonstrate that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.62.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is a highly accurate approximation of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.63.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, we analyze the discrepancy in their consecutive differences. Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.64.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> be the discrete derivative error given by</p>
<table id="A2.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{j}=f_{j}-f_{j-1}-\frac{2^{j}}{j}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>j</mi></msup><mi>j</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{j}=f_{j}-f_{j-1}-\frac{2^{j}}{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.67" class="ltx_p">By telescoping summation, <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{n}-f_{n}=S_{1}-f_{1}-\sum_{j=2}^{n}E_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n}-f_{n}=S_{1}-f_{1}-\sum_{j=2}^{n}E_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. To bound <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.66.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, we expand <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.67.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{j}-f_{j-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{j}-f_{j-1}</annotation></semantics></math> algebraically to obtain</p>
<table id="A2.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{j}-f_{j-1}-\frac{2^{j}}{j}=\frac{2^{j}\left[2P(j)(j-1)^{6}-P(j-1)j^{6}-j^{5}(j-1)^{6}\right]}{j^{6}(j-1)^{6}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>j</mi></msup><mi>j</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>j</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{j}-f_{j-1}-\frac{2^{j}}{j}=\frac{2^{j}\left[2P(j)(j-1)^{6}-P(j-1)j^{6}-j^{5}(j-1)^{6}\right]}{j^{6}(j-1)^{6}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.70" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(x)=2P(x)(x-1)^{6}-P(x-1)x^{6}-x^{5}(x-1)^{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(x)=2P(x)(x-1)^{6}-P(x-1)x^{6}-x^{5}(x-1)^{6}</annotation></semantics></math>. Expanding <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.69.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(x)</annotation></semantics></math> leaves a polynomial of strictly degree <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.70.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(x)=-4683x^{5}+13586x^{4}-19540x^{3}+15356x^{2}-6342x+1082" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4683</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>13586</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>19540</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>15356</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>6342</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1082</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(x)=-4683x^{5}+13586x^{4}-19540x^{3}+15356x^{2}-6342x+1082</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.72" class="ltx_p">In particular, it is easy to show that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A(j)|\leq 100000j^{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>100000</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A(j)|\leq 100000j^{5}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.72.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting this back into the error term yields</p>
<table id="A2.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|E_{j}|\leq\frac{100000\cdot 2^{j}}{j^{7}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>100000</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mn>7</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|E_{j}|\leq\frac{100000\cdot 2^{j}}{j^{7}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.76" class="ltx_p">Summing these errors up to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, the sum is dominated by its largest terms, giving <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.74.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j=2}^{n}|E_{j}|=\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{2^{n}}{n^{7}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>7</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j=2}^{n}|E_{j}|=\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{2^{n}}{n^{7}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Recall our decomposition <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.75.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{n}=f_{n}+(S_{n}-f_{n})-H_{n}+\sum_{k=1}^{n}R_{n,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{n}=f_{n}+(S_{n}-f_{n})-H_{n}+\sum_{k=1}^{n}R_{n,k}</annotation></semantics></math>. To prove the theorem, it suffices to show that the combined error terms are <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.76.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\left(\frac{2^{n+1}}{n^{6}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\left(\frac{2^{n+1}}{n^{6}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<ol id="A2.I13" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I13.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span>
<div id="A2.I13.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I13.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I13.i1.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{n}-f_{n}=\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{2^{n}}{n^{7}}\right)=o\left(\frac{2^{n+1}}{n^{6}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>7</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n}-f_{n}=\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{2^{n}}{n^{7}}\right)=o\left(\frac{2^{n+1}}{n^{6}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</li>
<li id="A2.I13.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span>
<div id="A2.I13.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I13.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I13.i2.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{n}\sim\ln n=o\left(\frac{2^{n+1}}{n^{6}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{n}\sim\ln n=o\left(\frac{2^{n+1}}{n^{6}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</li>
<li id="A2.I13.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span>
<div id="A2.I13.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I13.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I13.i3.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum R_{n,k}\leq 2n2^{n/2}=o\left(\frac{2^{n+1}}{n^{6}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum R_{n,k}\leq 2n2^{n/2}=o\left(\frac{2^{n+1}}{n^{6}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</li>
</ol>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.77" class="ltx_p">Since all residual terms are bounded by <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\left(\frac{2^{n+1}}{n^{6}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\left(\frac{2^{n+1}}{n^{6}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, we conclude that</p>
<table id="A2.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{n}=f_{n}+o\left(\frac{2^{n+1}}{n^{6}}\right)=\frac{2^{n+1}}{n}\left(1+\frac{1}{n}+\frac{3}{n^{2}}+\frac{13}{n^{3}}+\frac{75}{n^{4}}+\frac{541}{n^{5}}+o\left(\frac{1}{n^{5}}\right)\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>13</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>75</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>541</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{n}=f_{n}+o\left(\frac{2^{n+1}}{n^{6}}\right)=\frac{2^{n+1}}{n}\left(1+\frac{1}{n}+\frac{3}{n^{2}}+\frac{13}{n^{3}}+\frac{75}{n^{4}}+\frac{541}{n^{5}}+o\left(\frac{1}{n^{5}}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.87" class="ltx_p">This establishes the conjectured asymptotic expansion.  <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Box" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Box</annotation></semantics></math>


<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.87.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem.</span> (A conjecture of OEIS A228143, 2018) Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.79.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{m}=\sum_{k=0}^{m}\binom{m}{k}^{2}\binom{m+k}{k}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{m}=\sum_{k=0}^{m}\binom{m}{k}^{2}\binom{m+k}{k}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> be the sequence A005259. Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.80.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the determinant of the <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.81.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n+1)\times(n+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n+1)\times(n+1)</annotation></semantics></math> Hankel-type matrix whose <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.82.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math>-entry is <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.83.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i+j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i+j}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.84.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j=0,\dots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j=0,\dots,n</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.85.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(x)=\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}a_{n}x^{n}=1+48x+161856x^{2}+\dots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>48</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>161856</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(x)=\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}a_{n}x^{n}=1+48x+161856x^{2}+\dots</annotation></semantics></math> denote the ordinary generating function of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.86.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p1.87.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(x/3)^{1/8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(x/3)^{1/8}</annotation></semantics></math> has integer coefficients.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof.</span> We proceed in three main stages: analyzing the matrix entries modulo <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p2.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>, analyzing them modulo <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p2.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math>, and using the resulting divisibility properties of the determinant <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p2.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> to construct the required eighth root as a formal power series over the integers.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p3.24" class="ltx_p">First, we determine the residues of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p3.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> modulo <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p3.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>. By writing <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p3.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> in base <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p3.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>, Kummer’s Theorem dictates that the highest power of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p3.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> dividing <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p3.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{2k}{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{2k}{k}</annotation></semantics></math> equals the number of carries when evaluating <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p3.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k+k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k+k</annotation></semantics></math> in base <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p3.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p3.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> contains the digit <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p3.10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>, a carry occurs, so <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p3.11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{2k}{k}\equiv 0\pmod{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{2k}{k}\equiv 0\pmod{3}</annotation></semantics></math>. Alternatively, if <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p3.12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> consists only of the digits <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p3.13.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><mn>0</mn></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p3.14.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, there are no carries. Applying Lucas’s Theorem digit-by-digit to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p3.15.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{2k}{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{2k}{k}</annotation></semantics></math> yields a product of terms <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p3.16.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{0}{0}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>0</mn><mn>0</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{0}{0}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p3.17.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{2}{1}=2\equiv-1\pmod{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>2</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{2}{1}=2\equiv-1\pmod{3}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p3.18.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{2k}{k}\equiv(-1)^{c}\pmod{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>c</mi></msup><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{2k}{k}\equiv(-1)^{c}\pmod{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p3.19.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p3.20.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>s in the base-3 representation of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p3.21.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p3.22.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> shares the same parity as <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p3.23.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p3.24.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{2k}{k}\equiv(-1)^{k}\pmod{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{2k}{k}\equiv(-1)^{k}\pmod{3}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p4.19" class="ltx_p">We can rewrite the squared product of binomial coefficients as:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\binom{m}{k}\binom{m+k}{k}\right)^{2}=\binom{m+k}{2k}^{2}\binom{2k}{k}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\binom{m}{k}\binom{m+k}{k}\right)^{2}=\binom{m+k}{2k}^{2}\binom{2k}{k}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p4.14" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p4.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{2k}{k}\not\equiv 0\pmod{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≢</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{2k}{k}\not\equiv 0\pmod{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, the base-3 digits of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p4.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2k</annotation></semantics></math> are strictly <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p4.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><mn>0</mn></math>s and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p4.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>s. Applying Lucas’s Theorem to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p4.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{m+k}{2k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{m+k}{2k}</annotation></semantics></math>, each digit of the evaluation takes the form <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p4.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{d_{i}}{0}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>0</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{d_{i}}{0}=1</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p4.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{d_{i}}{2}\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{d_{i}}{2}\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p4.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{m+k}{2k}\equiv 0\text{ or }1\pmod{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> or </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{m+k}{2k}\equiv 0\text{ or }1\pmod{3}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since values in <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p4.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> are invariant under squaring, <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p4.10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{m+k}{2k}^{2}\equiv\binom{m+k}{2k}\pmod{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{m+k}{2k}^{2}\equiv\binom{m+k}{2k}\pmod{3}</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, since <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p4.11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{2k}{k}\in\{0,(-1)^{k}\}\pmod{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{2k}{k}\in\{0,(-1)^{k}\}\pmod{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, squaring it absorbs the parity: <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p4.12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{2k}{k}^{2}\equiv(-1)^{k}\binom{2k}{k}\pmod{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{2k}{k}^{2}\equiv(-1)^{k}\binom{2k}{k}\pmod{3}</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining these pieces, we find that for all <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p4.13.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p4.14.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\binom{m}{k}\binom{m+k}{k}\right)^{2}\equiv(-1)^{k}\binom{m+k}{2k}\binom{2k}{k}\equiv(-1)^{k}\binom{m}{k}\binom{m+k}{k}\pmod{3}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≡</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\binom{m}{k}\binom{m+k}{k}\right)^{2}\equiv(-1)^{k}\binom{m+k}{2k}\binom{2k}{k}\equiv(-1)^{k}\binom{m}{k}\binom{m+k}{k}\pmod{3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p4.18" class="ltx_p">Summing this equivalence over <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p4.15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0,\dots,m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0,\dots,m</annotation></semantics></math> yields <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p4.16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{m}\equiv\sum_{k=0}^{m}(-1)^{k}\binom{m}{k}\binom{m+k}{k}\pmod{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">≡</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{m}\equiv\sum_{k=0}^{m}(-1)^{k}\binom{m}{k}\binom{m+k}{k}\pmod{3}</annotation></semantics></math>. By a standard alternating binomial sum identity, <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p4.17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=0}^{m}(-1)^{k}\binom{m}{k}\binom{m+k}{k}=(-1)^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=0}^{m}(-1)^{k}\binom{m}{k}\binom{m+k}{k}=(-1)^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p4.18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{m}\equiv(-1)^{m}\pmod{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{m}\equiv(-1)^{m}\pmod{3}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p5.10" class="ltx_p">Using this congruence, we apply row operations to the matrix <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p5.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{(n)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{(n)}</annotation></semantics></math> to establish that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p5.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3^{n}\mid a_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>∣</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3^{n}\mid a_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p5.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be the lower-triangular matrix with ones on the main diagonal, <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p5.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i,0}=-(-1)^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i,0}=-(-1)^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p5.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, and zeros elsewhere. The matrix product <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p5.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{n}M^{(n)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{n}M^{(n)}</annotation></semantics></math> replaces each row <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p5.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> with the <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p5.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th row minus <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p5.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-1)^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-1)^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> times the <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p5.10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><mn>0</mn></math>-th row. Visually, the modified matrix takes the form:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{n}M^{(n)}=\begin{bmatrix}s_{0}&amp;s_{1}&amp;s_{2}&amp;\cdots&amp;s_{n}\\
s_{1}+s_{0}&amp;s_{2}+s_{1}&amp;s_{3}+s_{2}&amp;\cdots&amp;s_{n+1}+s_{n}\\
s_{2}-s_{0}&amp;s_{3}-s_{1}&amp;s_{4}-s_{2}&amp;\cdots&amp;s_{n+2}-s_{n}\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots\\
s_{n}-(-1)^{n}s_{0}&amp;s_{n+1}-(-1)^{n}s_{1}&amp;s_{n+2}-(-1)^{n}s_{2}&amp;\cdots&amp;s_{2n}-(-1)^{n}s_{n}\end{bmatrix}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋮</mi></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋮</mi></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋮</mi></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋱</mi></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋮</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{n}M^{(n)}=\begin{bmatrix}s_{0}&amp;s_{1}&amp;s_{2}&amp;\cdots&amp;s_{n}\\
s_{1}+s_{0}&amp;s_{2}+s_{1}&amp;s_{3}+s_{2}&amp;\cdots&amp;s_{n+1}+s_{n}\\
s_{2}-s_{0}&amp;s_{3}-s_{1}&amp;s_{4}-s_{2}&amp;\cdots&amp;s_{n+2}-s_{n}\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots\\
s_{n}-(-1)^{n}s_{0}&amp;s_{n+1}-(-1)^{n}s_{1}&amp;s_{n+2}-(-1)^{n}s_{2}&amp;\cdots&amp;s_{2n}-(-1)^{n}s_{n}\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p5.22" class="ltx_p">The new <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p5.11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math>-entry for <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p5.12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p5.13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i+j}-(-1)^{i}s_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i+j}-(-1)^{i}s_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. By our previous congruence, <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p5.14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i+j}-(-1)^{i}s_{j}\equiv(-1)^{i+j}-(-1)^{i}(-1)^{j}\equiv 0\pmod{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i+j}-(-1)^{i}s_{j}\equiv(-1)^{i+j}-(-1)^{i}(-1)^{j}\equiv 0\pmod{3}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, every entry in rows <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p5.15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> through <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p5.16.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> of the new matrix is divisible by <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p5.17.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>. Factoring a <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p5.18.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> out of each of these <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p5.19.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> rows gives a factor of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p5.20.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Because <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p5.21.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\det(P_{n})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\det(P_{n})=1</annotation></semantics></math>, we conclude that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p5.22.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3^{n}\mid\det(M^{(n)})=a_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.1389em">∣</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3^{n}\mid\det(M^{(n)})=a_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p6.11" class="ltx_p">Second, we analyze <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p6.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> modulo <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p6.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math>. For any <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p6.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, the product <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p6.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{m}{k}\binom{m+k}{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{m}{k}\binom{m+k}{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is always even, which implies its square is divisible by <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p6.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p6.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\binom{m}{k}\binom{m+k}{k}\right)^{2}\equiv 0\pmod{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\binom{m}{k}\binom{m+k}{k}\right)^{2}\equiv 0\pmod{4}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p6.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. The <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p6.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0</annotation></semantics></math> term evaluates to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p6.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p6.10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{m}\equiv 1\pmod{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{m}\equiv 1\pmod{4}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p6.11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p7.7" class="ltx_p">We apply a similar matrix transformation to establish divisibility by <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p7.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>4</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p7.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be the lower-triangular matrix with ones on the diagonal, <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p7.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}_{i,0}=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}_{i,0}=-1</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p7.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, and zeros elsewhere. The product <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p7.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}_{n}M^{(n)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}_{n}M^{(n)}</annotation></semantics></math> subtracts the <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p7.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><mn>0</mn></math>-th row from every subsequent row <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p7.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}_{n}M^{(n)}=\begin{bmatrix}s_{0}&amp;s_{1}&amp;\cdots&amp;s_{n}\\
s_{1}-s_{0}&amp;s_{2}-s_{1}&amp;\cdots&amp;s_{n+1}-s_{n}\\
s_{2}-s_{0}&amp;s_{3}-s_{1}&amp;\cdots&amp;s_{n+2}-s_{n}\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots\end{bmatrix}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋮</mi></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋮</mi></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋱</mi></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋮</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}_{n}M^{(n)}=\begin{bmatrix}s_{0}&amp;s_{1}&amp;\cdots&amp;s_{n}\\
s_{1}-s_{0}&amp;s_{2}-s_{1}&amp;\cdots&amp;s_{n+1}-s_{n}\\
s_{2}-s_{0}&amp;s_{3}-s_{1}&amp;\cdots&amp;s_{n+2}-s_{n}\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p7.16" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p7.8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p7.9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math>-entry becomes <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p7.10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i+j}-s_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i+j}-s_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p7.11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{m}\equiv 1\pmod{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{m}\equiv 1\pmod{4}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p7.12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, this difference evaluates to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p7.13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-1\equiv 0\pmod{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mspace style="width:0.949em;" width="0.949em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">mod</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-1\equiv 0\pmod{4}</annotation></semantics></math>. Factoring <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p7.14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> out of the <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p7.15.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> modified rows shows that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p7.16.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4^{n}\mid\det(M^{(n)})=a_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mn>4</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.1389em">∣</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4^{n}\mid\det(M^{(n)})=a_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p8.13" class="ltx_p">Now we combine these divisibility properties. We explicitly compute <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p8.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}=48" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>48</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}=48</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p8.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, we know <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p8.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4^{n}\mid a_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mn>4</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>∣</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4^{n}\mid a_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, and since <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p8.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4^{n}\geq 16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mn>4</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>≥</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4^{n}\geq 16</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p8.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p8.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16\mid a_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo>∣</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16\mid a_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p8.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> (as <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p8.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16\mid 48" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo>∣</mo><mn>48</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16\mid 48</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p8.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=1</annotation></semantics></math>). Because <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p8.10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p8.11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> are coprime, their respective divisibilities imply <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p8.12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16\cdot 3^{n}\mid a_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><mo>∣</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16\cdot 3^{n}\mid a_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p8.13.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p9.9" class="ltx_p">We consider the scaled generating function <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p9.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(x/3)=\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}\frac{a_{n}}{3^{n}}x^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(x/3)=\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}\frac{a_{n}}{3^{n}}x^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p9.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{n}=a_{n}/3^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{n}=a_{n}/3^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the coefficients of this series. Since <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p9.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{0}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{0}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p9.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{0}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{0}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p9.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, our divisibility result yields <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p9.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16\mid b_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo>∣</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16\mid b_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, we can write <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p9.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(x/3)=1+16Y(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(x/3)=1+16Y(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p9.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y(x)=\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}y_{n}x^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y(x)=\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}y_{n}x^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is a formal power series with integer coefficients and zero constant term (<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p9.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p10.3" class="ltx_p">Finally, we construct the eighth root <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p10.1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="C(x)=A(x/3)^{1/8}\in\mathbb{Z}\llbracket x\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(x)=A(x/3)^{1/8}\in\mathbb{Z}\llbracket x\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math>. We seek a series of the form <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p10.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(x)=1+2X(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(x)=1+2X(x)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p10.3.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="X(x)\in\mathbb{Z}\llbracket x\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(x)\in\mathbb{Z}\llbracket x\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math> has no constant term. Expanding the eighth power yields</p>
<table id="A2.Ex52" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex52X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex52X.2.1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(1+2X(x))^{8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>8</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(1+2X(x))^{8}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex52X.3.2.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1+6X(x)+12X(x)^{2}+48X(x)^{3}+120X(x)^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>112</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>448</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1120</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1+6X(x)+12X(x)^{2}+48X(x)^{3}+120X(x)^{4}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex52Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex52Xa.2.1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+792X(x)^{5}+792X(x)^{6}+024X(x)^{7}+56X(x)^{8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1792</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1792</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1024</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>7</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>256</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>8</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+792X(x)^{5}+792X(x)^{6}+024X(x)^{7}+56X(x)^{8}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p10.4" class="ltx_p">Factoring out <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p10.4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math> from the higher degree terms, we define the polynomial</p>
<table id="A2.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(X)=7X^{2}+28X^{3}+70X^{4}+112X^{5}+112X^{6}+64X^{7}+16X^{8}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>28</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>70</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>112</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>112</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>64</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>7</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>8</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(X)=7X^{2}+28X^{3}+70X^{4}+112X^{5}+112X^{6}+64X^{7}+16X^{8}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p10.8" class="ltx_p">Thus, <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p10.5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1+2X(x))^{8}=1+16(X(x)+P(X(x)))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>8</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1+2X(x))^{8}=1+16(X(x)+P(X(x)))</annotation></semantics></math>. To satisfy <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p10.6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(x)^{8}=A(x/3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>8</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(x)^{8}=A(x/3)</annotation></semantics></math>, we must solve the equation <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p10.7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+16(X(x)+P(X(x)))=1+16Y(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+16(X(x)+P(X(x)))=1+16Y(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, which simplifies to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p10.8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(x)+P(X(x))=Y(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(x)+P(X(x))=Y(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p11.4" class="ltx_p">We determine the coefficients <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p11.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p11.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(x)=\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}x_{n}x^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(x)=\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}x_{n}x^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> inductively. We set <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p11.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. For the inductive step, the coefficient of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p11.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math> in the equation is</p>
<table id="A2.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{n+1}+[x^{n+1}]P(X(x))=y_{n+1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{n+1}+[x^{n+1}]P(X(x))=y_{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p11.11" class="ltx_p">Because every term in <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p11.5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(X)</annotation></semantics></math> has degree at least <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p11.6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p11.7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(x)</annotation></semantics></math> has no constant term, the <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p11.8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math> coefficient of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p11.9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(X(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(X(x))</annotation></semantics></math> depends only on the terms <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p11.10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},\dots,x_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},\dots,x_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, we can uniquely solve for the integers <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p11.11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="A2.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{n+1}=y_{n+1}-[x^{n+1}]P\left(\sum_{k=1}^{n}x_{k}x^{k}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{n+1}=y_{n+1}-[x^{n+1}]P\left(\sum_{k=1}^{n}x_{k}x^{k}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p11.18" class="ltx_p">This well-defined recurrence provides an integer sequence <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p11.12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{n})_{n\geq 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{n})_{n\geq 1}</annotation></semantics></math> giving a formal power series <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p11.13.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="X(x)\in\mathbb{Z}\llbracket x\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(x)\in\mathbb{Z}\llbracket x\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math> that satisfies <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p11.14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(x)+P(X(x))=Y(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(x)+P(X(x))=Y(x)</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting this back into our expansion yields <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p11.15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1+2X(x))^{8}=1+16Y(x)=A(x/3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>8</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1+2X(x))^{8}=1+16Y(x)=A(x/3)</annotation></semantics></math>. Setting <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p11.16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(x)=1+2X(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(x)=1+2X(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have established the existence of the desired integer power series <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p11.17.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(x)=A(x/3)^{1/8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(x)=A(x/3)^{1/8}</annotation></semantics></math>.  <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p11.18.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Box" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Box</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx10.p12.1" class="ltx_p">These OEIS problems were added as conjectures in 2022 (<a href="https://oeis.org/A051293" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://oeis.org/A051293</a>) and 2018 (<a href="https://oeis.org/A228143" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://oeis.org/A228143</a>). Though neither problem has likely received much attention, the ability to provide a guarantee on the correctness of the statement that an expert conjectured serves value. For example, it appears that a good part of the work is done in identifying the asymptotic formula to be conjectured in OEIS A051293. In this case, ensuring the formula holds with a rigorous proof is a matter of validating intuition without carrying out potentially tedious proof steps, which our agent can handle. The Lean proofs for the two problems can be found at <a href="https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/main/APNOutputs/OEIS" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/main/APNOutputs/OEIS</a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSSx11" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">A variant of the Graph Reconstruction Conjecture</h4>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Kelly-Ulam graph reconstruction program aims to recover a graph from its deck of one-vertex-deleted subgraphs <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">ulam1960collection</span>, <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">Kelly1957</span>]</cite>. A standard bipartite version was formulated by Bondy and Hemminger as the problem of showing that bipartite graphs are reconstructible <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">BondyHemminger1977</span>]</cite>. The following theorem proves a structured incidence-deletion analogue under strong type-distinguishability assumptions.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.17" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.17.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Terminology</span>
Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega=L\sqcup R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⊔</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega=L\sqcup R</annotation></semantics></math> be a finite vertex set with a partition into the disjoint parts <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L,R\subseteq\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L,R\subseteq\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>.
A graph <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> is bipartite with respect to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(L,R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(L,R)</annotation></semantics></math> if every edge of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> has one endpoint in <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> and one endpoint in
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>. We say <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-connected if <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> is connected and, for every vertex <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, the induced graph on
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\setminus\{v\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\setminus\{v\}</annotation></semantics></math> is connected. For a graph <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.13.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and a vertex <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.14.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, write <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.15.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><msub><mo>∖</mo><mi>inc</mi></msub><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}v</annotation></semantics></math>
for the graph obtained from <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.16.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> by deleting all edges incident to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.17.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, while
leaving the vertex set unchanged. Thus</p>
<table id="A2.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E(K\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}v)=\{xy\in E(K):x\neq v,\ y\neq v\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><msub><mo>∖</mo><mi>inc</mi></msub><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E(K\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}v)=\{xy\in E(K):x\neq v,\ y\neq v\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.20" class="ltx_p">A bipartite isomorphism <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\cong_{B}K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><msub><mo>≅</mo><mi>B</mi></msub><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\cong_{B}K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is a graph isomorphism whose underlying
bijection preserves both parts <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.20.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>. The bipartite deck is the multiset</p>
<table id="A2.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{B}(K):=\{\!\{[K\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}v]_{B}:v\in\Omega\}\!\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.330em;" width="0.330em"><mo stretchy="false">{</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><msub><mo>∖</mo><mi>inc</mi></msub><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>B</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><mpadded style="width:0.330em;" width="0.330em"><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{B}(K):=\{\!\{[K\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}v]_{B}:v\in\Omega\}\!\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.25" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\cdot]_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>B</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\cdot]_{B}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes bipartite-isomorphism class.
Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{K}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{K}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> be the neighbor set of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.23.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.24.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>. The degree profile and type of
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.25.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> are</p>
<table id="A2.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{K}(x):=\{\!\{\deg_{K}(y):y\in N_{K}(x)\}\!\},\qquad\tau_{K}(x):=(\deg_{K}(x),P_{K}(x))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.330em;" width="0.330em"><mo stretchy="false">{</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>deg</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mpadded style="width:0.330em;" width="0.330em"><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>deg</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{K}(x):=\{\!\{\deg_{K}(y):y\in N_{K}(x)\}\!\},\qquad\tau_{K}(x):=(\deg_{K}(x),P_{K}(x)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.26" class="ltx_p">The type profile of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> is the multiset of the types of its neighbors:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{K}(u):=\{\!\{\tau_{K}(x):x\in N_{K}(u)\}\!\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.330em;" width="0.330em"><mo stretchy="false">{</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mpadded style="width:0.330em;" width="0.330em"><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{K}(u):=\{\!\{\tau_{K}(x):x\in N_{K}(u)\}\!\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.28" class="ltx_p">Finally, for a type <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=(d,M)\in\mathbb{N}\times\operatorname{Multiset}(\mathbb{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>Multiset</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=(d,M)\in\mathbb{N}\times\operatorname{Multiset}(\mathbb{N})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="A2.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{a}(t):=(\max(d-1,0),M\setminus\{a\})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{a}(t):=(\max(d-1,0),M\setminus\{a\}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.36" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\setminus\{a\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\setminus\{a\}</annotation></semantics></math> means deletion of one occurrence of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> from the multiset
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.31.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>. In the applications below, <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.32.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> is applied to neighbor-types, whose
first coordinate is positive, so <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.33.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max(d-1,0)=d-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max(d-1,0)=d-1</annotation></semantics></math> there. We write
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.34.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\#_{t}M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">#</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\#_{t}M</annotation></semantics></math> for the multiplicity of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.35.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> in a multiset <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p2.36.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p3.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p3.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem</span> (Weak bipartite graph reconstruction)
Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p3.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p3.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> be finite simple graphs on the same finite vertex set
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p3.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>, both bipartite with respect to the same parts <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p3.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega=L\sqcup R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⊔</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega=L\sqcup R</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p3.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\Omega\right|\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\Omega\right|\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p3.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is 2-connected and all vertex types of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p3.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> are pairwise distinct, that is, <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p3.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{G}(x)\neq\tau_{G}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{G}(x)\neq\tau_{G}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p3.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\neq y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\neq y</annotation></semantics></math>. If
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p3.10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{B}(G)=\mathcal{D}_{B}(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{B}(G)=\mathcal{D}_{B}(H)</annotation></semantics></math>,
then <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p3.11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p3.12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> are bipartite-isomorphic.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof.</span>
Write <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p4.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=\left|\Omega\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=\left|\Omega\right|</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p4.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e(K)=\left|E(K)\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e(K)=\left|E(K)\right|</annotation></semantics></math>. Since bipartite isomorphisms
preserve edge counts, the deck determines the multiset</p>
<table id="A2.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\!\{e(K\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}v):v\in\Omega\}\!\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.330em;" width="0.330em"><mo stretchy="false">{</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><msub><mo>∖</mo><mi>inc</mi></msub><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><mpadded style="width:0.330em;" width="0.330em"><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\!\{e(K\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}v):v\in\Omega\}\!\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p4.3" class="ltx_p">For every vertex <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p4.3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e(K\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}v)+\deg_{K}(v)=e(K)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><msub><mo>∖</mo><mi>inc</mi></msub><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>deg</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e(K\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}v)+\deg_{K}(v)=e(K),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p4.5" class="ltx_p">because <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p4.4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><msub><mo>∖</mo><mi>inc</mi></msub><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}v</annotation></semantics></math> removes exactly the edges incident to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p4.5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>. Also,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{v\in\Omega}e(K\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}v)=(n-2)e(K)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><msub><mo>∖</mo><mi>inc</mi></msub><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{v\in\Omega}e(K\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}v)=(n-2)e(K),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p4.11" class="ltx_p">because each edge of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p4.6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> remains in precisely the cards indexed by the
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p4.7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-2</annotation></semantics></math> vertices not incident to that edge. Since <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p4.8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>, equation (2) shows
that the deck determines <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p4.9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e(K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e(K)</annotation></semantics></math>. Applying this to the equal decks of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p4.10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p4.11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> gives</p>
<table id="A2.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e(G)=e(H)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e(G)=e(H),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p4.13" class="ltx_p">and then equation (1) shows that the degree multisets of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p4.12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p4.13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> are equal.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Equality of the two decks also gives a bijection <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p5.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\Omega\to\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\Omega\to\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> such that,
for every <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p5.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>, there is a bipartite isomorphism</p>
<table id="A2.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{v}:G\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}v\cong_{B}H\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}{f(v)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><msub><mo>∖</mo><mi>inc</mi></msub><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mo>≅</mo><mi>B</mi></msub><mrow><mi>H</mi><msub><mo>∖</mo><mi>inc</mi></msub><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{v}:G\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}v\cong_{B}H\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}{f(v)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p5.4" class="ltx_p">For this matched pair of cards, edge counts are equal. Combining this with
(1) and (3) yields</p>
<table id="A2.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg_{G}(v)=\deg_{H}(f(v))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>deg</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>deg</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg_{G}(v)=\deg_{H}(f(v))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p5.3" class="ltx_p">for every <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p5.3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p6.13" class="ltx_p">Next, <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p6.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> has minimum degree at least <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p6.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed, if a vertex had degree <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p6.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><mn>0</mn></math>,
then <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p6.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> would not be connected; if a vertex <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p6.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> had the unique neighbor <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p6.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>,
then the induced graph on <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p6.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\setminus\{y\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\setminus\{y\}</annotation></semantics></math> would contain the isolated
vertex <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p6.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, contradicting <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p6.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-connectivity. Since the
degree multisets of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p6.10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p6.11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> are equal, <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p6.12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> also has minimum degree at least
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p6.13.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p7.13" class="ltx_p">Therefore, in any graph <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p7.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> with minimum degree at least <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p7.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>, the card
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p7.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><msub><mo>∖</mo><mi>inc</mi></msub><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}v</annotation></semantics></math> has a unique isolated vertex, namely <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p7.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed, the vertex <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p7.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is isolated
because all its incident edges have been removed. On the other hand, if <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p7.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\neq v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\neq v</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p7.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> has at
least two neighbors in <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p7.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, at most one of which is <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p7.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>; hence <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p7.10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> has a
neighbor <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p7.11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\neq v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\neq v</annotation></semantics></math>, and the edge <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p7.12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="xy" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">xy</annotation></semantics></math> remains in <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p7.13.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><msub><mo>∖</mo><mi>inc</mi></msub><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}v</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p8.3" class="ltx_p">Applying this uniqueness to (4), the isomorphism <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p8.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> sends the unique
isolated vertex of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p8.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><msub><mo>∖</mo><mi>inc</mi></msub><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}v</annotation></semantics></math> to the unique isolated vertex of
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p8.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}{f(v)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><msub><mo>∖</mo><mi>inc</mi></msub><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}{f(v)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence</p>
<table id="A2.Ex71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{v}(v)=f(v)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{v}(v)=f(v).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p8.7" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p8.4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> preserves <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p8.5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p8.6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>, (6) implies that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p8.7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> preserves the two
parts:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in L\Longleftrightarrow f(v)\in L,\qquad v\in R\Longleftrightarrow f(v)\in R." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟺</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟺</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in L\Longleftrightarrow f(v)\in L,\qquad v\in R\Longleftrightarrow f(v)\in R.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.3" class="ltx_p">We now prove that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> preserves vertex types. It remains, in view of (5), to
compare degree profiles. For a graph <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and vertex <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, put</p>
<table id="A2.Ex75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{K}(k):=\#\{x\in\Omega:\deg_{K}(x)=k\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>deg</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{K}(k):=\#\{x\in\Omega:\deg_{K}(x)=k\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.Ex76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{K,v}(k):=\#\{x\in\Omega:\deg_{K\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}v}(x)=k\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>deg</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><msub><mo>∖</mo><mi>inc</mi></msub><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{K,v}(k):=\#\{x\in\Omega:\deg_{K\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}v}(x)=k\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.36" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A2.Ex77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{K,v}(k):=\#\{x\in N_{K}(v):\deg_{K}(x)=k\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>deg</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{K,v}(k):=\#\{x\in N_{K}(v):\deg_{K}(x)=k\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.6" class="ltx_p">Counting vertices of degree <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> before and after deleting the incidence set of
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> gives, for every <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{K,v}(k+1)+A_{K}(k)+\mathbf{1}_{k=0}=C_{K,v}(k)+B_{K,v}(k)+\mathbf{1}_{\deg_{K}(v)=k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>deg</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{K,v}(k+1)+A_{K}(k)+\mathbf{1}_{k=0}=C_{K,v}(k)+B_{K,v}(k)+\mathbf{1}_{\deg_{K}(v)=k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.16" class="ltx_p">Indeed, in <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><msub><mo>∖</mo><mi>inc</mi></msub><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}v</annotation></semantics></math>, every non-neighbor of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>
keeps its degree, while every neighbor of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> has its degree lowered by
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence the vertices of degree <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><msub><mo>∖</mo><mi>inc</mi></msub><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}v</annotation></semantics></math>
are precisely the old non-neighbors of degree <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, the old neighbors of
degree <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.14.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k+1</annotation></semantics></math>, and additionally <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.15.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> itself if <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.16.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore</p>
<table id="A2.Ex80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{K,v}(k)=A_{K}(k)-C_{K,v}(k)-\mathbf{1}_{\deg_{K}(v)=k}+C_{K,v}(k+1)+\mathbf{1}_{k=0}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>deg</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{K,v}(k)=A_{K}(k)-C_{K,v}(k)-\mathbf{1}_{\deg_{K}(v)=k}+C_{K,v}(k+1)+\mathbf{1}_{k=0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.23" class="ltx_p">Since the global
degree multisets are equal, <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{G}(k)=A_{H}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{G}(k)=A_{H}(k)</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> is an isomorphism
between the matched cards, <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{G,v}(k)=B_{H,f(v)}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{G,v}(k)=B_{H,f(v)}(k)</annotation></semantics></math>. By (5), the final
indicator in (8) is also the same for <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.20.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.21.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally,
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.22.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{K,v}(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{K,v}(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, because a neighbor always has positive degree. Induction on
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.23.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> in (8) gives</p>
<table id="A2.Ex81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{G,v}(k)=C_{H,f(v)}(k)\qquad(k\geq 0)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{G,v}(k)=C_{H,f(v)}(k)\qquad(k\geq 0).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.37" class="ltx_p">Thus</p>
<table id="A2.Ex82" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G}(v)=P_{H}(f(v))," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G}(v)=P_{H}(f(v)),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.38" class="ltx_p">and together with (5) this proves</p>
<table id="A2.Ex83" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{G}(v)=\tau_{H}(f(v))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{G}(v)=\tau_{H}(f(v))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.24" class="ltx_p">for every <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>.
We next prove equality of type profiles:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex85" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{G}(u)=T_{H}(f(u))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{G}(u)=T_{H}(f(u))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.32" class="ltx_p">for every <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>. Fix <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.27.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in L</annotation></semantics></math>, take <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.28.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=R</annotation></semantics></math>, otherwise take <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.29.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=L</annotation></semantics></math> (thus <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.30.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is the
opposite side from <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.31.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>). By (7) and (9), the multisets of global types on <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.32.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>
agree:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex87" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\!\{\tau_{G}(x):x\in S\}\!\}=\{\!\{\tau_{H}(x):x\in S\}\!\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.330em;" width="0.330em"><mo stretchy="false">{</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mpadded style="width:0.330em;" width="0.330em"><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.330em;" width="0.330em"><mo stretchy="false">{</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mpadded style="width:0.330em;" width="0.330em"><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\!\{\tau_{G}(x):x\in S\}\!\}=\{\!\{\tau_{H}(x):x\in S\}\!\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.35" class="ltx_p">The card isomorphism <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> also preserves <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, and therefore the multisets
of local types on <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p9.35.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> agree:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex89" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\!\{\tau_{G\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}u}(x):x\in S\}\!\}=\{\!\{\tau_{H\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}{f(u)}}(x):x\in S\}\!\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.330em;" width="0.330em"><mo stretchy="false">{</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><msub><mo>∖</mo><mi>inc</mi></msub><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mpadded style="width:0.330em;" width="0.330em"><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.330em;" width="0.330em"><mo stretchy="false">{</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>H</mi><msub><mo>∖</mo><mi>inc</mi></msub><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mpadded style="width:0.330em;" width="0.330em"><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\!\{\tau_{G\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}u}(x):x\in S\}\!\}=\{\!\{\tau_{H\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}{f(u)}}(x):x\in S\}\!\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p10.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p10.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in S</annotation></semantics></math>, bipartiteness gives the local-type formula</p>
<table id="A2.Ex91" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{G\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}u}(x)=\begin{cases}F_{\deg_{G}(u)}(\tau_{G}(x)),&amp;\text{if }x\in N_{G}(u),\\[2.84526pt]
\tau_{G}(x),&amp;\text{if }x\notin N_{G}(u).\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><msub><mo>∖</mo><mi>inc</mi></msub><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><msub><mi>deg</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{G\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}u}(x)=\begin{cases}F_{\deg_{G}(u)}(\tau_{G}(x)),&amp;\text{if }x\in N_{G}(u),\\[2.84526pt]
\tau_{G}(x),&amp;\text{if }x\notin N_{G}(u).\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p10.16" class="ltx_p">Indeed, if <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p10.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> is adjacent to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p10.3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>, then deleting the incidence set of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p10.4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>
removes the edge <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p10.5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ux" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ux</annotation></semantics></math>, lowering <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p10.6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg_{G}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>deg</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg_{G}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> by one and deleting one occurrence
of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p10.7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg_{G}(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>deg</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg_{G}(u)</annotation></semantics></math> from the degree profile of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p10.8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p10.9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> is not adjacent to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p10.10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>,
then any neighbor of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p10.11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> lies on the same side of the bipartition as <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p10.12.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>, and
therefore cannot be adjacent to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p10.13.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>; hence the type of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p10.14.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> is unchanged. The
same formula holds for <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p10.15.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p10.16.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(u)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p11.1" class="ltx_p">Taking the number of occurrences of an arbitrary type <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p11.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> in (13) gives</p>
<table id="A2.Ex93" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\#_{t}\{\!\{\tau_{G\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}u}(x):x\in S\}\!\}+\#_{t}T_{G}(u)=\#_{t}\{\!\{\tau_{G}(x):x\in S\}\!\}+\#_{t}\{\!\{F_{\deg_{G}(u)}(s):s\in T_{G}(u)\}\!\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">#</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.330em;" width="0.330em"><mo stretchy="false">{</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><msub><mo>∖</mo><mi>inc</mi></msub><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mpadded style="width:0.330em;" width="0.330em"><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">#</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">#</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.330em;" width="0.330em"><mo stretchy="false">{</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mpadded style="width:0.330em;" width="0.330em"><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">#</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.330em;" width="0.330em"><mo stretchy="false">{</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><msub><mi>deg</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mpadded style="width:0.330em;" width="0.330em"><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\#_{t}\{\!\{\tau_{G\setminus_{\mathrm{inc}}u}(x):x\in S\}\!\}+\#_{t}T_{G}(u)=\#_{t}\{\!\{\tau_{G}(x):x\in S\}\!\}+\#_{t}\{\!\{F_{\deg_{G}(u)}(s):s\in T_{G}(u)\}\!\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p11.15" class="ltx_p">There is an identical identity for <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p11.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>. The first terms on the two sides of
(14) agree by (12), and the global-type terms agree by (11). Also
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p11.3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg_{G}(u)=\deg_{H}(f(u))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>deg</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>deg</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg_{G}(u)=\deg_{H}(f(u))</annotation></semantics></math> by (5). Hence equality of the type-profile counts
can be proved by descending induction on the first coordinate of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p11.4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. The base
case is that no type in a type profile can have first coordinate at least <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p11.5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>,
since every vertex degree is <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p11.6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi></mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;n</annotation></semantics></math>. For the induction step, the only types
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p11.7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p11.8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\deg_{G}(u)}(s)=t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><msub><mi>deg</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\deg_{G}(u)}(s)=t</annotation></semantics></math> have first coordinate <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p11.9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{1}+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{1}+1</annotation></semantics></math>; moreover every
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p11.10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> occurring in a type profile has positive first coordinate. Thus the
rightmost term in (14) is already equal for <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p11.11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p11.12.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> by the induction
hypothesis, and subtracting the two versions of (14) yields equality of the
number of occurrences of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p11.13.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p11.14.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{G}(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{G}(u)</annotation></semantics></math> and in <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p11.15.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{H}(f(u))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{H}(f(u))</annotation></semantics></math>. This proves (10).</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p12.7" class="ltx_p">The distinctness of types transfers from <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p12.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p12.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>: if
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p12.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{H}(x)=\tau_{H}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{H}(x)=\tau_{H}(y)</annotation></semantics></math>, then by applying (9) to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p12.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{-1}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{-1}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p12.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{-1}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{-1}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> we
obtain equality of the corresponding <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p12.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-types, so <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p12.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=y</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p13.3" class="ltx_p">Since types are pairwise distinct, adjacency is determined by type profiles:
for every graph <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p13.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> among <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p13.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G,H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G,H</annotation></semantics></math> and every pair of vertices <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p13.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex95" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\text{ has edge }ab\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad\tau_{K}(b)\in T_{K}(a)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> has edge </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⟺</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\text{ has edge }ab\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad\tau_{K}(b)\in T_{K}(a).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p13.10" class="ltx_p">The forward implication is the definition of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p13.4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{K}(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{K}(a)</annotation></semantics></math>. Conversely, if
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p13.5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{K}(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{K}(b)</annotation></semantics></math> occurs in <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p13.6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{K}(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{K}(a)</annotation></semantics></math>, then some neighbor <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p13.7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p13.8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> has
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p13.9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{K}(c)=\tau_{K}(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{K}(c)=\tau_{K}(b)</annotation></semantics></math>, and distinctness of types gives <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p13.10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=b</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p14.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, for any <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p14.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u,v\in\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,v\in\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>, equations (9), (10), and (15) give</p>
<table id="A2.Ex97" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\text{ has edge }uv\Longleftrightarrow\tau_{G}(v)\in T_{G}(u)\Longleftrightarrow\tau_{H}(f(v))\in T_{H}(f(u))\Longleftrightarrow H\text{ has edge }f(u)f(v)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> has edge </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟺</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟺</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟺</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> has edge </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\text{ has edge }uv\Longleftrightarrow\tau_{G}(v)\in T_{G}(u)\Longleftrightarrow\tau_{H}(f(v))\in T_{H}(f(u))\Longleftrightarrow H\text{ has edge }f(u)f(v).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p14.4" class="ltx_p">Thus <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p14.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is a graph isomorphism <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p14.3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\cong H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>≅</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\cong H</annotation></semantics></math>. By (7), it preserves the two
bipartition parts, so it is a bipartite isomorphism.  <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p14.4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Box" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Box</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx11.p15.1" class="ltx_p">The Lean proof discovered for this problem is at <a href="https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/main/APNOutputs/AICollaborator/Graphs/bipartite_graph_reconstruction_conjecture_2.lean" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/main/APNOutputs/AICollaborator/Graphs/bipartite_graph_reconstruction_conjecture_2.lean</a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSSx12" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Log-Concavity of Hilbert Sequences</h4>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p1.3" class="ltx_p">A pure O-sequence is the Hilbert function of a monomial Artinian level algebra; equivalently, it counts monomials by degree in a pure finite order ideal of monomials. These sequences go back to Stanley’s work on Hilbert functions of graded algebras <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">Stanley1978</span>]</cite> and have since been extensively studied in combinatorial commutative algebra. In the systematic study <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">BMMNZ2012</span>]</cite>, the authors proved the related unimodality theorem for pure O-sequences of codimension <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> and type <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>. Zanello later formulated the corresponding log-concavity conjecture and identified this same <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(3,2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(3,2)</annotation></semantics></math> case as the main remaining open case for pure O-sequences <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">Zanello2024</span>]</cite>. The following theorem proves this conjecture.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem.</span> (Zanello’s conjecture, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">Zanello2024</span>]</cite>.)
Every pure <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p2.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math>-sequence of codimension <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p2.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> and type <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p2.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> is
log-concave.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p3.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p3.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Terminology.</span>
A monomial <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p3.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}^{m(0)}x_{1}^{m(1)}x_{2}^{m(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}^{m(0)}x_{1}^{m(1)}x_{2}^{m(2)}</annotation></semantics></math> in three variables is
identified with its exponent vector <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p3.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=(m(0),m(1),m(2))\in\mathbb{N}^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℕ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=(m(0),m(1),m(2))\in\mathbb{N}^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We write <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p3.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{\prime}\leq m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{\prime}\leq m</annotation></semantics></math> for coordinate-wise inequality and
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p3.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|m|=m(0)+m(1)+m(2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|m|=m(0)+m(1)+m(2)</annotation></semantics></math> for total degree. A finite order ideal
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p3.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma\subset\mathbb{N}^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℕ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma\subset\mathbb{N}^{3}</annotation></semantics></math> is a finite set closed downward under this
order: if <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p3.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p3.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p3.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p4.6" class="ltx_p">A monomial <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p4.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is maximal if every <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p4.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p4.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\leq n</annotation></semantics></math> also satisfies <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p4.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq m</annotation></semantics></math>. The ideal is pure if all maximal
monomials have the same total degree; this common degree is the socle
degree. The type is the number of maximal monomials. The pure
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p4.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math>-sequence of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p4.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A2.Ex98" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\Gamma}(d)=\#\{m\in\Gamma:|m|=d\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\Gamma}(d)=\#\{m\in\Gamma:|m|=d\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p4.9" class="ltx_p">For a monomial <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p4.7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>, we simply write <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p4.8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{g}(d)=\#\{u\leq g:|u|=d\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{g}(d)=\#\{u\leq g:|u|=d\}</annotation></semantics></math>. The <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p4.9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math>-sequence is log-concave if</p>
<table id="A2.Ex99" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\Gamma}(i-1)h_{\Gamma}(i+1)\leq h_{\Gamma}(i)^{2}\qquad(0&lt;i&lt;e)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\Gamma}(i-1)h_{\Gamma}(i+1)\leq h_{\Gamma}(i)^{2}\qquad(0&lt;i&lt;e),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p4.13" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p4.10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e</annotation></semantics></math> is the socle degree of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p4.11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>. We write
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p4.12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{1}_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>P</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}_{P}</annotation></semantics></math> for the indicator of the condition <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p4.13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof.</span>
Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p5.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> be a pure order ideal in three variables and suppose that
its two maximal monomials are <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p5.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{1}\neq m_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{1}\neq m_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p5.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is pure, <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p5.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|m_{1}|=|m_{2}|=e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|m_{1}|=|m_{2}|=e</annotation></semantics></math>.
Every element of a finite order ideal lies below a maximal element, so</p>
<table id="A2.Ex100" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma=\{u:u\leq m_{1}\}\cup\{u:u\leq m_{2}\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma=\{u:u\leq m_{1}\}\cup\{u:u\leq m_{2}\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p5.7" class="ltx_p">After possibly interchanging <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p5.5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p5.6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, there is a coordinate
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p5.7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\{0,1,2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\{0,1,2\}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A2.Ex101" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{2}(x)&gt;m_{1}(x),\qquad m_{2}(y)\leq m_{1}(y)\quad(y\neq x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{2}(x)&gt;m_{1}(x),\qquad m_{2}(y)\leq m_{1}(y)\quad(y\neq x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p5.8" class="ltx_p">Indeed, the three integers <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p5.8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{1}(i)-m_{2}(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{1}(i)-m_{2}(i)</annotation></semantics></math> sum to zero and are not all
zero, hence one sign occurs in a minority position; if necessary we swap
the two monomials so that the minority sign is negative.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p6.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=m_{1}(x)+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=m_{1}(x)+1</annotation></semantics></math>, and define</p>
<table id="A2.Ex103" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex103.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\rm red}(y)=\begin{cases}m_{2}(x)-m_{1}(x)-1,&amp;y=x,\\
m_{2}(y),&amp;y\neq x.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>red</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\rm red}(y)=\begin{cases}m_{2}(x)-m_{1}(x)-1,&amp;y=x,\\
m_{2}(y),&amp;y\neq x.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p6.3" class="ltx_p">Then <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p6.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|M_{\rm red}|=e-c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>red</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|M_{\rm red}|=e-c</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p6.3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\leq m_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\leq m_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, condition (1) implies</p>
<table id="A2.Ex104" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex104.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\not\leq m_{1}\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad u(x)\geq c." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>≰</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⟺</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\not\leq m_{1}\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad u(x)\geq c.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p6.10" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p6.4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq c</annotation></semantics></math>, the map <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p6.5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\mapsto u-ce_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\mapsto u-ce_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> bijects
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p6.6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{u\leq m_{2}:|u|=d,\ u(x)\geq c\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{u\leq m_{2}:|u|=d,\ u(x)\geq c\}</annotation></semantics></math>
with
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p6.7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{v\leq M_{\rm red}:|v|=d-c\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>red</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v\leq M_{\rm red}:|v|=d-c\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p6.8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d&lt;c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d&lt;c</annotation></semantics></math>, the first set is empty. Hence the <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p6.9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math> sequence of
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p6.10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as</p>
<table id="A2.Ex105" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex105.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(d):=h_{\Gamma}(d)=h_{m_{1}}(d)+\mathbf{1}_{d\geq c}\,h_{M_{\rm red}}(d-c)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>red</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(d):=h_{\Gamma}(d)=h_{m_{1}}(d)+\mathbf{1}_{d\geq c}\,h_{M_{\rm red}}(d-c).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p6.12" class="ltx_p">We need to prove that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p6.11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(d-1)H(d+1)\leq H(d)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(d-1)H(d+1)\leq H(d)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> holds for <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p6.12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;d&lt;e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;d&lt;e</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p7.1" class="ltx_p">For an integer-valued sequence <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p7.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F:\mathbb{N}\to\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F:\mathbb{N}\to\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>, define the first and scond difference sequences as</p>
<table id="A2.Ex107" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta F(0)=F(0),\qquad\Delta F(d)=F(d)-F(d-1)\quad(d&gt;0)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta F(0)=F(0),\qquad\Delta F(d)=F(d)-F(d-1)\quad(d&gt;0),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.Ex108" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{2}F(0)=\Delta F(0),\qquad\Delta^{2}F(d)=\Delta F(d)-\Delta F(d-1)\quad(d&gt;0)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{2}F(0)=\Delta F(0),\qquad\Delta^{2}F(d)=\Delta F(d)-\Delta F(d-1)\quad(d&gt;0).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p8.2" class="ltx_p">We first prove an elementary divisor-count formula for a single
monomial. Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p8.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=(\alpha,\beta,\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=(\alpha,\beta,\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> be a monomial.
For <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p8.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, set</p>
<table id="A2.Ex109" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{p,q}(k)=\#\{r\in\mathbb{N}:r&lt;p,\ r\leq k,\ k-r&lt;q\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{p,q}(k)=\#\{r\in\mathbb{N}:r&lt;p,\ r\leq k,\ k-r&lt;q\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p8.7" class="ltx_p">Thus <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p8.3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{p,q}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{p,q}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> counts the number of pairs <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p8.4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(r,s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(r,s)</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p8.5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq r&lt;p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq r&lt;p</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p8.6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq s&lt;q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq s&lt;q</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p8.7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r+s=k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r+s=k</annotation></semantics></math>. A direct box count gives</p>
<table id="A2.Ex110" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{m}(t)=\sum_{k=0}^{t}\mathbf{1}_{t-k&lt;\gamma+1}\,L_{\alpha+1,\beta+1}(k)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{m}(t)=\sum_{k=0}^{t}\mathbf{1}_{t-k&lt;\gamma+1}\,L_{\alpha+1,\beta+1}(k).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p8.8" class="ltx_p">With the convention <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p8.8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta F(0)=F(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta F(0)=F(0)</annotation></semantics></math>, the first-difference identities are</p>
<table id="A2.Ex111" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L_{p,q}(t)=\mathbf{1}_{t&lt;p}+\mathbf{1}_{t&lt;q}-\mathbf{1}_{t&lt;p+q}\qquad(t\geq 0)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L_{p,q}(t)=\mathbf{1}_{t&lt;p}+\mathbf{1}_{t&lt;q}-\mathbf{1}_{t&lt;p+q}\qquad(t\geq 0),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p8.14" class="ltx_p">and hence</p>
<table id="A2.Ex112" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex112.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta h_{m}(t)=L_{\alpha+1,\beta+1}(t)-\mathbf{1}_{t\geq\gamma+1}\,L_{\alpha+1,\beta+1}(t-\gamma-1)\qquad(t\geq 0)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta h_{m}(t)=L_{\alpha+1,\beta+1}(t)-\mathbf{1}_{t\geq\gamma+1}\,L_{\alpha+1,\beta+1}(t-\gamma-1)\qquad(t\geq 0).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p8.9" class="ltx_p">Taking one more difference gives, for every <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p8.9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex113"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex113.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta^{2}h_{m}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta^{2}h_{m}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex113.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{1}_{t\leq\alpha}+\mathbf{1}_{t\leq\beta}+\mathbf{1}_{t\leq\gamma}-\mathbf{1}_{t\leq\alpha+\beta+1}-\mathbf{1}_{t\leq\beta+\gamma+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{1}_{t\leq\alpha}+\mathbf{1}_{t\leq\beta}+\mathbf{1}_{t\leq\gamma}-\mathbf{1}_{t\leq\alpha+\beta+1}-\mathbf{1}_{t\leq\beta+\gamma+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex114"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex114.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 71.13188pt-\mathbf{1}_{t\leq\gamma+\alpha+1}+\mathbf{1}_{t\leq\alpha+\beta+\gamma+2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 71.13188pt-\mathbf{1}_{t\leq\gamma+\alpha+1}+\mathbf{1}_{t\leq\alpha+\beta+\gamma+2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p8.13" class="ltx_p">In particular, <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p8.10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{2}h_{m}(t)\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{2}h_{m}(t)\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
The same bound holds for the shifted sequence
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p8.11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\longmapsto\mathbf{1}_{t\geq c}h_{M_{\rm red}}(t-c)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟼</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>red</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\longmapsto\mathbf{1}_{t\geq c}h_{M_{\rm red}}(t-c),</annotation></semantics></math>
because below the shift its second difference is zero, and from the shift
onward it is the second difference of the principal sequence of
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p8.12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\rm red}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>red</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\rm red}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p8.13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{2}H(t)\leq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{2}H(t)\leq 2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p9.2" class="ltx_p">Formula (3) also implies the following useful dichotomy. If
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p9.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p9.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{2}h_{m}(t)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{2}h_{m}(t)=1</annotation></semantics></math>, then either</p>
<table id="A2.Ex115" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex115.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leq m(0),\qquad t\leq m(1),\qquad t\leq m(2)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leq m(0),\qquad t\leq m(1),\qquad t\leq m(2),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p9.4" class="ltx_p">or</p>
<table id="A2.Ex117" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex117.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq m(0)+m(1)+2,\qquad t\geq m(1)+m(2)+2,\qquad t\geq m(0)+m(2)+2,\qquad t\leq|m|+2." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq m(0)+m(1)+2,\qquad t\geq m(1)+m(2)+2,\qquad t\geq m(0)+m(2)+2,\qquad t\leq|m|+2.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p9.3" class="ltx_p">We refer to these as the lower and upper alternatives. For <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p9.3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the lower alternative is automatic.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p10.9" class="ltx_p">We shall also use the following elementary consequences of the same box
count.</p>
<ol id="A2.I14" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I14.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span>
<div id="A2.I14.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I14.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A2.I14.i1.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leq m(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leq m(i)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.I14.i1.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="A2.Ex119" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex119.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2h_{m}(t)=(t+1)(t+2),\qquad\Delta h_{m}(t)=t+1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2h_{m}(t)=(t+1)(t+2),\qquad\Delta h_{m}(t)=t+1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</li>
<li id="A2.I14.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span>
<div id="A2.I14.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I14.i2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A2.I14.i2.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq m(i)+m(j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq m(i)+m(j)</annotation></semantics></math> for every pair <math id="A2.I14.i2.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{i,j\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{i,j\}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and <math id="A2.I14.i2.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leq|m|+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leq|m|+2</annotation></semantics></math>,
then,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex121" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex121.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2h_{m}(t)=(|m|+1-t)(|m|+2-t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2h_{m}(t)=(|m|+1-t)(|m|+2-t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</li>
<li id="A2.I14.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span>
<div id="A2.I14.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I14.i3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A2.I14.i3.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq m(i)+m(j)+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq m(i)+m(j)+1</annotation></semantics></math> for every pair <math id="A2.I14.i3.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{i,j\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{i,j\}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and <math id="A2.I14.i3.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leq|m|+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leq|m|+2</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="A2.Ex123" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex123.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta h_{m}(t)=-(|m|+2-t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta h_{m}(t)=-(|m|+2-t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</li>
<li id="A2.I14.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span>
<div id="A2.I14.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I14.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For all <math id="A2.I14.i4.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex125" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex125.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2h_{m}(t)\leq(|m|-t+1)(|m|-t+2)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2h_{m}(t)\leq(|m|-t+1)(|m|-t+2).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</li>
<li id="A2.I14.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span>
<div id="A2.I14.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I14.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A2.I14.i5.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2t\geq|m|+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2t\geq|m|+1</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="A2.Ex127" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex127.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta h_{m}(t)\leq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta h_{m}(t)\leq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</li>
</ol>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p10.3" class="ltx_p">Now fix <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p10.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;d&lt;e=|m_{1}|=|m_{2}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;d&lt;e=|m_{1}|=|m_{2}|</annotation></semantics></math>. Using <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p10.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(d)=H(d-1)+\Delta H(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(d)=H(d-1)+\Delta H(d)</annotation></semantics></math>
and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p10.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta H(d+1)=\Delta H(d)+\Delta^{2}H(d+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta H(d+1)=\Delta H(d)+\Delta^{2}H(d+1)</annotation></semantics></math>
gives</p>
<table id="A2.Ex129" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex129.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(d)^{2}-H(d-1)H(d+1)=(\Delta H(d))^{2}-H(d-1)\Delta^{2}H(d+1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(d)^{2}-H(d-1)H(d+1)=(\Delta H(d))^{2}-H(d-1)\Delta^{2}H(d+1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p10.5" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p10.4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(d-1)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(d-1)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p10.5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{2}H(d+1)\leq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{2}H(d+1)\leq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, it is enough to prove the following two statements:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex131" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex131.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{2}H(d+1)=1\quad\Longrightarrow\quad H(d-1)\leq(\Delta H(d))^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{2}H(d+1)=1\quad\Longrightarrow\quad H(d-1)\leq(\Delta H(d))^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p10.10" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A2.Ex133" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex133.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{2}H(d+1)=2\quad\Longrightarrow\quad 2H(d-1)\leq(\Delta H(d))^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{2}H(d+1)=2\quad\Longrightarrow\quad 2H(d-1)\leq(\Delta H(d))^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p10.8" class="ltx_p">Indeed, if <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p10.6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{2}H(d+1)\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{2}H(d+1)\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, equation (10) is immediate; if it is
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p10.7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p10.8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>, then (11) or (12) applies.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p11.6" class="ltx_p">Write <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p11.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(t)=h_{m_{1}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(t)=h_{m_{1}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p11.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(t)=\mathbf{1}_{t\geq c}h_{M_{\rm red}}(t-c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>red</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(t)=\mathbf{1}_{t\geq c}h_{M_{\rm red}}(t-c)</annotation></semantics></math>, so that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p11.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=f+g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=f+g</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p11.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{2}f\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{2}f\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p11.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{2}g\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{2}g\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, if
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p11.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{2}H(d+1)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{2}H(d+1)=1</annotation></semantics></math>, then either</p>
<table id="A2.Ex135" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex135.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{2}f(d+1)=1,\qquad\Delta^{2}g(d+1)=0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{2}f(d+1)=1,\qquad\Delta^{2}g(d+1)=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p11.8" class="ltx_p">or</p>
<table id="A2.Ex137" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex137.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{2}f(d+1)=0,\qquad\Delta^{2}g(d+1)=1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{2}f(d+1)=0,\qquad\Delta^{2}g(d+1)=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p11.7" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p11.7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{2}H(d+1)=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{2}H(d+1)=2</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="A2.Ex139" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex139.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{2}f(d+1)=\Delta^{2}g(d+1)=1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{2}f(d+1)=\Delta^{2}g(d+1)=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p12.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case A1: (A)+(L) for <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p12.1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
Suppose equation (A) holds and the lower alternative (L) holds for <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p12.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p12.3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=d+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=d+1</annotation></semantics></math>. Then in particular <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p12.4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d+1\leq m_{1}(x)&lt;c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d+1\leq m_{1}(x)&lt;c</annotation></semantics></math>, thus <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p12.5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(d-1)=g(d)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(d-1)=g(d)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, hence <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p12.6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta g(d)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta g(d)=0</annotation></semantics></math> and therefore</p>
<table id="A2.Ex141" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex141.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(d-1)=f(d-1),\qquad\Delta H(d)=\Delta f(d)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(d-1)=f(d-1),\qquad\Delta H(d)=\Delta f(d).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p12.8" class="ltx_p">By (5), <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p12.7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2f(d-1)=d(d+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2f(d-1)=d(d+1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p12.8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta f(d)=d+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta f(d)=d+1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore</p>
<table id="A2.Ex142" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex142.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(d-1)=f(d-1)\leq(d+1)^{2}=(\Delta f(d))^{2}=(\Delta H(d))^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(d-1)=f(d-1)\leq(d+1)^{2}=(\Delta f(d))^{2}=(\Delta H(d))^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p12.9" class="ltx_p">This proves (11) in this case.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p13.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case A2: (A)+(U) for <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p13.1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math></span>. Assume equation (A) holds and the upper alternative (U) holds for <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p13.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p13.3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=d+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=d+1</annotation></semantics></math>. Let us introduce the shorthand notation <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p13.4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=e-d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=e-d</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then (U) gives <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p13.5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\geq-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\geq-1</annotation></semantics></math>. Applying
(6) and (7) gives</p>
<table id="A2.Ex143" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex143.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2f(d-1)=(\rho+2)(\rho+3),\qquad\Delta f(d)=-(\rho+2)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2f(d-1)=(\rho+2)(\rho+3),\qquad\Delta f(d)=-(\rho+2).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p13.19" class="ltx_p">The shifted summand satisfies</p>
<table id="A2.Ex145" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex145.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta g(d)\leq 0,\qquad 2g(d-1)\leq(\rho+2)(\rho+3),\qquad 2g(d)\leq(\rho+1)(\rho+2)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta g(d)\leq 0,\qquad 2g(d-1)\leq(\rho+2)(\rho+3),\qquad 2g(d)\leq(\rho+1)(\rho+2).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p13.12" class="ltx_p">Indeed, the two inequalities for <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p13.6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(d-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(d-1)</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p13.7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(d)</annotation></semantics></math> follow from the universal upper bound (8),
applied to the shifted sequence. For the sign of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p13.8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta g(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta g(d)</annotation></semantics></math>, if
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p13.9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d&lt;c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d&lt;c</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p13.10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta g(d)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta g(d)=0</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p13.11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq c</annotation></semantics></math>, then the upper alternative
for <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p13.12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> implies</p>
<table id="A2.Ex147" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex147.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq m_{1}(x)+m_{1}(y)+1,\qquad d\geq m_{1}(x)+m_{1}(z)+1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq m_{1}(x)+m_{1}(y)+1,\qquad d\geq m_{1}(x)+m_{1}(z)+1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p13.13" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p13.13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x,y,z\}=\{0,1,2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x,y,z\}=\{0,1,2\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Adding these inequalities gives</p>
<table id="A2.Ex148" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex148.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2d\geq 2m_{1}(x)+m_{1}(y)+m_{1}(z)+2=e+m_{1}(x)+2." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2d\geq 2m_{1}(x)+m_{1}(y)+m_{1}(z)+2=e+m_{1}(x)+2.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p13.18" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p13.14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=m_{1}(x)+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=m_{1}(x)+1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p13.15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|M_{\rm red}|=e-c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>red</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|M_{\rm red}|=e-c</annotation></semantics></math>, this is equivalent to
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p13.16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2(d-c)\geq|M_{\rm red}|+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>red</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2(d-c)\geq|M_{\rm red}|+1</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus the midpoint monotonicity (9) applies
to the shifted <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p13.17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\rm red}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>red</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\rm red}</annotation></semantics></math>-sequence and gives <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p13.18.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta g(d)\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta g(d)\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p14.4" class="ltx_p">To prove (11), by (13) it remains to show</p>
<table id="A2.Ex149" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex149.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(d-1)+g(d-1)\leq\bigl(-(\rho+2)+\Delta g(d)\bigr)^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(d-1)+g(d-1)\leq\bigl(-(\rho+2)+\Delta g(d)\bigr)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p14.5" class="ltx_p">By (13) and (14), this follows from</p>
<table id="A2.Ex150" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex150.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\rho+2)(\rho+3)+2g(d-1)\leq 2\bigl(-(\rho+2)+\Delta g(d)\bigr)^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\rho+2)(\rho+3)+2g(d-1)\leq 2\bigl(-(\rho+2)+\Delta g(d)\bigr)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p14.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p14.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(d)=g(d-1)+\Delta g(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(d)=g(d-1)+\Delta g(d)</annotation></semantics></math>, the third inequality in (14) gives</p>
<table id="A2.Ex152" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex152.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2g(d-1)\leq(\rho+1)(\rho+2)-2\Delta g(d)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2g(d-1)\leq(\rho+1)(\rho+2)-2\Delta g(d).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p14.6" class="ltx_p">Therefore the difference between the right-hand side and the left-hand
side of (15) is at least</p>
<table id="A2.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex153"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex153.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\bigl(-(\rho+2)+\Delta g(d)\bigr)^{2}-(\rho+2)(\rho+3)-\bigl((\rho+1)(\rho+2)-2\Delta g(d)\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\bigl(-(\rho+2)+\Delta g(d)\bigr)^{2}-(\rho+2)(\rho+3)-\bigl((\rho+1)(\rho+2)-2\Delta g(d)\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex154"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex154.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad=2\Delta g(d)\bigl(\Delta g(d)-2(\rho+2)+1\bigr)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi></mi><mo lspace="2.278em">=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad=2\Delta g(d)\bigl(\Delta g(d)-2(\rho+2)+1\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p14.3" class="ltx_p">This is nonnegative because <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p14.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta g(d)\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta g(d)\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p14.3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\geq-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\geq-1</annotation></semantics></math>, and hence</p>
<table id="A2.Ex155" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex155.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta g(d)-2(\rho+2)+1\leq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta g(d)-2(\rho+2)+1\leq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p14.7" class="ltx_p">Thus (11) holds in this case, and we completed the (A) case.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p15.1" class="ltx_p">For the two cases when (B) holds, that is <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p15.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{2}g(d+1)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{2}g(d+1)=1</annotation></semantics></math>, we use the following
shift reduction. If</p>
<table id="A2.Ex156" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex156.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{2}H(d+1)=1\qquad\text{and}\qquad H(d+1)\leq(\Delta H(d+1))^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{2}H(d+1)=1\qquad\text{and}\qquad H(d+1)\leq(\Delta H(d+1))^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p15.4" class="ltx_p">then</p>
<table id="A2.Ex157" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex157.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(d-1)\leq(\Delta H(d))^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(d-1)\leq(\Delta H(d))^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p15.3" class="ltx_p">Indeed, <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p15.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta H(d)=\Delta H(d+1)-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta H(d)=\Delta H(d+1)-1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p15.3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(d-1)=H(d+1)-\Delta H(d+1)-\Delta H(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(d-1)=H(d+1)-\Delta H(d+1)-\Delta H(d)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore</p>
<table id="A2.Ex159" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex159.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(d-1)=H(d+1)-2\Delta H(d+1)+1\leq(\Delta H(d+1))^{2}-2\Delta H(d+1)+1=(\Delta H(d))^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(d-1)=H(d+1)-2\Delta H(d+1)+1\leq(\Delta H(d+1))^{2}-2\Delta H(d+1)+1=(\Delta H(d))^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p16.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case B1: (B)+(L) for <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p16.1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
Assume equation (B) holds and the lower alternative (L) holds for <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p16.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p16.3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=d+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=d+1</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p16.4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=d+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=d+1</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p16.5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{2}g(D)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{2}g(D)=1</annotation></semantics></math>, necessarily <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p16.6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\geq c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\geq c</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p16.7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{2}h_{M_{\rm red}}(D-c)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>red</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{2}h_{M_{\rm red}}(D-c)=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
In the lower subcase <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p16.8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D-c\leq M_{\rm red}(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>red</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D-c\leq M_{\rm red}(i)</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p16.9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p16.10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D-c+1\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D-c+1\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, and the lower formula (5) gives</p>
<table id="A2.Ex160" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex160.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2g(D)=(D-c+1)(D-c+2),\qquad\Delta g(D)=D-c+1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2g(D)=(D-c+1)(D-c+2),\qquad\Delta g(D)=D-c+1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p16.12" class="ltx_p">We next prove two bounds for <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p16.11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p16.12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex162" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex162.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(D)\leq(D+1)\Delta f(D),\qquad\Delta f(D)=c." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(D)\leq(D+1)\Delta f(D),\qquad\Delta f(D)=c.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p16.14" class="ltx_p">First, since <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p16.13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{2}f(D)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{2}f(D)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the explicit formula (3), together with
the lower inequalities for <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p16.14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\rm red}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>red</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\rm red}</annotation></semantics></math>, implies</p>
<table id="A2.Ex164" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex164.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\leq m_{1}(0)+m_{1}(1)+1,\qquad D\leq m_{1}(1)+m_{1}(2)+1,\qquad D\leq m_{1}(0)+m_{1}(2)+1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\leq m_{1}(0)+m_{1}(1)+1,\qquad D\leq m_{1}(1)+m_{1}(2)+1,\qquad D\leq m_{1}(0)+m_{1}(2)+1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p16.20" class="ltx_p">Indeed, the two pair inequalities involving <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p16.15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> follow directly from
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p16.16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D-c\leq M_{\rm red}(y)\leq m_{1}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>red</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D-c\leq M_{\rm red}(y)\leq m_{1}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p16.17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\neq x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\neq x</annotation></semantics></math>. The remaining pair
inequality follows from (3): if it failed, then the corresponding two
single indicators would be zero; since <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p16.18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\geq c=m_{1}(x)+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\geq c=m_{1}(x)+1</annotation></semantics></math>, the
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p16.19.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>-single indicator is also zero, and the right-hand side of (3)
would be negative, contradicting <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p16.20.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{2}f(D)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{2}f(D)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p17.8" class="ltx_p">Thus, in (3) for <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p17.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p17.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>, all three pair indicators and the triple
indicator are equal to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p17.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p17.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{2}f(D)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{2}f(D)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, exactly two of
the three single indicators are equal to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p17.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover the
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p17.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>-single indicator is zero, because <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p17.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\geq m_{1}(x)+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\geq m_{1}(x)+1</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence the
two remaining single indicators are equal to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p17.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p18.3" class="ltx_p">It follows that for every <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p18.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq k\leq D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq k\leq D</annotation></semantics></math>, the same two single
indicators are still equal to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p18.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, while the three pair indicators and
the triple indicator are also equal to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p18.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore</p>
<table id="A2.Ex166" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex166.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{2}f(k)\geq 2-3+1=0\qquad(1\leq k\leq D)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{2}f(k)\geq 2-3+1=0\qquad(1\leq k\leq D).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p18.5" class="ltx_p">Thus the first differences <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p18.4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta f(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta f(k)</annotation></semantics></math> are nondecreasing on
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p18.5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0,1,\ldots,D\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0,1,\ldots,D\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since</p>
<table id="A2.Ex167" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex167.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(D)=\sum_{j=0}^{D}\Delta f(j)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></munderover><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(D)=\sum_{j=0}^{D}\Delta f(j),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p18.6" class="ltx_p">we get</p>
<table id="A2.Ex168" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex168.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(D)\leq(D+1)\Delta f(D)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(D)\leq(D+1)\Delta f(D).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p18.7" class="ltx_p">This proves the first inequality in (18).</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p19.2" class="ltx_p">For the second inequality in (18), relabel the two coordinates different
from <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p19.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p19.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y,z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y,z</annotation></semantics></math>, and write</p>
<table id="A2.Ex169" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex169.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=m_{1}(y)+1,\qquad B=m_{1}(z)+1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=m_{1}(y)+1,\qquad B=m_{1}(z)+1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p19.4" class="ltx_p">and recall <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p19.3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=m_{1}(x)+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=m_{1}(x)+1</annotation></semantics></math>. Using the box-count formula with <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p19.4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> as the third coordinate, the
first-difference formula gives</p>
<table id="A2.Ex170" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex170.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta f(D)=L_{A,B}(D)-L_{A,B}(D-c)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta f(D)=L_{A,B}(D)-L_{A,B}(D-c),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p19.7" class="ltx_p">because <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p19.5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\geq c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\geq c</annotation></semantics></math>. From the preceding paragraph,
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p19.6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D&lt;A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D&lt;A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p19.7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D&lt;B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D&lt;B</annotation></semantics></math>, hence</p>
<table id="A2.Ex171" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex171.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{A,B}(D)=D+1,\qquad L_{A,B}(D-c)=D-c+1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{A,B}(D)=D+1,\qquad L_{A,B}(D-c)=D-c+1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p19.12" class="ltx_p">Therefore</p>
<table id="A2.Ex172" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex172.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta f(D)=(D+1)-(D-c+1)=c," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta f(D)=(D+1)-(D-c+1)=c,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p19.13" class="ltx_p">proving (18). Using (17) and (18), we have</p>
<table id="A2.Ex173" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex173.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2H(D)=2f(D)+2g(D)\leq 2\Delta f(D)(D+1)+(D-c+1)(D-c+2)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2H(D)=2f(D)+2g(D)\leq 2\Delta f(D)(D+1)+(D-c+1)(D-c+2).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p19.14" class="ltx_p">Also, by (17),</p>
<table id="A2.Ex174" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex174.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta H(D)=\Delta f(D)+\Delta g(D)=\Delta f(D)+(D-c+1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta H(D)=\Delta f(D)+\Delta g(D)=\Delta f(D)+(D-c+1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p19.15" class="ltx_p">Thus it is enough to show</p>
<table id="A2.Ex175" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex175.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\Delta f(D)(D+1)+(D-c+1)(D-c+2)\leq 2\bigl(\Delta f(D)+D-c+1\bigr)^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\Delta f(D)(D+1)+(D-c+1)(D-c+2)\leq 2\bigl(\Delta f(D)+D-c+1\bigr)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p19.8" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p19.8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D+1=(D-c+1)+c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D+1=(D-c+1)+c</annotation></semantics></math>, the difference between the right-hand side and
the left-hand side is</p>
<table id="A2.Ex176" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex176.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\Delta f(D)\bigl(\Delta f(D)-c\bigr)+2\Delta f(D)(D-c+1)+(D-c+1)(D-c)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\Delta f(D)\bigl(\Delta f(D)-c\bigr)+2\Delta f(D)(D-c+1)+(D-c+1)(D-c).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p19.11" class="ltx_p">This is nonnegative because <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p19.9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta f(D)\geq c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta f(D)\geq c</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p19.10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D-c+1\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D-c+1\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p19.11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(D)\leq(\Delta H(D))^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(D)\leq(\Delta H(D))^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the shift reduction (16), this proves (11).</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p20" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p20.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case B2: (B)+(U) for <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p20.1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
Again let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p20.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=d+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=d+1</annotation></semantics></math> and put <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p20.3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=e-D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=e-D</annotation></semantics></math>. The upper alternative for
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p20.4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{M_{\rm red}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>red</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{M_{\rm red}}</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p20.5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D-c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D-c</annotation></semantics></math> gives <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p20.6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\geq-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\geq-2</annotation></semantics></math>. Since
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p20.7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|M_{\rm red}|=e-c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>red</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|M_{\rm red}|=e-c</annotation></semantics></math>, formulas (6) and (7) give</p>
<table id="A2.Ex177" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex177.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2g(D)=(\rho+1)(\rho+2),\qquad\Delta g(D)=-(\rho+2)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2g(D)=(\rho+1)(\rho+2),\qquad\Delta g(D)=-(\rho+2).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p20.8" class="ltx_p">For the first summand, the universal upper bound (8) gives</p>
<table id="A2.Ex179" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex179.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2f(D)\leq(e-D+1)(e-D+2)=(\rho+1)(\rho+2)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2f(D)\leq(e-D+1)(e-D+2)=(\rho+1)(\rho+2).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p21.3" class="ltx_p">It remains to justify the sign of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p21.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta f(D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta f(D)</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p21.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is in the
upper alternative at <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p21.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A2.Ex181" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex181.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D-c\geq M_{\rm red}(0)+M_{\rm red}(1)+2,\ D-c\geq M_{\rm red}(1)+M_{\rm red}(2)+2,\ D-c\geq M_{\rm red}(0)+M_{\rm red}(2)+2." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>red</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>red</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>red</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>red</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>red</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>red</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D-c\geq M_{\rm red}(0)+M_{\rm red}(1)+2,\ D-c\geq M_{\rm red}(1)+M_{\rm red}(2)+2,\ D-c\geq M_{\rm red}(0)+M_{\rm red}(2)+2.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p21.10" class="ltx_p">Adding these three inequalities gives</p>
<table id="A2.Ex182" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex182.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3(D-c)\geq 2|M_{\rm red}|+6=2(e-c)+6." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>red</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3(D-c)\geq 2|M_{\rm red}|+6=2(e-c)+6.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p21.11" class="ltx_p">Hence</p>
<table id="A2.Ex183" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex183.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2(D-c)\geq\frac{2}{3}\bigl(2|M_{\rm red}|+6\bigr)=|M_{\rm red}|+1+\frac{|M_{\rm red}|+9}{3}&gt;|M_{\rm red}|+1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>red</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>red</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>red</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">&gt;</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>red</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2(D-c)\geq\frac{2}{3}\bigl(2|M_{\rm red}|+6\bigr)=|M_{\rm red}|+1+\frac{|M_{\rm red}|+9}{3}&gt;|M_{\rm red}|+1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p21.4" class="ltx_p">because <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p21.4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|M_{\rm red}|\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>red</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|M_{\rm red}|\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore</p>
<table id="A2.Ex184" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex184.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2D=2(D-c)+2c\geq(e-c+1)+2c=e+c+1\geq e+1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2D=2(D-c)+2c\geq(e-c+1)+2c=e+c+1\geq e+1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p21.6" class="ltx_p">By midpoint monotonicity (9), applied to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p21.5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=h_{m_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=h_{m_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we get <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p21.6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta f(D)\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta f(D)\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Using (20), (21), we get</p>
<table id="A2.Ex185" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex185.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2H(D)\leq 2(\rho+1)(\rho+2),\qquad\Delta H(D)=\Delta f(D)-(\rho+2)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2H(D)\leq 2(\rho+1)(\rho+2),\qquad\Delta H(D)=\Delta f(D)-(\rho+2).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p21.8" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p21.7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\geq-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\geq-2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p21.8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta f(D)\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta f(D)\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A2.Ex186" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex186.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\rho+1)(\rho+2)\leq\bigl(-\Delta f(D)+\rho+2\bigr)^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\rho+1)(\rho+2)\leq\bigl(-\Delta f(D)+\rho+2\bigr)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p21.9" class="ltx_p">giving the desired <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p21.9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(D)\leq(\Delta H(D))^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(D)\leq(\Delta H(D))^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. By the shift reduction (16), this proves (11).</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case C: (C) holds.</span>
So here <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{2}H(d+1)=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{2}H(d+1)=2</annotation></semantics></math> and hence <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{2}f(d+1)=\Delta^{2}g(d+1)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{2}f(d+1)=\Delta^{2}g(d+1)=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{2}g(d+1)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{2}g(d+1)=1</annotation></semantics></math>, necessarily <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d+1\geq c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d+1\geq c</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore the lower alternative (L) for <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is impossible, because it
would imply <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d+1\leq m_{1}(x)&lt;c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d+1\leq m_{1}(x)&lt;c</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is in its upper alternative, that is, (U) holds for <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>. The lower alternative (L) for <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is also impossible. Indeed, if <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22.10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d+1-c\leq M_{\rm red}(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>red</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d+1-c\leq M_{\rm red}(i)</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22.11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>,
then, choosing any <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22.12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\neq x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\neq x</annotation></semantics></math>, we get</p>
<table id="A2.Ex187" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex187.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d+1\leq m_{1}(x)+1+M_{\rm red}(y)=m_{1}(x)+1+m_{2}(y)\leq m_{1}(x)+1+m_{1}(y)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>red</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d+1\leq m_{1}(x)+1+M_{\rm red}(y)=m_{1}(x)+1+m_{2}(y)\leq m_{1}(x)+1+m_{1}(y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22.21" class="ltx_p">But the upper alternative for <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22.13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> gives <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22.14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d+1\geq m_{1}(x)+m_{1}(y)+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d+1\geq m_{1}(x)+m_{1}(y)+2</annotation></semantics></math>, a contradiction. Thus <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22.15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is also in its upper alternative, and (U) holds for <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22.16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>.
Put <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22.17.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=e-d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=e-d</annotation></semantics></math> again. Since <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22.18.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|M_{\rm red}|=e-c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>red</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|M_{\rm red}|=e-c</annotation></semantics></math>, we also have <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22.19.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|M_{\rm red}|-(d-c)=e-d=\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>red</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|M_{\rm red}|-(d-c)=e-d=\rho</annotation></semantics></math>.
The upper formulas (6) and (7), applied to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22.20.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> and to the shifted
summand <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22.21.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>, give</p>
<table id="A2.Ex188" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex188.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2f(d-1)=(\rho+2)(\rho+3),\qquad\Delta f(d)=-(\rho+2)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2f(d-1)=(\rho+2)(\rho+3),\qquad\Delta f(d)=-(\rho+2),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22.30" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A2.Ex189" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex189.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2g(d-1)=(\rho+2)(\rho+3),\qquad\Delta g(d)=-(\rho+2)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2g(d-1)=(\rho+2)(\rho+3),\qquad\Delta g(d)=-(\rho+2).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22.31" class="ltx_p">Therefore</p>
<table id="A2.Ex190" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex190.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2H(d-1)=2(\rho+2)(\rho+3),\qquad\Delta H(d)=-2(\rho+2)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2H(d-1)=2(\rho+2)(\rho+3),\qquad\Delta H(d)=-2(\rho+2).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22.23" class="ltx_p">Since the upper alternative for <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22.22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> gives <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22.23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\geq-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\geq-1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A2.Ex191" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex191.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Delta H(d))^{2}-2H(d-1)=4(\rho+2)^{2}-2(\rho+2)(\rho+3)=2(\rho+2)(\rho+1)\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Delta H(d))^{2}-2H(d-1)=4(\rho+2)^{2}-2(\rho+2)(\rho+3)=2(\rho+2)(\rho+1)\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22.29" class="ltx_p">which proves (12). This completes the proof of (11) and (12), and hence by (10) <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22.24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(d-1)H(d+1)\leq H(d)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(d-1)H(d+1)\leq H(d)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22.25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;d&lt;e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;d&lt;e</annotation></semantics></math> was arbitrary and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22.26.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> is the pure <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22.27.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math>-sequence of
<math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22.28.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> by (2), the theorem follows.  <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p22.29.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Box" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Box</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p23" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx12.p23.1" class="ltx_p">The Lean proof for the problem can be found at <a href="https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/tree/main/APNOutputs/AICollaborator/AlgebraicGeometry" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/tree/main/APNOutputs/AICollaborator/AlgebraicGeometry</a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSSx13" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">A Convergence Proof of Modified Anchored Gradient Descent-Ascent</h4>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx13.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A natural-language version of the convergence proof we discovered can be found in Surina et al. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">surina2026improvedlastiterateconvergencerate</span>]</cite>.
The Lean proof is at <a href="https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/main/APNOutputs/Optimization/LastIterateConvergence.lean" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/main/APNOutputs/Optimization/LastIterateConvergence.lean</a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSSx14" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Written on the Wall, Conjecture 2</h4>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p1.19" class="ltx_p">For a graph <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(G)</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of vertices and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E(G)</annotation></semantics></math> the set of edges. For <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p1.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V(G)</annotation></semantics></math>, write <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p1.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(v)</annotation></semantics></math> for the degree of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p1.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p1.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(v)</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of vertices adjacent to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p1.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p1.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p1.10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha(v)</annotation></semantics></math> be the local independence number of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p1.11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>: the size of the largest independent set in <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p1.12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G[N(v)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G[N(v)]</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p1.13.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(G):=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{v}\alpha(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>v</mi></msub><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(G):=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{v}\alpha(v)</annotation></semantics></math> be the average of the local independence numbers, and let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p1.14.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{S}(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{S}(G)</annotation></semantics></math> be the maximum number of leaves in a spanning tree of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p1.15.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, or <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p1.16.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><mn>0</mn></math> if <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p1.17.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is not connected.

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p1.19.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem.</span>
If <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p1.18.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is a simple connected graph on <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p1.19.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> vertices, then</p>
<table id="A2.Ex192" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex192.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{S}(G)\geq 2(\ell(G)-1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{S}(G)\geq 2(\ell(G)-1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p1.24" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p1.24.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof.</span>
Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p1.20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V:=V(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V:=V(G)</annotation></semantics></math>. For every vertex <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p1.21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V</annotation></semantics></math>, fix a maximum independent set <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p1.22.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(v)</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p1.23.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G[N(v)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G[N(v)]</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p1.24.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha(v)=|A(v)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha(v)=|A(v)|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p2.7" class="ltx_p">Now take two copies of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p2.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>, and add edges <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p2.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="uv" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">uv</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p2.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in V</annotation></semantics></math> on the left to <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p2.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in A(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in A(u)</annotation></semantics></math> on the right. This forms a bipartite graph, where vertices on the left side have degree <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p2.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha(v)</annotation></semantics></math>. The key idea is to look at the degrees of the vertices on the right side, and formulate the entire proof in terms of them. Formally, put <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p2.6.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="c(v):=|{u\in V(G):v\in A(u)|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">:=</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(v):=|{u\in V(G):v\in A(u)|}</annotation></semantics></math> as the degree of a vertex <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p2.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> on the right side.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p3.27" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p3.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(v)\leq d(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(v)\leq d(v)</annotation></semantics></math>, for all <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p3.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V</annotation></semantics></math>. Because <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p3.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{v}\alpha(v)=\sum_{v}c(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>v</mi></msub><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>v</mi></msub><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{v}\alpha(v)=\sum_{v}c(v)</annotation></semantics></math>, it is enough to show that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p3.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{v}c(v)\leq n(L_{S}(G)/2+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>v</mi></msub><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{v}c(v)\leq n(L_{S}(G)/2+1)</annotation></semantics></math>. To simplify the notation, we set <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p3.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu:=L_{S}(G)/2+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu:=L_{S}(G)/2+1</annotation></semantics></math>, and so the goal is to show <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p3.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{v}c(v)\leq n\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>v</mi></msub><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{v}c(v)\leq n\mu</annotation></semantics></math>.

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p3.27.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1.</span>
For every edge <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p3.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="uv\in E(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">uv\in E(G)</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p3.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(u)+c(v)\leq|N(u)\cup N(v)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(u)+c(v)\leq|N(u)\cup N(v)|</annotation></semantics></math>.

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p3.27.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Lemma 1.</span> For every vertex <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p3.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in N(u)\cup N(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in N(u)\cup N(v)</annotation></semantics></math>, at most one of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p3.10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p3.11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> can be part of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p3.12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(w)</annotation></semantics></math>, otherwise the edge <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p3.13.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="uv" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">uv</annotation></semantics></math> would contradict the fact that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p3.14.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(w)</annotation></semantics></math> is independent. On the other hand, if <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p3.15.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in V</annotation></semantics></math> is such that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p3.16.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p3.17.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is in <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p3.18.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(w)</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p3.19.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> must be part of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p3.20.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(u)\cup N(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(u)\cup N(v)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p3.21.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(u)+c(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(u)+c(v)</annotation></semantics></math> is at most the size of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p3.22.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(u)\cup N(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(u)\cup N(v)</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p3.23.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Box" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Box</annotation></semantics></math>

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p3.27.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2.</span>
For every edge <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p3.24.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="uv\in E(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">uv\in E(G)</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p3.25.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|N(u)\cup N(v)|\leq L_{S}(G)+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|N(u)\cup N(v)|\leq L_{S}(G)+2</annotation></semantics></math>.

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p3.27.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Lemma 2.</span> We construct a spanning tree in <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p3.26.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> with at least <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p3.27.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|N(u)\cup N(v)|-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|N(u)\cup N(v)|-2</annotation></semantics></math> leaves.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p4.17" class="ltx_p">Start with the edge <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p4.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="uv" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">uv</annotation></semantics></math> and add all the vertices in <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p4.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(u)\cup N(v)\setminus\{u,v\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(u)\cup N(v)\setminus\{u,v\}</annotation></semantics></math> as pendant vertices of degree <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p4.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>. There are <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p4.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|N(u)\cup N(v)|-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|N(u)\cup N(v)|-2</annotation></semantics></math> leaves in this tree <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p4.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Because <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p4.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is connected, we can expand <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p4.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> to a spanning tree <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p4.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p4.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> by adding edges until no more can be added. Then from every leaf in <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p4.10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> there is a path to a leaf in <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p4.11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> that doesn’t cross <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p4.12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="uv" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">uv</annotation></semantics></math>. All these leaves must be distinct, since they are contained in distinct subtrees of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p4.13.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p4.14.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> has at least <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p4.15.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|N(u)\cup N(v)|-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|N(u)\cup N(v)|-2</annotation></semantics></math> leaves. <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p4.16.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Box" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Box</annotation></semantics></math>

<br class="ltx_break">Lemmas 1 and 2 show that for every edge <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p4.17.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="uv\in E(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">uv\in E(G)</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex193" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex193.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(u)+c(v)\leq L_{S}(G)+2=2\mu." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(u)+c(v)\leq L_{S}(G)+2=2\mu.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p5.5" class="ltx_p">Next, we observe that <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p5.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{v}c(v)\leq n\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>v</mi></msub><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{v}c(v)\leq n\mu</annotation></semantics></math> trivially holds if every <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p5.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(v)\leq\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(v)\leq\mu</annotation></semantics></math>. So assume this is not the case. Then we can split the vertices into "heavy" vertices with <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p5.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(v)&gt;\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(v)&gt;\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, and "light" vertices with <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p5.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(v)\leq\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(v)\leq\mu</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p5.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of heavy vertices.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p6.12" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p6.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> must be an independent set, since the above equation shows that for any edge <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p6.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="uv" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">uv</annotation></semantics></math>, at most one of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p6.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p6.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> can be heavy. Less obvious is that light vertices cannot have many neighbors in <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p6.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>.

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p6.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.</span> If <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p6.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is a light vertex, then <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p6.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|N(v)\cap S|&lt;\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|N(v)\cap S|&lt;\mu</annotation></semantics></math>.

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p6.12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Lemma 3.</span> Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p6.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in N(v)\cap S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in N(v)\cap S</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p6.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is independent, all neighbours of <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p6.10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> are outside <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p6.11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(v)\cap S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(v)\cap S</annotation></semantics></math>. So <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p6.12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|N(u)\cup N(v)|\geq|N(v)\cap S|+|N(u)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|N(u)\cup N(v)|\geq|N(v)\cap S|+|N(u)|</annotation></semantics></math>. Using Lemma 2 we get</p>
<table id="A2.Ex194" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex194.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|N(v)\cap S|\leq|N(u)\cup N(v)|-|N(u)|\leq L_{S}(G)+2-d(u)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|N(v)\cap S|\leq|N(u)\cup N(v)|-|N(u)|\leq L_{S}(G)+2-d(u).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p6.15" class="ltx_p">As <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p6.13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(u)\geq c(u)&gt;\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(u)\geq c(u)&gt;\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p6.14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|N(v)\cap S|&lt;L_{S}(G)+2-\mu=\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|N(v)\cap S|&lt;L_{S}(G)+2-\mu=\mu</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p6.15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Box" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Box</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p7.2" class="ltx_p">Then the theorem follows from the following more general statement:

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claim.</span> Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p7.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c:V\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c:V\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p7.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy:</p>
<ol id="A2.I15" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I15.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span>
<div id="A2.I15.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I15.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I15.i1.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(v)\leq d(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(v)\leq d(v)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.I15.i1.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div>
</li>
<li id="A2.I15.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span>
<div id="A2.I15.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I15.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I15.i2.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(u)+c(v)\leq 2\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(u)+c(v)\leq 2\mu</annotation></semantics></math> for every edge <math id="A2.I15.i2.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="uv" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">uv</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div>
</li>
<li id="A2.I15.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span>
<div id="A2.I15.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I15.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I15.i3.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S:=\{u:c(u)&gt;\mu\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S:=\{u:c(u)&gt;\mu\}</annotation></semantics></math> is an independent set,</p>
</div>
</li>
<li id="A2.I15.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span>
<div id="A2.I15.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I15.i4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I15.i4.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|N(v)\cap S|&lt;\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|N(v)\cap S|&lt;\mu</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="A2.I15.i4.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\notin S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\notin S</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</li>
</ol>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p7.10" class="ltx_p">Then <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p7.3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{v}c(v)\leq n\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>v</mi></msub><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{v}c(v)\leq n\mu</annotation></semantics></math>.

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p7.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Claim.</span> We assume <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p7.4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is non-empty, otherwise the claim is trivially true. The proof uses a discharging argument: it sends the <span id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p7.10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">excess</span> <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p7.5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(u)-\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(u)-\mu</annotation></semantics></math> from a heavy vertex <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p7.6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in S</annotation></semantics></math> to its neighbors. The redistribution keeps the total sum <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p7.7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{v}c(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>v</mi></msub><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{v}c(v)</annotation></semantics></math> constant. However, the amount sent to a light vertex <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p7.8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is less than the <span id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p7.10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">slack</span> <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p7.9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu-c(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu-c(v)</annotation></semantics></math>, so the overall sum can’t exceed <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p7.10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\mu</annotation></semantics></math>.
Precisely, define a weight function that transfers excess from heavy to light vertices:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex195" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex195.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W(u,v):=\begin{cases}\frac{\mu-c(v)}{d(u)}&amp;\textrm{if $u\in S$ and $uv$ is an edge},\\
0&amp;\textrm{otherwise}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mtext> and </mtext><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mtext> is an edge</mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>otherwise</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W(u,v):=\begin{cases}\frac{\mu-c(v)}{d(u)}&amp;\textrm{if $u\in S$ and $uv$ is an edge},\\
0&amp;\textrm{otherwise}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p7.15" class="ltx_p">Because <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p7.11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is independent, the weight flows only from heavy to light vertices. We now show two statements.

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p7.15.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Each heavy vertex sends out enough weight</span>. If <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p7.12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in S</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p7.13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="uv" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">uv</annotation></semantics></math> is an edge, then <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p7.14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(u)+c(v)\leq 2\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(u)+c(v)\leq 2\mu</annotation></semantics></math> by condition 2. So <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p7.15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu-c(v)\geq c(u)-\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu-c(v)\geq c(u)-\mu</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</p>
<table id="A2.Ex196" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex196.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{v\in N(u)}W(u,v)\geq d(u)\frac{c(u)-\mu}{d(u)}=c(u)-\mu." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{v\in N(u)}W(u,v)\geq d(u)\frac{c(u)-\mu}{d(u)}=c(u)-\mu.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<br class="ltx_break">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p7.20" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p7.20.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Each light vertex absorbs at most its slack</span>. Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p7.16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\notin S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\notin S</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p7.17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> receives weight from vertices in <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p7.18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F:=N(v)\cap S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F:=N(v)\cap S</annotation></semantics></math>.

<br class="ltx_break">Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p7.19.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in F</annotation></semantics></math>. From conditions (1) and (4), we have <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p7.20.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|F|&lt;\mu&lt;c(u)\leq d(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|F|&lt;\mu&lt;c(u)\leq d(u)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the total weight received is</p>
<table id="A2.Ex197" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex197.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{u\in F}W(u,v)=\sum_{u\in F}\frac{\mu-c(v)}{d(u)}&lt;\sum_{u\in F}\frac{\mu-c(v)}{|F|}=\mu-c(v)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">&lt;</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{u\in F}W(u,v)=\sum_{u\in F}\frac{\mu-c(v)}{d(u)}&lt;\sum_{u\in F}\frac{\mu-c(v)}{|F|}=\mu-c(v).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p7.23" class="ltx_p">These two statements together show that</p>
<table id="A2.Ex198" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex198.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{u\in S}c(u)-\mu\leq\sum_{u\in S}\sum_{v\notin S}W(u,v)=\sum_{v\notin S}\sum_{u\in S}W(u,v)\leq\sum_{v\notin S}\mu-c(v)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{u\in S}c(u)-\mu\leq\sum_{u\in S}\sum_{v\notin S}W(u,v)=\sum_{v\notin S}\sum_{u\in S}W(u,v)\leq\sum_{v\notin S}\mu-c(v).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p7.22" class="ltx_p">Re-arranging the terms gives <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p7.21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{v}c(v)&lt;n\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>v</mi></msub><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{v}c(v)&lt;n\mu</annotation></semantics></math> as desired.  <math id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p7.22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Box" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Box</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSSx14.p8.1" class="ltx_p">The discovered lean proof for this is available at  <a href="https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/main/APNOutputs/OEIS/GraphConjecture2.lean" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/main/APNOutputs/OEIS/GraphConjecture2.lean</a>.</p>
</div>
